{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression","id":997612,"title":"A critical look at Genius: the Transgression","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-03T02:00:12-07:00","id":997612,"title":"A critical look at Genius: the Transgression","content":"This turned out to be more of an opinion piece, if you have any thoughts on the points brought up please post them below. <br /> <br /> <br /> I like Genius: the Transgression, never though I'd be saying that but I do none the less. It shows what creativity a fan game can bring to the table, and it's ideas can inspire stories that wouldn't normally come up in a Chronicle of Darkness.<br /> <br /> This is what make me so disappointed in Genius' failings though. For all it's themes of inspiration, potential, and creativity the game itself is one of the most stifling gamelines of the fan-made series. And here's why, my own thesis if you will: Geniuses must be scientists.<br /> <br /> Sure, this might be the obvious point of the game. Play as a mad scientists, create impossible inventions, explore infinite dimensions, Ect. But not all geniuses are scientists, but in Genius the Inspired must become scientist or inventors in order to do anything involving Wonders. There are no artists who seek to create masterpieces in mediums never before attempted, no athlete so dedicated to the craft that their mind masters the physics of the game to elevate it to new dimensions, no musician who writes a song so inspiring that it births a sentient thought form in the depths of the human subconsciousness. If any of those examples became Inspired, their only hope to be playable is to don the white lab coat, strap on goggles, or take oration lessons because there is no way their Wonders will ever see the light of gameplay the way the rules are now. And that is the very opposite of inspiring.<br /> <br /> Again, this might just be the point of the game though. Being a mad scientist. But consider this: having the option to be a Genius from any background and profession opens up unlimited possibilities for character creation. Having the option to only play a Genius who's from a scientific field limits players options at character creation. Playing a mad scientist is achievable in both of the above options, while any other option is only available in one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T06:24:53-07:00","id":997655,"title":"","content":"I believe that's called the dark hero template.<br /> <br /> I actually spent a few days thinking about how one would make genius and have it cover things like athlete's and artists, but in the end it just diluted the themes and ended up looking like dark heroes+ a lot more work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-03-2016, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:00:12-07:00","id":997669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression#post997612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no artists who seek to create masterpieces in mediums never before attempted</div> </div> </div> </div>Their artwork are Wonders built using Expression. Probably a fair degree of Epikrato, since most &quot;magical artwork&quot; affects others via observation mediated mental influence. Alternatively, if you just want far out there artwork, Metatropi has you covered for shifting artwork, impossible engineering, and other material manipulations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression#post997612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no athlete so dedicated to the craft that their mind masters the physics of the game to elevate it to new dimensions</div> </div> </div> </div>Internalized Wonders representing their new inhuman feats. Probably best to be Navigators for their Grant ability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression#post997612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no musician who writes a song so inspiring that it births a sentient thought form in the depths of the human subconsciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>See above for artists, but add in some automata for new beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression#post997612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this might just be the point of the game though. Being a mad scientist. But consider this: having the option to be a Genius from any background and profession opens up unlimited possibilities for character creation. Having the option to only play a Genius who's from a scientific field limits players options at character creation. Playing a mad scientist is achievable in both of the above options, while any other option is only available in one.</div> </div> </div> </div>See above regarding options. While the material casts it as &quot;scientists and academics only&quot;, that's more because the source material lends itself directly there. The actual rule set allows for a staggering degree of flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:09:07-07:00","id":997703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression#post997612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This turned out to be more of an opinion piece, if you have any thoughts on the points brought up please post them below.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like Genius: the Transgression, never though I'd be saying that but I do none the less. It shows what creativity a fan game can bring to the table, and it's ideas can inspire stories that wouldn't normally come up in a Chronicle of Darkness.<br /> <br /> This is what make me so disappointed in Genius' failings though. For all it's themes of inspiration, potential, and creativity the game itself is one of the most stifling gamelines of the fan-made series. And here's why, my own thesis if you will: Geniuses must be scientists.<br /> <br /> Sure, this might be the obvious point of the game. Play as a mad scientists, create impossible inventions, explore infinite dimensions, Ect. But not all geniuses are scientists, but in Genius the Inspired must become scientist or inventors in order to do anything involving Wonders. There are no artists who seek to create masterpieces in mediums never before attempted, no athlete so dedicated to the craft that their mind masters the physics of the game to elevate it to new dimensions, no musician who writes a song so inspiring that it births a sentient thought form in the depths of the human subconsciousness. If any of those examples became Inspired, their only hope to be playable is to don the white lab coat, strap on goggles, or take oration lessons because there is no way their Wonders will ever see the light of gameplay the way the rules are now. And that is the very opposite of inspiring.<br /> <br /> Again, this might just be the point of the game though. Being a mad scientist. But consider this: having the option to be a Genius from any background and profession opens up unlimited possibilities for character creation. Having the option to only play a Genius who's from a scientific field limits players options at character creation. Playing a mad scientist is achievable in both of the above options, while any other option is only available in one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Concise. Infinitely more than <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> post. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T11:18:25-07:00","id":997783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=997703#post997703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Concise. Infinitely more than <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> post. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aiming for concise. I was aiming for thorough and clarifying. I was aiming for evisceration.<br /> <br /> That aside, I agree with Dusk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:09:01-07:00","id":997845,"title":"","content":"Wow, I'm now really glad I posted this. Thank you all so much for sharing your opinions on this matter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> I'm still a little confused about what you mean by the Dark Hero template, but I believe I understand the point your trying to make. While I still believe Genius has everything to benefit from non-scientist Geniuses, I can see how certain players might see an opportunity to make PCs that ruin the tone of the game.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> You knowI was afraid I might have overlooked something like those. It warms my heart tremendously to see that there are options for Wonders beyond scientific inventions. Thank you so much for pointing those out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a> *bows* thank you for the complement. I was afraid my critique was a bit too biased, I'm very glad you found it even handed. This is the first real Critique post I've ever done.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Very glad to see I'm not the only one with those critiques about Genius. Would you mind posting a link to that critique you wrote about Genius, I'm a long time fan of your posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If there is still an interest I could continue this Critical Evaluation of Genius, my biggest point was it's scientist-centrism but there are a few nitpicks I have that might make interesting topics for discussion. Like how the Baramin of Lemuria are fantastic antagonists but have no real playability (which really sucks because they're so cool), or how the Peerage's decisive victory in the Invisible War has actually weakened the story potential for the game over all (seriously without the Lemurians I have no idea why the Peerage hasn't fallen to infighting yet), or how Catalysts could really use a reinventing since they really seem out of place amongst all of the other X Splats (seriously your supposed to become the Hulk because the experiment goes wrong, not because your mind expands to new unfathomable dimensions...ok that was a pot shot at the Grimm but come on!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:14:46-07:00","id":997850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=997845#post997845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Very glad to see I'm not the only one with those critiques about Genius. Would you mind posting a link to that critique you wrote about Genius, I'm a long time fan of your posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Here's what's up <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius\">(namely an intro and a <i>lot</i> of talking about Genius up to the Catalysts)</a>. I've actually been getting a lot of requests to continue, and a recent conversation has me wanting to compare the science fetishism of Genius versus Mage and Demon, so some conversations should be starting soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:25:45-07:00","id":997856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=997850#post997850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Here's what's up <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius\">(namely an intro and a <i>lot</i> of talking about Genius up to the Catalysts)</a>. I've actually been getting a lot of requests to continue, and a recent conversation has me wanting <b>to compare the science fetishism of Genius versus Mage and Demon,</b> so some conversations should be starting soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>YAAAAAAAASSSSSSS.<br /> <br /> Ahem. I mean, &quot;Yes, please&quot;. Your critique wasn't concise, but it was sure as hell as thorough as it was entertaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:38:04-07:00","id":997914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=997845#post997845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I'm now really glad I posted this. Thank you all so much for sharing your opinions on this matter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> I'm still a little confused about what you mean by the Dark Hero template, but I believe I understand the point your trying to make. While I still believe Genius has everything to benefit from non-scientist Geniuses, I can see how certain players might see an opportunity to make PCs that ruin the tone of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mirrors has a supernatural template that represents the person being supernaturally good at what they're good at. A craftsman could create amazing devices with little materials, an athlete could run as fast as a car, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T16:31:49-07:00","id":997952,"title":"","content":"Aaaah, ok. It did sound like something out of Mirrors. <br /> <br /> I guess my beef was mostly that Genius seems to have such a narrow focus. If a Genius is a Genius because their minds can process chaos fueled Mania into Inspiration and Wonders then why does it matter what form those wonders take. So much delicious weirdness has already come out of bleeding edge Chroncles of Darkness supplements like Demon: the Descent and especially the upcoming Deviant: the Renegades, why not explore all conceivable iterations of creativity and mad inspiration? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:09:43-07:00","id":997966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=997952#post997952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So much delicious weirdness has already come out of bleeding edge Chroncles of Darkness supplements like Demon: the Descent and especially the upcoming Deviant: the Renegades, why not explore all conceivable iterations of creativity and mad inspiration? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly just making sure it says with the theme of mad science. Tends to be difficult unless you're either a mad scientist or a mad scientist's experiment (or both in the case of some self-afflicted Remade). It's not really mad science if a guy is just a ridiculously good painter or sculpter, it just ends up being that they're supernaturally good at art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-04-2016, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:48:23-07:00","id":997984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=997952#post997952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaah, ok. It did sound like something out of Mirrors.<br /> <br /> I guess my beef was mostly that Genius seems to have such a narrow focus. If a Genius is a Genius because their minds can process chaos fueled Mania into Inspiration and Wonders then why does it matter what form those wonders take. So much delicious weirdness has already come out of bleeding edge Chroncles of Darkness supplements like Demon: the Descent and especially the upcoming Deviant: the Renegades, why not explore all conceivable iterations of creativity and mad inspiration? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the big things overlooked with Genius was why mad scientists were folded in with Mages to begin with-that it's a surprisingly limited view that really just echoes the larger realm that mages were for a much longer period of time. It needed fleshing out and expanding, and Genius really didn't do that in any sense of the concept. Mad scientists was already a narrower niche than a whole splat needed to be (and that's keeping in mind that in fan-splats we're talking about contenders that includes <i>just </i>dragons, magical girls, and things of the like), but then it goes on to shoot itself in the foot over and over again by refusing to deepen itself out. Whether the answer was applying artistry and other things into it or branching outward with it's theme of mad science to make it so it could apply to any character concept, Genius just didn't care and opted for this half-assed middle ground that doesn't amount to anything.<br /> <br /> Again, if you asked me to sum up the main problem of Genius, it's that it spends a whole lot time proving that it is nothing. It obstinately <i>refuses</i> to be anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T00:38:47-07:00","id":998129,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> Well this is sort of the root of my critique though. Genius' theme isn't Mad Science, it's Transgression. It's theme is about breaking an accepted law, be it mundane or cosmic, and having to live with the consequences of such an action. Hell, one could say that the process of becoming inspired is the First Transgression. The metaphorical fruit of knowledge that will forever take away the paradise of innocence and rationality. Mad Science is the trappings of Genius, just like Magic is the trappings of both Mage the Awakening and Ascension. Both games were never about magic. Their trappings gave framework for how to begin exploring the game world. Genius' trappings don't do that. Instead it suffocates creativity like Manes doubt to an Unmada's obsession. Genius could be great! But instead it's simply decent. (My major nitpick that keeps it from being good will be addressed in the paragraph below.) <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I've been reading the post you linked earlier and am impressed with your review. It's given me a little more insight into the history of Genius and is entertaining to boot. In regards to your critique in the post above though, I would postulate that it's problem isn't so much refusing to be anything (After everything I've read I believe it's definitely trying to be something), but rather it's refusing to be a Chronicles of Darkness game. And by that, and I mean this truly, it's refusing to be a horror game. (At the end of the day, Genius is a game about power fantasy rather than horror. One of the many vestiges of it's One World of Darkness heritage.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 11-04-2016, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T00:51:34-07:00","id":998135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998129#post998129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> Well this is sort of the root of my critique though. Genius' theme isn't Mad Science, it's Transgression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't mean that it shouldn't be Mad Science. People who are just really good painters aren't exactly known as horror archetypes are they? If you take away the mad science, it is Just mage or Just Dark Heroes. In my opinion, the focus on mad science should be increased, so that it does it's own thing with it rather than just being &quot;Mage + that hack from Chronicler's Guide&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T01:59:32-07:00","id":998143,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> I've given Genius a lot of the benefit of the doubt, but if you're going to purpose that the game's core theme become Mad Science then let's take a critical look at exactly what mad science is getting done in Genius: the Transgression. <br /> <br /> In Genius, a Wonder is an invention that's powered by a supernatural power source called Mania. A Wonder works because the Genius believes it does, and will either go haywire or self destruct if a regular mortal, supernatural creature, or just another Genius with a different set of beliefs examines it or sees it function. And the Lemurians, Geniuses who believe their delusions are real, use Wonders that are already scientifically impossible and only work because of the Mania powering it and because they truly believe it works. And Wonders are able to alter the very fabric of space and time to a degree that could spell the end of the entire world should one powerful enough get out of hand.<br /> <br /> That isn't science. That isn't even mad science. That's magic. Specifically, that is Mage: the Ascension Magik. <br /> <br /> If one was to center the core theme around a supernatural power source that alters the fabric of space and time when given a physical medium in reality, the only real themes that could be explored with any real depth would be themes of choice and consequences. Of exploration and transgression. If it doesn't freak'n matter what medium the Mana...I mean Mania takes then why shackle the entire game to one single trope?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 11-04-2016, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T04:01:00-07:00","id":998165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998143#post998143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> I've given Genius a lot of the benefit of the doubt, but if you're going to purpose that the game's core theme become Mad Science then let's take a critical look at exactly what mad science is getting done in Genius: the Transgression.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're misunderstanding me. I'm suggesting the point is to be Mad Science, it fails at it (horribly in my opinion), but that is the horror archetype it is trying to reflect. By stopping it from trying to be mad science, it has no reason to even exist because what you desire is just mage or just dark heroes. At least mad science has a reason to try and find a way for the mechanics to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That isn't science. That isn't even mad science. That's magic. Specifically, that is Mage: the Ascension Magik. </div> </div> </div>I'm aware, that's why I said the mad science needs to be increased as right now if you take away the mad science it has, it's just Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-04-2016, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T04:20:26-07:00","id":998168,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> Sorry, you're entirely right. I feel that more concretely defining what Mania is and how Wonders are science would<br /> greeeeeatly help the gameline as a whole. One way or another Genius really needs to commit to either real weird science or Occult Matrix God Machine science-magic. <br /> <br /> That being said, my aesthetic for what constitutes mad science is very broad. Essentially if you can make an Etherite out of it you can make a mad scientist out of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:30:09-07:00","id":998219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998129#post998129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to your critique in the post above though, I would postulate that it's problem isn't so much refusing to be anything (After everything I've read I believe it's definitely trying to be something), but rather it's refusing to be a Chronicles of Darkness game. And by that, and I mean this truly, it's refusing to be a horror game. (At the end of the day, Genius is a game about power fantasy rather than horror. One of the many vestiges of it's One World of Darkness heritage.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Horror of Genius is a more personal Horror - the dread of knowing your mind is not entirely under your control and that the grand visions of possibility you see are crippled (perhaps terminally) by your own madness. It's <i>knowing</i> you can cure cancer, and knowing that if you try to publish or mass produce your work, being laughed at is the best outcome.<br /> <br /> It's also the Horror of knowing that your peers are capable of equally great wonders... and statistically possessing fewer scruples.<br /> <br /> Read (if you haven't already) Soon I Will Be Invincible and examine Doctor Impossible's plight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998143#post998143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Genius, a Wonder is an invention that's powered by a supernatural power source called Mania. A Wonder works because the Genius believes it does, and will either go haywire or self destruct if a regular mortal, supernatural creature, or just another Genius with a different set of beliefs examines it or sees it function. And the Lemurians, Geniuses who believe their delusions are real, use Wonders that are already scientifically impossible and only work because of the Mania powering it and because they truly believe it works. And Wonders are able to alter the very fabric of space and time to a degree that could spell the end of the entire world should one powerful enough get out of hand.<br /> <br /> That isn't science. That isn't even mad science. That's magic. Specifically, that is Mage: the Ascension Magik.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Wonder is an Invention that exploits scientific laws to achieve an outcome, like any other technology. Mania is what lets the fact that <i>physics do not work that way here</i> be ignored. A Wonder works because of the principles behind it, regardless of whether the Genius truly believes them (as proper Peers don't). It goes Haywire when exposed to others due to Havoc (<u>Watsonian</u>: incompatable observers collapse the waveform that makes Wonders stable | <u>Doylist</u>: Havoc is necessary for any kind of Masquerade, and for certain Mad Scientist tropes).<br /> <br /> It isn't science. It's Mad Science (which isn't actually related, except on surface aesthetic, to real science).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-04-2016, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:00:34-07:00","id":998250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998219#post998219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Horror of Genius is a more personal Horror - the dread of knowing your mind is not entirely under your control and that the grand visions of possibility you see are crippled (perhaps terminally) by your own madness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh. Of all horror tropes, this is probably my least favorite. It just has such distasteful implications. Same reason I'm not a fan of The Mad in Awakening. &quot;Mental instability is a thing to be feared&quot; just... doesn't sit well with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:13:49-07:00","id":998260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998250#post998250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh. Of all horror tropes, this is probably my least favorite. It just has such distasteful implications. Same reason I'm not a fan of The Mad in Awakening. &quot;Mental instability is a thing to be feared&quot; just... doesn't sit well with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; There's elements of it Vampire and Werewolf as well, with the influence of Frenzy and Death Rage. You (the hypothetical Vampire/Werewolf, I mean) might not want those to be factors, but they are and you'll need to deal with them. Changeling with Clarity as well - at a certain point, they must realize that what they think they see, isn't what is (what most would call) true. Their perceptions, if not their mind, is not entirely their own.<br /> <br /> And remembering that Genii don't get power from their atypical neural architecture, but rather that is a consequence of Inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:34:42-07:00","id":998268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998250#post998250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh. Of all horror tropes, this is probably my least favorite. It just has such distasteful implications. Same reason I'm not a fan of The Mad in Awakening. &quot;Mental instability is a thing to be feared&quot; just... doesn't sit well with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mad really need to be renamed, given that their point is that your reach has so exceeded it's grasp it's now <i>stuck</i> there. Theirs is not a broken mind, but a broken <i>will</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:40:18-07:00","id":998275,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998143#post998143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In Genius, a Wonder is an invention that's powered by a supernatural power source called Mania. A Wonder works because the Genius believes it does, and will either go haywire or self destruct if a regular mortal, supernatural creature, or just another Genius with a different set of beliefs examines it or sees it function. And the Lemurians, Geniuses who believe their delusions are real, use Wonders that are already scientifically impossible and only work because of the Mania powering it and because they truly believe it works. And Wonders are able to alter the very fabric of space and time to a degree that could spell the end of the entire world should one powerful enough get out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is simply factually wrong.<br /> <br /> 1) A Genius does not have to believe their wonder should work. The peerage explicitly encourages it's members to remember nobody has a clue why Wonders work.<br /> 2) Havoc is <i>only</i> caused by physical contact between mortals and wonders. If a Genius wants to make his living by selling ray guns to vampires you could do that with no Havoc at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998219#post998219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Horror of Genius is a more personal Horror - the dread of knowing your mind is not entirely under your control and that the grand visions of possibility you see are crippled (perhaps terminally) by your own madness. It's <i>knowing</i> you can cure cancer, and knowing that if you try to publish or mass produce your work, being laughed at is the best outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always read it as a more existential horror. The lack of control of your own mind is part of it. But it's only part.<br /> <br /> Lack of control in Genius is everywhere. Lack of control over your own mind. Lack of control over your country. Lack of control over your society.<br /> <br /> It's basically Lovecraft's cosmic horror, but from a different angle. Lovecraft says the universe is too big for anything you do to matter. Genius says the world is too chaotic for anything you do to matter. I much prefer Genius' take because ultimately the universe beyond Earth doesn't have much effect on my life, and here on Earth chaos is more potent than vastness.<br /> <br /> At the risk of using real life politics: The horror of Genius is basically the horror of the 2016 election. Of seeing a man like Trump moving closer and closer to the white house and realising you cannot do anything about it*. Of realising the things you thought you knew about how the world worked was wrong and being left adrift with no way to understand this strange new world. And of realising that everything you built is destined to crumble away: The American political system, an elegantly crafted wonder made by some of the finest minds slowly decays into Trump wielding unprecedented executive power.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Technically in the real world there are things you can do about it; Trump's victory is far from garmented and a Trump presidency is not garmented to destroy America. But metaphors don't have to be perfect. Actually just pretend I used the Republican primaries and you're a decent principled Republican.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998250#post998250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh. Of all horror tropes, this is probably my least favorite. It just has such distasteful implications. Same reason I'm not a fan of The Mad in Awakening. &quot;Mental instability is a thing to be feared&quot; just... doesn't sit well with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that idea really so strange to you? When somebody says they think Donald Tump's instability means people shouldn't vote for him does that make you uncomfortable?<br /> <br /> The thought of Donald Trump sitting in the oval office one tantrum away from declaring war makes me uncomfortable. I don't think that reflects any prejduice or moral failing on my part.<br /> <br /> (For the record I would say of all the Splats Donald Trump fits Genius best. Not because of his personality or mental state, but because he embodies Transgression. And the 2016 election is definately a Genius story: Nobody is in charge, nobody understand's what's going on, and nobody has a plan).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:42:30-07:00","id":998308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998268#post998268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mad really need to be renamed, given that their point is that your reach has so exceeded it's grasp it's now <i>stuck</i> there. Theirs is not a broken mind, but a broken <i>will</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. They don't really represent fear of madness, they just have an unfortunate name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:58:52-07:00","id":998314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998275#post998275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that idea really so strange to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not strange to me. Modern horror is replete with fear of &quot;insanity&quot;, so much so that psychological horror is its own subgenre. The fact that it's everywhere doesn't make me dislike it any less, in fact it's part of what makes me dislike it as much as I do. It worked when Lovecraft did it, because of the scientific climate of the time. Now it's old hat, and with our growing understanding of psychology, it's nice to see places where the horror genre is beginning to grow out of using &quot;madness&quot; as a cheap source of horror and start handling the subject with a bit more maturity, and saddening when I see horror that still treats &quot;losing your mind&quot; as a fate equal to or worse than death.<br /> <br /> Full disclosure, I haven't actually read Genius, for all I know it could be a mature and nuanced take on psychological horror. But, the subject matter just isn't appealing to me in the first place, so I am unlikely to dig into it enough to find out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998275#post998275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When somebody says they think Donald Tump's instability means people shouldn't vote for him does that make you uncomfortable?<br /> <br /> The thought of Donald Trump sitting in the oval office one tantrum away from declaring war makes me uncomfortable. I don't think that reflects any prejduice or moral failing on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a completely different case. This is a fear of what Donald Trump might <i>do</i> if given the power to do it, not a fear of &quot;losing your mind&quot;. It's also not a work of fiction influencing how the general public views &quot;insanity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is really not the place for this discussion, so I'll step off my soapbox. Sorry for bringing it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:32:32-07:00","id":998338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998314#post998314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full disclosure, I haven't actually read Genius, for all I know it could be a mature and nuanced take on psychological horror.</div> </div> </div> </div> As I said to Vent0: I wouldn't consider Genius to be a psychological horror at all. The horror in Genius is loss of control, and loosing control over your own mind is just one aspect of a central theme that's far broader than psychological or modern ideas of psychology.<br /> <br /> To give an example. You could play Joan of Arc as a Genius. She has Transgression (woman in a man's role sense, peasent looking kings in the eye sense) and ultimately even with her armies and &quot;god on her side&quot; she was powerless before the English (who didn't hold onto France forever).<br /> <br /> Modern Geniuses consider their mental differences (to pick a neutral word) to be madness. Medieval Geniuses literally believed that their Inspiration was an angel riding in their body whispering ideas. While in the real world I feel confident saying Joan of Arc wasn't being given guidence directly from heaven perhaps the Geniuses are. Angels do exist in the WoD.<br /> <br /> (However the Peerage discourages thinking like that. It tends to result in ranting on the today show and giant death robots attacking your old university).<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW Joan of Arc would probably specalise in creating speaches so powerful they have supernatural effects. It's easy to do with the Genius mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998314#post998314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a completely different case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. I was thinking of the Genius from a mortals point of view. I fear a Genius' mental instability because he has a giant death robot; just like I fear Trump's instability because he might have the presidency.<br /> <br /> You and Vent0 were thinking about the Genius' own fear of his own mental instability and I mixed it up. Mia Culpa.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:04:07-07:00","id":998357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998338#post998338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As I said to Vent0: I wouldn't consider Genius to be a psychological horror at all. The horror in Genius is loss of control, and loosing control over your own mind is just one aspect of a central theme that's far broader than psychological or modern ideas of psychology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sure. Just saying, fear of loss of control of your own mind is an aspect, and one that I tend not to be a big fan of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998338#post998338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To give an example. You could play Joan of Arc as a Genius. She has Transgression (woman in a man's role sense, peasent looking kings in the eye sense) and ultimately even with her armies and &quot;god on her side&quot; she was powerless before the English (who didn't hold onto France forever).<br /> <br /> Modern Geniuses consider their mental differences (to pick a neutral word) to be madness. Medieval Geniuses literally believed that their Inspiration was an angel riding in their body whispering ideas. While in the real world I feel confident saying Joan of Arc wasn't being given guidence directly from heaven perhaps the Geniuses are. Angels do exist in the WoD.<br /> <br /> (However the Peerage discourages thinking like that. It tends to result in ranting on the today show and giant death robots attacking your old university).<br /> <br /> BTW Joan of Arc would probably specalise in creating speaches so powerful they have supernatural effects. It's easy to do with the Genius mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Casting Joan of Arc as a mad scientist does not sound cool to me, to be honest. I agree with Dusksage on this, it might appeal to me more if the mad science focus was broadened to divine inspiration of all stripes. I also agree with Arcane that we've got a perfectly good source of divine inspiration and obsession in the ChroD already, and it just makes sense for it to be the source that Genii's inspiration comes from. But, I'm committed to taking my own advice and just not playing Genius because I'm distinctly not it's target audience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998338#post998338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair point. I was thinking of the Genius from a mortals point of view. I fear a Genius' mental instability because he has a giant death robot; just like I fear Trump's instability because he might have the presidency.<br /> <br /> You and Vent0 were thinking about the Genius' own fear of his own mental instability and I mixed it up. Mia Culpa.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-04-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:46:30-07:00","id":998393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998357#post998357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, sure. Just saying, fear of loss of control of your own mind is an aspect, and one that I tend not to be a big fan of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998357#post998357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... Casting Joan of Arc as a mad scientist does not sound cool to me, to be honest. I agree with Dusksage on this, it might appeal to me more if the mad science focus was broadened to divine inspiration of all stripes. I also agree with Arcane that we've got a perfectly good source of divine inspiration and obsession in the ChroD already, and it just makes sense for it to be the source that Genii's inspiration comes from. But, I'm committed to taking my own advice and just not playing Genius because I'm distinctly not it's target audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it <i>is</i> called <i>Inspiration</i>. You can model prophets as well as physicists. Where Genius is useful is in more targeted applications of ability (which Mage doesn't lend itself as well to - Arcana are <i>made</i> to be flexible). Themes are different as well. Genius doesn't claim to have The Truth (in fact, the Peerage knows they have anything but).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T13:23:33-07:00","id":998411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998357#post998357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... Casting Joan of Arc as a mad scientist does not sound cool to me, to be honest. I agree with Dusksage on this, it might appeal to me more if the mad science focus was broadened to divine inspiration of all stripes.</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't say &quot;mad scientist&quot; did I?<br /> <br /> Genius: the Transgression is quite explicit that &quot;mad science&quot; is a cultural thing among the Inspired rather than the one true expression of Inspiration.<br /> <br /> From the introduction <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As humanity has always admired and feared its law-givers, it has always admired and feared its law-breakers, its madmen, its geniuses. Every society has stories of those who went too far, who asked too much, and who suffered for it. The mad scientist is new, but the genius is an old dream indeed: the prophet, the trickster-god, the master of techne, the artificer who makes the world, the demiurge who seeks to control, bind, and direct it. </div> </div> </div>Or even more explicitly from the Z-Splats appendix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> some people are able to create objects of wonder, impossible by any reasonable understanding of how the world works.<br /> <br /> But there is nothing except tradition, say the members of the Hermetic Order, that says that these wonders must be &quot;mad science.&quot; </div> </div> </div>(The Hermetic Order like to build &quot;magic wands&quot; and other such un-scientific Wonders. Some are sincere researchers trying to see how far away from science they can go before Wonders won't work. Others just think magic wands are cool or enjoy annoying the more hidebound members of the Peerage)<br /> <br /> Joan of Arc isn't a mad scientist, but she is a &quot;transgressive visionary&quot;, and the themes of Genius fit her story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998357#post998357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also agree with Arcane that we've got a perfectly good source of divine inspiration and obsession in the ChroD already</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically I don't think the Divine Fire would work.<br /> <br /> While it's certainly not the only valid reading; the existence of the Divine Fire says to me that there is a purpose to the universe, there is a Divine Plan. Genius' fundamental theme is that there is no plan.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is not the first time the WoD's had multiple similar things before. Remember the Arcadia/Arcadia debates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-04-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:31:13-07:00","id":998469,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>, your both entirely right about my mistake in comparing Wonders to Ascension Magik. Sorry about that, I knew I'd make some missteps with some of my example and just hoped they wouldn't be to large. Two thing I still believe I haven't misstepped though is my assertion that Wonders aren't Mad Science, and that Genius isn't a horror game. The latter I'll get into in a second because I've been wanting to talk about this but didn't know how well my first critique would be received (which was beyond my wildest hopes after all I've heard about the Genius fanbase, thank you all so much for helping me better understand this beautifully flawed game), but for the former I'm going to have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> point that Genius' refusal to properly define how Wonders work and function might be one of the games biggest aesthetic shortcomings. It's a shortcoming I can accept though, so long as they more properly define Mania and it's source, but it's still a shortcoming. <br /> <br /> And now nothing more to do and to get to it shall we? My second thesis if you will: Genius isn't a Horror Game.<br /> <br /> Genius: the Transgression, like it's progenitors in the One World of Darkness, is a Urban (Science)Fantasy game with Horror Elements. It's core gameplay is power fantasy because it's Theme is Transgression but it has no real Accusers to punish the Geniuses should they transgress beyond having their own inventions go haywire, or loosing their grip on conventional reality for a time. It's set in the Chronicles of Darkness world because it's Mood is Bitter Disappointment, but there are no stakes or motivations to fuel said despair beyond having one's inventions blow up in one's face or loosing a grip on conventional reality. <br /> <br /> My point: A good horror game merely need to paint a world where the player character become unavoidably tied to the unknown, that way horror can sink into the player characters as they slowly discover what they've become, who they really are, how the world truly is, how much remains unknown, an how horrifying those mysteries would be should they ever be answered. <br /> <br /> And to Genius' credit it does try to do this. By the powers does it try so hard to be horror. But ultimately it falls flat because nothing cathartic is gained from the horror elements in the game. There's no lesson learned or question asked by the horror elements, so it winds up more set dressing than anything. And that's a real shame, because loss of control can be an excellent source of horror. Instead, it just becomes a side effect of failure. There's no horror in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:43:35-07:00","id":998612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998393#post998393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it <i>is</i> called <i>Inspiration</i>. You can model prophets as well as physicists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dilution is a problem. A game about magic users has enough space for prophets and physicists. To say a game about mad scientists can model prophets as well as physicists sounds off. There's some technical truth there, but not as much as the former. It's weaker, it looses strength as it becomes spread out too thin. Our suspension of disbelief wavers, our investment in the icon that is trying to be sold here decreases.<br /> <br /> Genius was always going to be a limited game in one of two ways-it could either broaden up and be a game about visionaries, artists, sociologists, etc, or it could really dig into it's area of science, at the cost of everything else.<br /> <br /> Genius tells me it's about Mad Scientists, so I assume it thinks it chose the latter. It performed it poorly, and the fact that people keep telling me this is a game about visionaries tells me it didn't commit to that choice.<br /> <br /> If you want a game about visionaries, <i>make that game</i>. And yeah, good fucking luck not making it Another Mage. If you want a game about Mad Scientists, cut your loses and <i>make that game</i>. You actually have a chance to make that Not Another Mage. It will not be as extensive or elaborate as some people want, but this is the price you pay for subject matter. You have to make to the scale of your concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-05-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T00:58:33-07:00","id":998645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DsgHmwnAIV4\" data-code=\"DsgHmwnAIV4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DsgHmwnAIV4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> This?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T01:38:43-07:00","id":998651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998469#post998469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius: the Transgression, like it's progenitors in the One World of Darkness, is a Urban (Science)Fantasy game with Horror Elements.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think that Genius needs an accuser splat to be horrific. Geniuses are supposed to be their own accusers, in their moments of lucidity asking themselves how their attempts to cure cancer ended up with harvesting orphans for parts or accusing their ecconomic supercomputer when it decides the best way to create new jobs is to build a wall on the Mexican border.<br /> <br /> It requires a skilled group of players and Storytellers to consistently make decisions that lead to their own downfall but I do not think that it is wrong for a Storytelling game to target itself at skilled players.<br /> <br /> Besides however horrific or un-horrific Genius is. It's no more of an urban fantasy game with horror elements than Geist: the Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998612#post998612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dilution is a problem. A game about magic users has enough space for prophets and physicists. To say a game about mad scientists can model prophets as well as physicists sounds off.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm know a lot of people who think Werewolves being &quot;spirit world border patrol&quot; feels off. That doesn't mean it actually is off.<br /> <br /> In the introduction to Frankenstein Mary Shelly says she was inspired by Shakespear's the Tempest. Compare victor Frankenstein hidden on the Orkney Islands with his monster practising his secret art to Prospero on his island surrounded by mythical creatures and practising his secret art. Prospero in turn is inspired by Merlin - who is of course a famous prophet.<br /> <br /> Frankenstein is also an alchemist, not a scientist, and in this he is from a long and established literacy tradition of alchemists that draw a distinction between bad alchemists who (like Victor) peruse worldly knowledge or worldly power and good alchemists who use their art to bring themselves closer to god (the other definition of prophet).<br /> <br /> <br /> The literacy tradition of the mad scientist has increasingly diverged from it's historical origins in the spiritual, but the legacy remains. Prospero on is island with spirits, became Victor on his island with the monster, became Ozymandus in Antarctica with Bubastis and Syndrome on his island with his robots.<br /> <br /> To say that it's &quot;off&quot; for a game about mad scientists to acknowledge the historical origins of the mad scientist archetype and include characters modelled on those earlier archetypes (common in the sitting's backstory, rarer as the setting passes the point the mad scientist archetype diverges from it's roots) is frankly baffling to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998612#post998612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius tells me it's about Mad Scientists</div> </div> </div> </div>No. This is factually wrong. Genius tells you it's about visionaries in the introduction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T02:37:11-07:00","id":998663,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a>, Thank you for putting a link to that video as a response. It's a fine example of how to build an environment of horror. I do believe Genius really tries to do that too. It's just that rather than making it about the dark, terrifying, and wondrous world of the Chronicles of Darkness fighting back against a perfectly sane and brilliant mind trying to unlock it's mysteries and push it's boundaries, it instead tries to make...Quiet. It tries to make Quiet from Mage the Ascension. There, I said it. But you see, here's the thing. Quiet is a horror element in Ascension because it represents the Consensus punishing a Mage's hubris for trying to make it bend to their beliefs. It's response: give the Mage a piece of their own medicine by bending their perception of reality to mirror the Mage's hubris. In Genius though, Unmada is no outside force punishing a Genius for their transgressions. It's just a Genius' brain getting fried on Mania juice because they thought they could handle it. It's more of a drug overdose rather than opening Pandora's box. That's why it falls flat horror wise. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>, I can definitely agree that Geist is certainly the most Urban Fantasy oriented of the CofD gamelines (alongside Vampire of course) but it is definitely a Horror game. The reason for that (and a reason Genius certainly could benefit from) is the inescapable Other in the form of the Geist itself. A Sin-Eater's life depends upon the Geist, and it's an alien entity that feeds on death. No matter what, there will always be a shadow over the Sin-Eaters shoulder, a homage to Wraith the Oblivion's Shadow Play. Genius has no such tension, a Genius lost to Unmada is driven by certainty. There is no horror in certainty. There an be dread and despair, but not horror. Horror doesn't come during moments of lucidity where you ask yourself how your attempts to cure cancer ended up with you harvesting orphans for parts. Horror comes from discovering that the world you live in is nothing like you innocently believed. Horror lives and breaths in the moments where you wonder what's better: knowing or not knowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-05-2016, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T03:35:41-07:00","id":998678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998663#post998663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason for that (and a reason Genius certainly could benefit from) is the inescapable Other in the form of the Geist itself. A Sin-Eater's life depends upon the Geist, and it's an alien entity that feeds on death.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was actually pretty disapointed by how benign and passive the Geist came across (especially in the games I played).<br /> <br /> While the Dem Bones SAS did a really good job of creating a unique and horrific Geist. I don't think I've ever seen a Geist cause trouble for a Sin-Eater in any of the games I've played. You don't even loose Synergy if a moral Sin-Eater refuses to kill people when their Geist Murder McSlauhgter asks them too.<br /> <br /> Genius very much does have in inescapable Other in the form of Inspiration. A Geist (who died in a car accident) whipsering in your ear to cut the break lines when you walk past a parked car is very similar to Inspiration pushing you to upgrade the engine (which would cause a car crash when it goes 0-500 mph in seconds). Inspiration isn't portrayed as a singular entity you can talk to like the Geist, but it is <i>definately</i> an inescapable Other riding along in your head.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've certainly seen more Geniuses pushed into making bad decisions by Inspiration than Sin-Eaters pushed into making bad decisions by their Geist. That might just be a coincidence of course, but I suspect that it might be more interesting for players to create giant death robots and attack the university than to cut break lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998663#post998663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horror lives and breaths in the moments where you wonder what's better: knowing or not knowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Geist asks you &quot;what's better knowing or not knowing&quot;. Take one of the biggest mysteries in all of human existance: what happens after death. Geist answers that question and it pretty firmly says Sin-Eaters are better of now that they know. Even with a particularly nasty Geist in your head, you still get to a point where the knowledge is good and the Geist is bad. I cannot think of anywhere in Geist where it says Sin-Eaters would be better of for not knowing about the truths of death.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile that question, &quot;what's better knowing or not knowing&quot; is the very core of Genius: What's better blissful ignornace or knowing that the world is so chaotic that nothing anyone does will ever go according to plan?<br /> <br /> <br /> I think your view on horror is rather narrow - but given your views I can see why you wouldn't see Unmada as horrific. If you take &quot;what's better knowing or not knowing&quot; then from that perspective Unmada are the people who say &quot;blissful ignorance is definately better&quot; and dive right in. From that perspective, of course choosing blissful ignorance is going to be less horrific than not choosing blissful ignorance.<br /> <br /> From that perspective the fact nobody punishes an Unmada is missing the point. For the choice between blissful ignorance and painful knowledge to be meaningful you have to have the ability to choose blissful ignorance. Punishing Unmada would just be taking that choice away from Geniuses and deminish the possibility.<br /> <br /> Being an Unmada isn't horrific. Being a non-Unmada Genius and having to live every day with facing the truth or giving in, becoming Unmada, and becoming part of the problem is horrific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T04:20:20-07:00","id":998692,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>, I don't want to assume anything. But I fear you might have been robbed of some of Geists' best features. To me it's always been a game about human nature, attachment, memory, death, suffering, and the unknown. I have had a very positive experience with Geist on the other hand. Perhaps that shadows out disagreements with the two games mentioned. <br /> <br /> It is getting rather late for me though so I'll leave for now after a quick final though: The best horror stories in my opinion leave the reader asking themselves questions at the end. The last Chonicle I had the privilege to play in left me asking myself if I put to much faith in the writen word when the hand that wrote it may have had treacherous intent, if I had ever let my assumptions and pride make a bad situation out of nothing, if there was any lesson to be learned at all from an event where there were no witnesses left to tell the tale. This all coming from a Chronicle where in the end all of the player character turned out to be the real monsters of the chronicle the entire time, and this was a 1st Edition NWoD Mortals Chronicle too. That is how I gained catharsis from the train wreck that Chonicle turned out to be for our characters (Best Chronicle I ever played in though.) What questions were you left with at the end of your horror story? How did you gain catharsis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-05-2016, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T05:18:29-07:00","id":998706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998692#post998692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>, I don't want to assume anything. But I fear you might have been robbed of some of Geists' best features.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh. It's probably a fair assumption.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I had a <i>bad</i> experience with Geist. The games I played were urban fantasy and not horror, but they were good urban fantasy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998692#post998692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it's always been a game about human nature, attachment, memory, death, suffering, and the unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div> No disagreements from me. But none of those things are inherently horrific. It's all about how they're portrayed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998692#post998692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What questions were you left with at the end of your horror story? How did you gain catharsis?</div> </div> </div> </div>The question I was left with: What do you do when nothing you do is going to matter.<br /> <br /> The answer: Enjoy the day to day and try not to think too much about it. I have family members who're literally terrified that Donald Trump might get elected. But to me, this will always be the election where a presidential candidate picked a fight with a cartoon frog. Accepting I can't do anything has liberated me from that fear. That's the catharsis Genius left me, not just from the chronicle, but from the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:48:26-07:00","id":998762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998706#post998706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question I was left with: What do you do when nothing you do is going to matter.<br /> <br /> The answer: Enjoy the day to day and try not to think too much about it. I have family members who're literally terrified that Donald Trump might get elected. But to me, this will always be the election where a presidential candidate picked a fight with a cartoon frog. Accepting I can't do anything has liberated me from that fear. That's the catharsis Genius left me, not just from the chronicle, but from the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really leaving you with a question if it asks a question and then answers it. Also the fact that the answer &quot;liberates you from fear&quot; is kind of a clear indication that it's not so horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-05-2016, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T09:35:51-07:00","id":998800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998762#post998762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really leaving you with a question if it asks a question and then answers it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Genius didn't answer the question. I answered it, because Genius gave me a question and a world to explore it in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998762#post998762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also the fact that the answer &quot;liberates you from fear&quot; is kind of a clear indication that it's not so horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does not compute.<br /> <br /> The fact I faced something scary, then overcame that fear to the point it didn't phase me at all the second time does not in any way mean it's wasn't scary in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:05:00-07:00","id":998826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998762#post998762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really leaving you with a question if it asks a question and then answers it. Also the fact that the answer &quot;liberates you from fear&quot; is kind of a clear indication that it's not so horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, this is kind of par for the course given certain elements of the play here, vis a vis certain peoples and certain subjects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-05-2016, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T14:21:40-07:00","id":998886,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>, Good morning. For what it's worth Geist is the closest of the CofD gamelines to being Urban Fantasy, and as long as you had a great time with it then I'm glad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Right, now back to the thick of things. I believe what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> was trying to say, and please correct me if I'm assuming to much, is that horror is nullified if the mystery behind the horror is transparent. It would be like walking up to an enclosure at the zoo and seeing behind the glass window a black and roiling void that seems to pull you in while simultaneously trying to expand and escape it's enclosure vs. that exact same scenario except there's a display name on the glass window that says: Paradox Spirit, avoid eye contact. <br /> <br /> Ok, sorry. That was a bit of an extreme example, but here's the thing. If a horror game is going to be about nihilism, then nihilism needs to stalk the players like a hungry wolf, always at the treeline gathering it's pack until the player is at their most vulnerable. Then *Blam!* it goes in for the kill. Here's the problem with that, if there is no win scenario for the players, then this is essentially a one trick pony. Because if nothing truly matters in that game then there's no reason to pick it up again except for cathartic wanton abandon. <br /> <br /> I mentioned that the best horror stories make you ask questions once the story is over, this is because at it's heart horror is about terrifying agency. It's about examining the steps the characters took to get to the end and realize mistakes and empathy along the way. I ask you this: Was &quot;What do you do when nothing you do is going to matter?&quot; the only question Genius left you with? If not, then there is more nuance to the game then it let's aware upon examination. If so, then why isn't there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 11-05-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T14:36:18-07:00","id":998891,"title":"","content":"The terror of the mad scientist is not in that they fail, but that they might succeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:48:48-07:00","id":998922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998891#post998891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The terror of the mad scientist is not in that they fail, but that they might succeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that they fail, but in such a way that sucks for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T16:17:51-07:00","id":998934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998891#post998891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The terror of the mad scientist is not in that they fail, but that they might succeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even Pokemon realised this was the horror of mad scientists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T17:48:53-07:00","id":998960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998922#post998922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or that they fail, but in such a way that sucks for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a &quot;Success in tampering with forces they weren't mean to touch, failure to control in any meaningful way&quot;<br /> <br /> Grasp, Reach, etc. The personal horror of a mad scientist is realizing that what they thought they wanted was nothing but a lie they told themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:18:15-07:00","id":998971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998960#post998960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a &quot;Success in tampering with forces they weren't mean to touch, failure to control in any meaningful way&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. Depends how one is defining Success and Failure criteria.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998960#post998960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The personal horror of a mad scientist is realizing that what they thought they wanted was nothing but a lie they told themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreement.<br /> <br /> I think (and run) part of the horror behind Genius is that Inspiration gives you want you <i>want</i> (or, as you said, think you do), but not what you <i>need</i>. It offers shortcuts that rob the final result of any real victory. A mind-controlled board still doesn't actually respect your research (which frankly, is probably bunk anyways), and vaporizing goons still doesn't fix the underlying reason for the crime problems in a city. It just makes you an asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:49:38-07:00","id":998985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998960#post998960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a &amp;quot;Success in tampering with forces they weren't mean to touch, failure to control in any meaningful way&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Grasp, Reach, etc. The personal horror of a mad scientist is realizing that what they thought they wanted was nothing but a lie they told themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you did there, but I'm not sure if I should spoil it for everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:20:52-07:00","id":998998,"title":"","content":"It's not like it's some big secret. Honestly, the worst part about that is I spent about five minutes trying to avoid saying it before I caved in.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest-while, yes, the biggest problem with Genius is basically that it wants to be a Mage(even if it technically doesn't, it sure as fuck reads that way) but fails to get why the Mages work the way it does(because it does), I <i>reall</i><i>y</i> hate having to even mention it. It is a point that has been brought up to death, and while the fact it is so like the Mages can be chocked up as another failure, at the end of the day, I've seen a lot of fans be annoyed to death by the comparisons, and in fairness I think there's better conversation beyond &quot;It's a failed Mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> Namely in that Genius can fail in a thousand ways unrelated to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:01:35-07:00","id":999017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998998#post998998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like it's some big secret. Honestly, the worst part about that is I spent about five minutes trying to avoid saying it before I caved in.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest-while, yes, the biggest problem with Genius is basically that it wants to be a Mage(even if it technically doesn't, it sure as fuck reads that way) but fails to get why the Mages work the way it does(because it does), I <i>reall</i><i>y</i> hate having to even mention it. It is a point that has been brought up to death, and while the fact it is so like the Mages can be chocked up as another failure, at the end of the day, I've seen a lot of fans be annoyed to death by the comparisons, and in fairness I think there's better conversation beyond &quot;It's a failed Mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> Namely in that Genius can fail in a thousand ways unrelated to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the goal, in the end, is to make sure it fails one of <i>those</i> ways instead.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I really do like Genius, but I also don't deny that it is kind of a Mage Ersatz in a lot of ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 11-05-2016, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:08:32-07:00","id":999024,"title":"","content":"I think the goals for it should be a) do more to concretely set it's identity in place, and b) don't fail at all. It currently has the problem of failing in all those ways.<br /> <br /> Catalysts are a good idea, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T03:50:34-08:00","id":999146,"title":"","content":"Ok, I have one last nitpick that I'd like to talk about...ok, I'm not even sure if it's a nitpick anymore. I saw this was a topic being brought up in the 2nd Edition Idea Thread for Genius and now my mind won't know rest until I've at least put them to words. <br /> <br /> I like Genius: the Transgression, but I fear Genius: the Transgression doesn't like me. Or, in other words: Genius has a reeeaaaalllly big chip on it's shoulders as a game setting.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the whole &quot;Being a Genius means realizing that nothing I do will ever matter&quot; theme the game so often reiterates. It's so strange because compared to all of the CofD Core Gamelines (and hell, even all of the other CofD Fan Gamelines) it really doesn't match up to the world that those games paint the setting as a whole to be, and Chronicles goes soooooo far out of it's way to maintain a pretty consistent aesthetic and tone for it's setting's world. When examined as a whole in the Chronicles of Darkness, it's almost like the games trying to say &quot;Being a Genius means that nothing I do will ever matter.&quot; That...that...whaaaat?!? Please someone tell me I'm not understanding this correctly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-06-2016, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T04:58:12-08:00","id":999168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999146#post999146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I have one last nitpick that I'd like to talk about...ok, I'm not even sure if it's a nitpick anymore. I saw this was a topic being brought up in the 2nd Edition Idea Thread for Genius and now my mind won't know rest until I've at least put them to words.<br /> <br /> I like Genius: the Transgression, but I fear Genius: the Transgression doesn't like me. Or, in other words: Genius has a reeeaaaalllly big chip on it's shoulders as a game setting.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the whole &quot;Being a Genius means realizing that nothing I do will ever matter&quot; theme the game so often reiterates. It's so strange because compared to all of the CofD Core Gamelines (and hell, even all of the other CofD Fan Gamelines) it really doesn't match up to the world that those games paint the setting as a whole to be, and Chronicles goes soooooo far out of it's way to maintain a pretty consistent aesthetic and tone for it's setting's world. When examined as a whole in the Chronicles of Darkness, it's almost like the games trying to say &quot;Being a Genius means that nothing I do will ever matter.&quot; That...that...whaaaat?!? Please someone tell me I'm not understanding this correctly...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, I've never been fond of the literal &quot;Nothing a Genius Does Matters&quot;. It doesn't hold true in setting, and doesn't hold true in play. You Aren't Going To Change The World On Your Own is more fitting, I feel. Genii <i>can</i> make a difference, but they must do so as a group, or focus on the small scale. Scaled up, without any kind of external correction, and their own flaws sabotage whatever grand scheme they try to implement. You'll never <i>cure Cancer</i>, but you can cure <i>some people's</i> Cancer. You'll never <i>solve criminality</i>, but you can bring some criminals to justice. You'll never develop a <i>Grand Unifying Theory</i>, but you can see how some things inter-relate.<br /> <br /> Inspiration promises the Genius grand triumphs, but part of learning to live as an Inspired is finding out that small victories are still victories and have meaning all on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:43:21-08:00","id":999233,"title":"","content":"A theme of Genius is &quot;failure/frustration&quot;.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a theme of Vampire is &quot;hunger/bloodlust&quot;. That doesn't mean it's <i>impossible </i>to resist your hunger for blood. It means there's a constant struggle with it.<br /> <br /> Genius is a game about dealing with human limitations, in much the same way Mage is about dealing with power corruption, and Vampire is about addiction and desire, and Geist is about dealing with death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:52:14-08:00","id":999273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999168#post999168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> See, I've never been fond of the literal &quot;Nothing a Genius Does Matters&quot;. It doesn't hold true in setting, and doesn't hold true in play. You Aren't Going To Change The World On Your Own is more fitting, I feel. Genii <i>can</i> make a difference, but they must do so as a group, or focus on the small scale. Scaled up, without any kind of external correction, and their own flaws sabotage whatever grand scheme they try to implement. You'll never <i>cure Cancer</i>, but you can cure <i>some people's</i> Cancer. You'll never <i>solve criminality</i>, but you can bring some criminals to justice. You'll never develop a <i>Grand Unifying Theory</i>, but you can see how some things inter-relate.<br /> <br /> Inspiration promises the Genius grand triumphs, but part of learning to live as an Inspired is finding out that small victories are still victories and have meaning all on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would help if the game didn't make such a point of it.<br /> <br /> Yes, I imagine in play you can do a lot of things, but because of the way the books sells it, it feels like it's done in spite of the game instead of in the spirit of the game. I'm all for a game of succeeding at the small things but not winning the large things.<br /> <br /> As is, Genius reads out like there is no point to even playing the game because it's fatalism reads so heavy. It doesn't help when Genius's fanbase, particularly it's pre-eminent voices, tell you that that's the point and we're supposed to invest in a game that says you'll never do anything worthwhile again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:46:44-08:00","id":999353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999168#post999168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I've never been fond of the literal &quot;Nothing a Genius Does Matters&quot;. It doesn't hold true in setting, and doesn't hold true in play. You Aren't Going To Change The World On Your Own</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think you're disagreeing with Genius (or me). It's just different wording to express the same concept.<br /> <br /> To use your example &quot;You'll never <i>cure Cancer</i>, but you can cure <i>some people's</i> Cancer.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would say that a Genius who realises that and gives up on a quest for the cure for cancer to instead cure people one by one with Exelixi is a Genius who's won the game. They're the equivilent of a Vampire who's found a way to stay stable at humanity 8+ (and cut ties with the poisonous vampire society).<br /> <br /> I have previously used The Doctor and Morty from Rick and Morty as examples of charachters in a Genius story who've figured this out. (Morty is not a Genius, which is probably why he figured it out so easily. Ghouls are better at retaining Humanity than Vampires).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999273#post999273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't help when Genius's fanbase, particularly it's pre-eminent voices, tell you that that's the point and we're supposed to invest in a game that says you'll never do anything worthwhile again.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* Vampire and Beast tell you that you're supposed to be an abuser. I can get invested in a game about fatalism but not one where I play an abuser. Not every game is for everyone. Not every game needs to be for everyone. Genius is for me, Vampire isn't.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:25:47-08:00","id":999370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998612#post998612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A game about magic users has enough space for prophets and physicists. To say a game about mad scientists can model prophets as well as physicists sounds off.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A game about wizards has enough space for physicists&quot; <i>doesn't </i>sound odd to you? Do you think physicists are a type of wizard?<br /> <br /> You can't play mad scientists in [new] Mage.<br /> <br /> You <i>can </i>play wizards who are also scientists. But the two don't tie into each other - if you can levitate anything, but consciously choose only to levitate your flying car, you're <i>not a mad scientist</i> - you're a really thick wizard who's obsessed with cars. In practice, nobody is dumb enough to do that; you get the occasional person who has a flying car <i>and also</i> can levitate stuff with their mind, and that's about it.<br /> <br /> In Genius, on the other hand, you can personally enhance yourself so you have the ability to levitate stuff with your mind. <i>Or </i>you can enhance yourself to have superhuman strength, or you can not enhance yourself at all, and instead build a flying car.<br /> <br /> You don't have to build a character who can levitate stuff with their mind <i>and</i> has a flying car, then deliberately hide the flying car in your garage and deny it's existence.<br /> <br /> That's not to say Genius is <i>better</i> at doing mages than Mage is, any more than Changeling is better at doing vampires just because you could theoretically play a Changeling whose durance was spent in an old castle with Edward, and who returned with the ability to suck the life out of people, and who has a Frailty that means they can't touch garlic.<br /> <br /> Changeling isn't a copy of Vampire; vampires happen to fall under the purview of &quot;fairytale creatures&quot;.<br /> <br /> Similarly, prophets are a small sub-category of Genius' thing, and an unusual one at that, so most players go for one of the bajilion other character ideas &quot;mad genius&quot; can include. Like physicists, or mathematicians, or biologists, or...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=997984#post997984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big things overlooked with Genius was why mad scientists were folded in with Mages to begin with-that it's a surprisingly limited view that really just echoes the larger realm that mages were for a much longer period of time. It needed fleshing out and expanding, and Genius really didn't do that in any sense of the concept. Mad scientists was already a narrower niche than a whole splat needed to be (and that's keeping in mind that in fan-splats we're talking about contenders that includes <i>just </i>dragons, magical girls, and things of the like), but then it goes on to shoot itself in the foot over and over again by refusing to deepen itself out. Whether the answer was applying artistry and other things into it or branching outward with it's theme of mad science to make it so it could apply to any character concept, Genius just didn't care and opted for this half-assed middle ground that doesn't amount to anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998612#post998612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's weaker, it looses strength as it becomes spread out too thin. Our suspension of disbelief wavers, our investment in the icon that is trying to be sold here decreases.<br /> <br /> Genius was always going to be a limited game in one of two ways-it could either broaden up and be a game about visionaries, artists, sociologists, etc, or it could really dig into it's area of science, at the cost of everything else.<br /> <br /> Genius tells me it's about Mad Scientists, so I assume it thinks it chose the latter. It performed it poorly, and the fact that people keep telling me this is a game about visionaries tells me it didn't commit to that choice.<br /> <br /> If you want a game about visionaries, <i>make that game</i>. And yeah, good fucking luck not making it Another Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like you've decided to hate Genius no matter what it does. If it includes lots of different types of mad genius, it's &quot;spread out too thin&quot; and trying to be &quot;another mage&quot;, and it needs to &quot;commit&quot;. If it <i>doesn't </i>include those options, as you apparently assumed, that proves that it's inherently &quot;limited&quot; and &quot;cliche&quot; and needs to &quot;broaden up&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is it?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999353#post999353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that a Genius who realises that and gives up on a quest for the cure for cancer to instead cure people one by one with Exelixi is a Genius who's won the game. They're the equivilent of a Vampire who's found a way to stay stable at humanity 8+ (and cut ties with the poisonous vampire society).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, I always tended to see the Genius who manages to build a giant gonzo cancer-curing ray powered by fifteen Generators and blast the whole city with cancer cure as having &quot;won the game&quot;.<br /> <br /> But then, I always saw the Ordo Dracul as the most relatable vampire faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 11-06-2016, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:07:35-08:00","id":999419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999370#post999370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny, I always tended to see the Genius who manages to build a giant gonzo cancer-curing ray powered by fifteen Generators and blast the whole city with cancer cure as having &amp;quot;won the game&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> But then, I always saw the Ordo Dracul as the most relatable vampire faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you are blasting a whole city, many of whom do not have cancer with your Anti-Cancer Rays (patent pending), and expecting *no* side effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:11:49-08:00","id":999422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998651#post998651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. This is factually wrong. Genius tells you it's about visionaries in the introduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it does a shitty job upholding that as a splat. Mainly, because their inspiration doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 11-06-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:18:37-08:00","id":999426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999419#post999419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you are blasting a whole city, many of whom do not have cancer with your Anti-Cancer Rays (patent pending), and expecting *no* side effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly he double bound Mania to remove it's fault <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally if I were ST I would let that be a Genius' win if they had enough charachter development to earn it, or if we were playing a non-horrific gonzo game (lets be honest. What WoD game isn't occasionally played as horrror free gonzo?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:12:43-08:00","id":999453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999370#post999370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <i>can </i>play wizards who are also scientists. But the two don't tie into each other - if you can levitate anything, but consciously choose only to levitate your flying car, you're <i>not a mad scientist</i> - you're a really thick wizard who's obsessed with cars. In practice, nobody is dumb enough to do that; you get the occasional person who has a flying car <i>and also</i> can levitate stuff with their mind, and that's about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are here describing the exact problem with Genius's use of Aesthetics and also conflating &quot;doesn't use their powers for everything they could conceivably be used for&quot; with &quot;is really thick.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:37:23-08:00","id":999491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999370#post999370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A game about wizards has enough space for physicists&quot; <i>doesn't </i>sound odd to you? Do you think physicists are a type of wizard?<br /> <br /> It sounds like you've decided to hate Genius no matter what it does. If it includes lots of different types of mad genius, it's &quot;spread out too thin&quot; and trying to be &quot;another mage&quot;, and it needs to &quot;commit&quot;. If it <i>doesn't </i>include those options, as you apparently assumed, that proves that it's inherently &quot;limited&quot; and &quot;cliche&quot; and needs to &quot;broaden up&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Genius basically does treat its physicists as wizards. The PCs are basically capable of performing supernatural effects through their technology.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but I think that ArcaneArts is saying isn't inconsistent but rather describing the rock and hard place that they are saying Genius is between. The argument, unless I'm wrong, goes something like this: If Genius is about people whose superpseudoscience can do a variety of effects under wide but vaguely defined penumbras, then those mechanics are comparable to Mage, and thus the game itself invites comparison to Mage. If Genius is claiming to be about visionaries, then it needs mechanics on &quot;how to be visionary&quot; in a wide variety of ways, but the game proper has only being visionary through superscience. If Genius were try to focus solely on &quot;Things Science can do, but better,&quot; then there's the unanswered question of whether there's enough content there to do a full splat.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I agree completely, but I admit to seeing major similarities between Axioms and Arcanum, and between Wonder Creation and Creative Thamaturgy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999273#post999273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would help if the game didn't make such a point of it.<br /> <br /> Yes, I imagine in play you can do a lot of things, but because of the way the books sells it, it feels like it's done in spite of the game instead of in the spirit of the game. I'm all for a game of succeeding at the small things but not winning the large things.<br /> <br /> As is, Genius reads out like there is no point to even playing the game because it's fatalism reads so heavy. It doesn't help when Genius's fanbase, particularly it's pre-eminent voices, tell you that that's the point and we're supposed to invest in a game that says you'll never do anything worthwhile again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit the stories are more fatalistic then the gameplay and gameplay suggesstions want to be. What particularly interests me is how the CofD rules could make this more interesting in terms of roleplay and player advancement.<br /> <br /> There are two areas where Genius explicitly builds failure points into the system. One is the Resources Merit, which is needed to build Wonders without penalty. Genius makes these Resources an explicit weak point, providing suggestions as to how the plot can temporarily block access to these dots, which is ripe for a Condition as a source of Beats, or take them away permanently - Sanctity of Merits could do much to turn this potential turn-off into a way to create more diverse character development.<br /> <br /> The other is the fault system, where Wonders gain random flaws. (I was going to say this could be another Beat source, but I'm probably not looking hard enough for a good solution to that...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8064,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","user":"mp122984","date":". 11-06-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:43:25-08:00","id":999494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999422#post999422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then it does a shitty job upholding that as a splat. Mainly, because their inspiration doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also because the rest of book talks about mad scientists. I was just reading it yesterday, and I read mad scientist a whole damn lot and visionsary only, funnily enough, in reference to the Catalyst of Vision.<br /> <br /> No, this game is not about visionaries. This has, for six years now, been a game about mad scientists. both in the writing and in the advertising. No one ever called it a game about visionaries, until a really strong argument emerged that Genius sucked at being a game of mad science. Hell, in the most recent case(Mine, I think), the argument for it being about visionaries didn't come up at all in between the time I put up the intro and the time I put up the first half of chapter one. I made it clear I was approaching Genius as a game about mad scientists, and no one corrected me-until I said this game sucked at being a game about mad scientists.<br /> <br /> People are backpedaling, and the place they are retreating to just makes Genius look worse and worse.<br /> <br /> And yeah Mug, I see you, I'll get to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T18:28:55-08:00","id":999516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999370#post999370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A game about wizards has enough space for physicists&quot; <i>doesn't </i>sound odd to you? Do you think physicists are a type of wizard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing about having been a history education major before becoming an english major-I tend to look at history in terms of how that endless waltz is executed, particularly in the broad strokes and the archetypes.<br /> <br /> The scientist fills in for the witch at the edge of the woods, with her knowledge of herbs and weather patterns, her baleful distrust of the elders and her wisdom reaching far ahead. The scientist fills in for the priest, his invocations telling the populace how the world is, his miracles pushing forth the promises of the gods. Likewise, the mad scientist, with his radiation and anthrax and mind-control radio waves, is nothing more than the witch with blood sacrifices and poisons, the priest who evokes the gods who stand for the end of civilization.<br /> <br /> And funnily enough, when you look at history with that abstract expressionist/cubist lens, yes, the myth of the Mad Scientist is a <span style=\"font-size:10px\">blip </span>in comparison to the Human Who Masters The World Beyond The Kenning of Peers-particularly when you look at in the view of the Chronicles of Darkness where the supernatural and ancient are more predominant that mundane modernity.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. That sounds <i>fine</i> to me. And yes, Physicists are just the new wizards.We have not buried the old religions, we have merely changed their shape. The endless waltz continues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't play mad scientists in [new] Mage. </div> </div> </div>Okay. Cool. Awakening was not about playing mad scientists. It never was, never will be. It aims archetypally, recognizing that icons are just vehicles for meaning, and so translates the symbol of the mad scientists, iconographically, into what it always was-that of the wizard. So I don't care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You <i>can </i>play wizards who are also scientists. But the two don't tie into each other - if you can levitate anything, but consciously choose only to levitate your flying car, you're <i>not a mad scientist</i> - you're a really thick wizard who's obsessed with cars. In practice, nobody is dumb enough to do that; you get the occasional person who has a flying car <i>and also</i> can levitate stuff with their mind, and that's about it. </div> </div> </div>Maybe he just has a thing for lifting cars with his mind.<br /> <br /> Jokes aside. So Science, the flying car, the german with the foot fetish, they are all symbols that the mage exploits for the Truths they carry or can be used to translate. The mage recognizes there is a difference between message and messenger. If he cares a lot about the image of mad science, then he can do that, but it's power comes from the way he uses it-the meaning that was buried in there or has emerged from it, depending on which sect you listen to. The mad science he wears is but the image by which it's larger truths are seen.<br /> <br /> Is there a problem here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Genius, on the other hand, you can personally enhance yourself so you have the ability to levitate stuff with your mind. <i>Or </i>you can enhance yourself to have superhuman strength, or you can not enhance yourself at all, and instead build a flying car. </div> </div> </div> With Havoc, one has to wonder why a Genius would internalize it any of their inventions. It's practically begging to become Springlock. At least when a Mage does it, you don't have bits of tech or biology wrecking merry hell with your body-well, except Paradox.<br /> <br /> Sorry, distracted, anyways!<br /> <br /> Or you could do all those things, and then you're a guy who can lift things with his mind who also has a flying car and wow circles.<br /> <br /> Got distracted again, ANYWAYS.<br /> <br /> ...actually, I have no idea where this point of the argument is going.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't have to build a character who can levitate stuff with their mind <i>and</i> has a flying car, then deliberately hide the flying car in your garage and deny it's existence. </div> </div> </div>Well, actually, you do, because if people find out you have a flying car, they're gonna wanna touch it, and then you're not going to have a flying car and people are going to think you're a rank liar. Also, if they touch you, you'll probably end up lobotomizing yourself. Because Havoc.<br /> <br /> Look, I know it can't work like that, but Genius Chapter 1 really wanted me to believe there was zero public use of Wonders at all. I'm just listening to that Chapter.<br /> <br /> But seriously, so you're saying it can go the other way, which I could actually make an argument for, even though the cultural weight of these things don't work that way-still, yeah, it could from an objective stand point go the other way, sans the interaction of cultural/ historical archetypal weight.<br /> <br /> But, uh, a) I'm not going to go sans that, and b), This is the Chronicles of Darkness, so even if I wanted to, it's delineation of priority is clear-Witch trumps Mad Scientist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not to say Genius is <i>better</i> at doing mages than Mage is, any more than Changeling is better at doing vampires just because you could theoretically play a Changeling whose durance was spent in an old castle with Edward, and who returned with the ability to suck the life out of people, and who has a Frailty that means they can't touch garlic.<br /> <br /> Changeling isn't a copy of Vampire; vampires happen to fall under the purview of &quot;fairytale creatures&quot;. </div> </div> </div>1) Well, funnily enough.<br /> <br /> But no, we'll set that aside, actually.<br /> <br /> 2) This is not an indecent argument. Now if only Genius would do what Vampire did to make itself not a Changeling spin off* and actually give a damn enough to at least try make a bigger deal of it's points that aren't shared with Mage. Namely by digging deeper into the themes, icons, trends, etc. that have emerged from the mad scientist specifically. This has always been my main argument, that it doesn't do that enough. If it can't do that, for unfathomable reasons, then it needs to extend outward and play it smart with how it extends by drawing other things falls under Genius rather than mad scientists, and do it all in a way that makes it distinct from Mage. That's a losing game, but theoretically it can be played.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, prophets are a small sub-category of Genius' thing, and an unusual one at that, so most players go for one of the bajilion other character ideas &quot;mad genius&quot; can include. Like physicists, or mathematicians, or biologists, or... </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm liking option two less and less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It sounds like you've decided to hate Genius no matter what it does. </div> </div> </div>I have read one chapter and the introduction. I have liked the X-Splat's idea and nothing else. I have four other chapters to read. Opinions might change, but go figure at this point I am very negative about it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Eh, I don't need the rest of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it includes lots of different types of mad genius, it's &quot;spread out too thin&quot; and trying to be &quot;another mage&quot;, and it needs to &quot;commit&quot;. If it <i>doesn't </i>include those options, as you apparently assumed, that proves that it's inherently &quot;limited&quot; and &quot;cliche&quot; and needs to &quot;broaden up&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is it? </div> </div> </div>I admit, I've been playing a faulty game.<br /> <br /> Truthfully, Genius is untenable by going on the 'visionary'/artist route, because it will eventually crash into that Mage problem time and time again-and ironically, It will also crash the fuck into Mummy, sooner or later.<br /> <br /> Realistically, what I think Ge-no, not Genius, mad scientists-what I think Mad Scientists should be is a minor template or Hunter Conspiracy, a collection of merits that offers possibilities within the confines that best fit mad scientists in the ChroD game. It should really surrender this notion of cosmic affecting/traversing shit-or at the very least, the entire thing needs to be treated on a smaller level for what is there to really magnify. If we have to play mad scientists as a major template, then dig really fucking deep into the archetype and what has emerged from it since it's inception, work on making it more and more distinct and more more solidly mad scientist, while spreading the skirt and exploring what that means without crossing the lines back into the Mages. Fuck, that's what should be done even if you went the &quot;collection of merits&quot; route.<br /> <br /> This is why the visionary argument is bullshit, because it's a way to justify Genius as is, but in such a way that it's even more superficial and superfluous, makes it seem more pathetically like a Mage ripoff. Even if you wanted to go the artists/sociologists/etc., Genius'd have to play that card very carefully, and honestly it's succeed more by downsizing the reach of the character if it wanted to go that way.<br /> <br /> My main point is that, while I don't agree with this idea that the visionary/artist route is the way to agree, I <i>do</i> agree with the feeling at the core of it-that Genius is anemic, that it lacks substance of it it's own, that it has no meat worth investing in. The heart of the argument is that Genius is <i>lacking</i>, and that's fundamentally true. I'll entertain the messenger, the visionary/artist route, because it carries that message.<br /> <br /> Also it's one of those &quot;Try to be open minded&quot; things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-06-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:34:12-08:00","id":999651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999491#post999491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I agree completely, but I admit to seeing major similarities between Axioms and Arcanum, and between Wonder Creation and Creative Thamaturgy.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are similarities - thats pretty inevitable since the WoD does mechanics in fairly broad strokes.<br /> <br /> I'd say the key difference between them is how much a charachter can do when their devices are removed. In Awakening Mage who looses is staff has a small disadvantage, but if he still has full access to his Arcana. In Genius a charachter who looses his jetpack cannot fly at all until he reclaims it or a replacement.<br /> <br /> This means that Awakening would find it rather hard to mimic the very common plot line where a mad scientist or a science hero's devices are taken away and they have to solve the challenge without them.<br /> <br /> But fair's fair. Genius has it's limitations for charachters who fit the themes but are not device builders too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still. I don't think it really matters that much how different or similar Axioms and Arcana are. The thematic differences between the two games are what matters. As I said above origonal Doctor Frankenstein was an alchemist and Mary Shelly drew on Shakespear's Prospero when writing him. Mages and mad scientists have a lot in common so there will of course be plenty of overlap in both directions: Both games are about people who live and think apart from regular society and weild strange powers normal society cannot touch.<br /> <br /> But Mage is about how that power corrupts*. Genius is about how that power** (and all other power) is ultimately an illusion. That's the difference, all else is elaboration.<br /> <br /> * Especially in 1E where it was stated as the theme in the introduction.<br /> <br /> ** I use the word power, but it might be more accurate to call it &quot;control&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999494#post999494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has, for six years now, been a game about mad scientists. both in the writing and in the advertising. No one ever called it a game about visionaries, until a really strong argument emerged that Genius sucked at being a game of mad science.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is factually untrue.<br /> <br /> I might not have used the actual word &quot;visionaries&quot;, but I have been using examples like Karl Marx and feminists (e.g. visionaries who are not mad scientists in any traditonal sense) as real life examples of Genius' themes since long before your thread. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod/page4\">Here's one example.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T09:34:12-08:00","id":999787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999651#post999651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is factually untrue.<br /> <br /> I might not have used the actual word &quot;visionaries&quot;, but I have been using examples like Karl Marx and feminists (e.g. visionaries who are not mad scientists in any traditonal sense) as real life examples of Genius' themes since long before your thread. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/265914-what-is-your-favorite-fan-splat-for-nwod/page4\">Here's one example.</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, are you the author?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T09:47:25-08:00","id":999790,"title":"","content":"He penned a small part of it. There's a reason he's invested.<br /> <br /> And Raven, the occasional use of visionaries does not change the number of times you have made it abundantly clear that Genius is about Mad Scientists because you were, at one point, so bad about bringing up Genius that Dave Brookshaw made fun of you for it. You were like a less hostile Gecko. I know, I was there. When I talk about pushy Genius fans, I'm talking about a whole host of people, but you are right at the top of that list, and you have made it <i>crystal clear time and again</i> that Genius was about mad scientists-except for when someone calls the game out on it.<br /> <br /> And even if, for some reason, I pretend that you actually did make a clear case for Genius as visionaries, I am reading the book <i>right now</i>. This game is about mad scientists. It's telling me this all over the place.<br /> <br /> You wanna live in denial, fine, but don't try and sell the bullshit here. No one's buying who hasn't already bought it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-07-2016, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:06:18-08:00","id":999792,"title":"","content":"Hey, leave me out of this. I make fun of a lot of people. Including you, a lot more recently than KR's bad phase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:08:40-08:00","id":999793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999792#post999792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, leave me out of this. I make fun of a lot of people. Including you, a lot more recently than KR's bad phase.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Didn't need to bring you in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-07-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:04:45-08:00","id":999821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999790#post999790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the number of times you have made it abundantly clear that Genius is about Mad Scientists</div> </div> </div> </div> You're going to have to cite some sources for this assertion, because the only thing I can think of myself saying anything that implies that Genius is about Mad Scientists is in threads along the lines of &quot;who would x be in the WoD&quot;. And for those<br /> <br /> 1) Most mad scientists are visionaries anyway.<br /> 2) Even when a non-WoD mad scientist's story has different themes to Genius one can still think Genius works for it. Just like how Mage 2E uses Dresden Files as inspirational media despite vastly different themes. (At least that's my interpretation of Dresden Files. From a purely thematic perspective, I'd make Harry a Changeling)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:10:06-08:00","id":999936,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mad scientist&quot; is mentioned 168 times in the PDF. I looked through the first 20 mentions. 15 of those use the term mad scientist as a synonym for Genius. One of them is even in a heading. The language of the game is completely based around playing a mad scientist.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that the post about Karl Marx uses him as an analogue to the tragedy of a Genius, not as an actual example of what a Genius might be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:41:06-08:00","id":999956,"title":"","content":"Nitpick - Chronicle of Darkness games are Urban Fantasy as well as Horror. They take place in urban settings (possible exception of werewolf). They include the supernatural as setting elements. That's all it takes to be part of the Urban Fantasy genre. <br /> <br /> As for the rest of the thread.... Can't everyone agree to disagree? This is an old argument where no one is going to change minds. Genius has its fans, and they like it. As long as those fans don't go into every other thread and brag about how great the game is for being about Mad Scientists (and that was an issue for a while, but that's a different matter), does it matter? If its fun for them, and its not offensive to real world cultures, then the game is Doing It Right. <br /> <br /> I seem to remember bits from Arcane's review about some rather racist/sexist statistics and I say it should be exicsed; any amount of that kind of attitude is poison, and games should instead strive to have minority representives by design. But is that kind of thought process throughout the entire game? Is it baked in on a fundamental level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:17:09-08:00","id":999971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999956#post999956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to remember bits from Arcane's review about some rather racist/sexist statistics and I say it should be exicsed; any amount of that kind of attitude is poison, and games should instead strive to have minority representives by design. But is that kind of thought process throughout the entire game? Is it baked in on a fundamental level?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the historical and statistics part: basically, Inspired society mirrored the dominant cultural mores (and of those, predominantly Western European) of the time - hence, for much of recent history, was sexist and racist. The Peerage was nominally more progressive, but only by a bit.<br /> <br /> Setting/Organization wise, there is also the bit where the conflict between the Peerage vs Lemuria is pretty much only as listed in the Western Hemisphere. The Eastern (at least, India and China) are firmly under the control of Lemuria (baring the sole near-Foundation level Ten Thousand Fans). Take that as you will.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the mechanics factors in race, sex, etc. Though since Genii are more dependent upon funding and supplies than most other splats, you might be able to infer local inequality affecting Genii (Glass Ceiling, Profiling, Unequal Opportunity, etc.). That isn't listed, though, so is really up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-07-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:25:47-08:00","id":999978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999971#post999971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in the historical and statistics part: basically, Inspired society mirrored the dominant cultural mores (and of those, predominantly Western European) of the time - hence, for much of recent history, was sexist and racist. The Peerage was nominally more progressive, but only by a bit.<br /> <br /> Setting/Organization wise, there is also the bit where the conflict between the Peerage vs Lemuria is pretty much only as listed in the Western Hemisphere. The Eastern (at least, India and China) are firmly under the control of Lemuria (baring the sole near-Foundation level Ten Thousand Fans). Take that as you will.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the mechanics factors in race, sex, etc. Though since Genii are more dependent upon funding and supplies than most other splats, you might be able to infer local inequality affecting Genii (Glass Ceiling, Profiling, Unequal Opportunity, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, those statistics do really bug me.<br /> <br /> And <i>holy shit</i>, I'd totally forgotten about the &quot;Lemuria controls a bunch of Asia&quot; thing. That's racist as hell. Like, so much so that I'm surprised I didn't remember that, but I'm looking at it and holy shit, there it is. That's definitely gotta go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:45:36-08:00","id":999994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999978#post999978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, those statistics do really bug me.<br /> <br /> And <i>holy shit</i>, I'd totally forgotten about the &quot;Lemuria controls a bunch of Asia&quot; thing. That's racist as hell. Like, so much so that I'm surprised I didn't remember that, but I'm looking at it and holy shit, there it is. That's definitely gotta go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I always ignored that part as old history, if I even cared to include it. It lends itself to &quot;plucky rebels&quot; stories, but that's about it, and dropping it over <i>at least 2/3rds of the world's population</i>, seemed a bit dumb (if not exclusionary and racist). If needed, I see no reason it couldn't be confined to one small region (or even time, considering Time Travel is on the table).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:59:26-08:00","id":1000002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999790#post999790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Raven, the occasional use of visionaries does not change the number of times you have made it abundantly clear that Genius is about Mad Scientists</div> </div> </div> </div>You're moving the goal posts. You said I came up with the concept of visonaries as a response to you, I demonstrated that in fact the concept of visionaries predates your review by years.<br /> <br /> That's the end of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999936#post999936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also point out that the post about Karl Marx uses him as an analogue to the tragedy of a Genius, not as an actual example of what a Genius might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=819818#post819818\">Karl Marx is an example of the Genius who tries to save the world</a>&quot; - me, most of a year before Arc started a review.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999956#post999956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rest of the thread.... Can't everyone agree to disagree?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean ignore the fact that those fools in the institute laughed at my theories? Get on with my life instead of wasting it on impractical schemes of revenge?<br /> <br /> My good sir, just whom do you think you're talking to?!<br /> <br /> (Sorry, I couldn't resist such an obvious opening)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999956#post999956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is that kind of thought process throughout the entire game? Is it baked in on a fundamental level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without knowing what exactly you mean by &quot;that kind of thought process&quot; I cannot answer that question.<br /> <br /> I can say that Genius has diverse sample characters.<br /> <br /> Racism does exist in the setting: Historical Geniuses are stated to have shared the attitudes of the time they live in, but this is wholly condemned by the text. The only sizeable modern group of Geniuses who still admit to racism are the Nazis, who're Nazis and pretty much shoot on sight antagonists.<br /> <br /> The statistics section you're talking about doesn't mention race at all. It mostly talks about educational backgrounds, and when it comes to gender it says Geniuses are more gender balanced than not and the remaining gender gap is vanishing.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if that's what you want to see or exactly what you hate seeing. Personally I think white washing history and the real world is worse than acknowledging the ugly parts of history.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:00:05-08:00","id":1000003,"title":"","content":"I mean, if we really needed a place controlled by Lemuria, it should have been made a Bardo, or a possible Bad Future. Not a huge swath of the present-day planet where actual people live now and have a whole bunch of differing points of view.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, the idea of Asian Genii being almost entirely part of a group that has turned its back on huge chunks of modern science is pretty laughable considering how huge electronics and other necessarily modern industries are there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T17:07:49-08:00","id":1000027,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000002#post1000002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=819818#post819818\">Karl Marx is an example of the Genius who tries to save the world</a>&quot; - me, most of a year before Arc started a review.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is that accurately presented in the work itself? I don't think so. It looks like you're retroactively covering your ass.<br /> <br /> Nevermind the poor choice in a theme such as &quot;accepting one's impotence&quot; in a medium such as an RPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000002#post1000002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can say that Genius has diverse sample characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who seem to be, practically, all mad scientists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999936#post999936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Mad scientist&quot; is mentioned 168 times in the PDF. I looked through the first 20 mentions. 15 of those use the term mad scientist as a synonym for Genius. One of them is even in a heading. The language of the game is completely based around playing a mad scientist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T17:59:55-08:00","id":1000058,"title":"","content":"Also, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/moochava/genius\" target=\"_blank\">from the place where you grab the pdf's</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Genius: The Transgression is a fan-made role-playing game for the New World of Darkness. In it, players take on the roles of mad scientists and wonder-workers, driven to the brink of insanity by the secrets they have uncovered. Version 1.1 of the rules is available for free download as a .pdf file. </div> </div> </div>Just saying.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, from the Select Concept section of Chapter Two:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the beginning of the chronicle, most geniuses in the collaborative will be new to the whole &quot;mad science&quot; thing, with at most a few months of experience on the job. </div> </div> </div>Also, from a little earlier:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> New geniuses begin play with a few Axioms and a handful of wonders, but they are not super-scientists; not yet. </div> </div> </div>Just saying. I could go on.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also in the Select Concept section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You should also consider an aesthetic, what your mad scientist's inventions will look like. </div> </div> </div>This is getting fun.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mental Skills are often primary, but which Skills receive the most attention can tell a person much about a mad scientist. </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geniuses often focus on strange and seemingly-useless specializations that are too narrow to be useful anywhere except mad science. </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The foundation is a considered choice, based on how the genius approaches mad science. </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Also,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geniuses who have flirted previously with mad science may begin the chronicle with two or three dots of Inspiration. </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Also,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A genius builds wonders based on Axioms, which are the branches of mad science. </div> </div> </div>We're still in the first four pages of Chapter 2.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This may reflect some sin committed before the Breakthrough, but more likely represents a grave transgression that the genius committed in her first days as a mad scientist. </div> </div> </div>Urge to quote Sans rising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-07-2016, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:41:45-08:00","id":1000071,"title":"","content":"Is there an actual point to any of that? Because a game about playing the modern concept of &quot;mad scientist/evil genius&quot; listing &quot;mad science&quot; alot isn't at all surprising.<br /> <br /> Nor, as I am sure will be pointed out, does &quot;mad scientist&quot; preclude any precursor concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:43:29-08:00","id":1000072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000071#post1000071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an actual point to any of that? Because a game about playing the modern concept of &quot;mad scientist/evil genius&quot; listing &quot;mad science&quot; alot isn't at all surprising.<br /> <br /> Nor, as I am sure will be pointed out, does &quot;mad scientist&quot; preclude any precursor concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making the point.<br /> <br /> Also childish amusement.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, none of that is also counting the other language that paints a clear picture without pointing out directly that what Geniuses do is mad science.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-07-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:49:07-08:00","id":1000076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000072#post1000072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making the point.<br /> <br /> Also childish amusement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Carry on then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T19:28:36-08:00","id":1000092,"title":"","content":"I think I need to re-evaluate my original opinion of Genius: the Transgression. It been a loooong couple of days since I first discovered Genius and was drawn in by the cool ideas it presented. That was before the cracks began to show, it was a more innocent time back then. And yet even then there was one thing about Genius that made me worry, and as I delved deeper into that abyss it only grew and grew until now what few bright points I could say about Genius have been all but drowned out. And that is such a shame, because I still believe Genius could be a good game. It won't, but it could. So....in a manner of speaking I truly did get to experience the core premise of Genius. Discovering a whole new vista of reality, only to be crushed and broken on the ground like Icarus because that vision of a better Genius will never come to pass. But more on that soon, first I need to cut the melodrama and give some credit where credit is due.<br /> <br /> To all those who have posted so far. Those who have provided their own critiques about Genius, those who provided engaging counter arguments in favor of Genius, those who provided insight and corrections to above mentioned critiques and counter arguments. I thank you all. If it wasn't for this dialogue I fear that my time spent thinking about Genius and how it could be better would have been completely wasted. Right, let's get to the heart of this one last time. <br /> <br /> I mentioned in my original post that Genius is one of the most stifling games I've ever seen. I original though this was because it clung to stubbornly to the trappings of Mad Science, until it was later pointed out in a counter argument that the rules themselves lend for a lot of wiggle room. My fears were abated for a time, but that stifling feeling never really went away. After exploring more and more nitpicks of mine in an attempt to reach the root of this frustrating feeling I had I ran across a part of the source material I hadn't read before. This is when I fully understood why Genius felt so stifling and frustrating. Genius the Transgression has a constant subtext that's reinforced in all of it's terminology, mechanics, aesthetic, themes, and writing. And it's no more apparent (besides maybe the infamous &quot;No one's in charge&quot; section that I foolishly gave the benefit of the doubt too) than in the section about the Clockstoppers, Genius the Transgression's version of the Autumn People from Changeling the Dreaming...oh how foolish I've been. <br /> <br /> Genius isn't trying to be Mage the Ascension, Genius is trying to be Changeling the Dreaming. Or more specifically: Genius suffers from a subtext of pride &amp; pretension.<br /> <br /> Now to be fair, Changeling the Dreaming learned from it's subtext and greatly improved from it's 1st Edition roots (With the exception of the Autumn People, but that was their Time of Judgment phase so they're optional.) But Genius has yet to do so, there is still an unearthly level of pretension surrounding being a Genius and how their culture views the world. Mania (creativity energy) exists in all humans, but only academia generate enough of it for Genii to draw upon via &quot;science talk.&quot; Regular humans disrupt Mania in a Genius' inventions and forces the poor misunderstood souls to hide that part of their life from anyone outside of the Genii community. Both good and bad Genii truly believe that humans can't lead themselves without being guided by one or more of the Genii, even the insane yet still superior somehow Lemurians. When foolish non-Genii make astounding discoveries about reality it literally creates contradiction paradoxes that not only invalidate the discovery but normally go about trying to destroy the world unless the beneficent Genii step in to save them. The horror of the game is supposed to come from the Genii realizing that their own superior intellect is the most horrifying thing in the world because it will either inevitably drive them tragically mad or the universe will never appreciate their genius and ensure every miraculous super-device they will into being is crushed by the mundane plebeians or their own extraordinary hubris. And of course, the greatest danger to a Genii outside of themselves and the chaotic universe where there is no meaning without their own brilliance, is the Clockstoppers: humans who's minds don't have a single creative or original though in their heads who literally suck up and destroy all Mania around them as they seek to make a world without scientific and technological advancement...<br /> <br /> ...*sigh*...<br /> <br /> <br /> Originally I said that I liked Genius the Transgression. Well, that's not the case anymore. And the tragedy of that is that I know the above isn't what the game is trying to be about. Genius wants to be a game about trying to make a difference in a world of darkness, and the struggles of that endless battle. I was shone that by those who love this game, and I want so much for Genius to be that game. But the subtext is there: Genius has nothing but utter contempt for those who don't consider intelligence to be the defining quality of a human being. And that means that all of the author's veiled distain is targeted at people like me. I am not an exceptionally intelligent person, heck I have trouble doing mental math. According to the game Mania doesn't overflow from me, and likely if I touch an invention I'll ruin it for someone who's superior in every way to me. It hurts reading a game like that, it's depressing seeing a world like that. If that is what being a Genius is like then I don't want to play from the perspective of one.<br /> <br /> And that is all I have. Just bitter disappointment and melted wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-07-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T05:47:06-08:00","id":1000237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000002#post1000002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without knowing what exactly you mean by &quot;that kind of thought process&quot; I cannot answer that question.</div> </div> </div> </div> The propagation of harmful stereotypes. Two examples are given above. A third is the focus on centers of higher education, which unduly puts a focus on white males, at certain points in the text, despite that Inspiration should hit everyone equally, irregardless of education. If you're going to quote Jeane d'Arc as an example, then that shit needs to go away.<br /> <br /> There are instances of casual racism and sexism in the game that I don't like. It could simply be the result of simple lack of awareness - subconcious biases can be hard to notice for many unless others point them out from the outside. But it still exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Racism does exist in the setting: Historical Geniuses are stated to have shared the attitudes of the time they live in, but this is wholly condemned by the text. The only sizeable modern group of Geniuses who still admit to racism are the Nazis, who're Nazis and pretty much shoot on sight antagonists. </div> </div> </div> Nazi. It... you know, this is an entirely different conversation for a different time, but I will say this - &quot;At least we're not Nazis!&quot; does not absolve anything. Casual prejudice is a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> doesn't mention race at all. </div> </div> </div> I've been focused on both racism and sexism, but I'm also worried about other prejudices. They're all interconnected.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like I said, I'm not a fan of the game. The only thing I actually care about is about prejudices, and how that affects gamers when we internalize bits of the game and normalize things for ourselves. It creates hostile environments. That does affect everyone, and it is a concern to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-08-2016, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T09:37:27-08:00","id":1000297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000092#post1000092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius wants to be a game about trying to make a difference in a world of darkness, and the struggles of that endless battle. I was shone that by those who love this game, and I want so much for Genius to be that game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The two fan-splats that never really made it past the &quot;neat idea&quot; stage for me were about figuring out what it meant to make a difference: a game about paladins and the religions they championed and the consequences of crusading; and a game about people who personify cities and uphold civilization in doing so. (Don't ask me for details; there are no details.) I'm not sure it ever would have occurred to me that Genius was about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000237#post1000237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nazi. It... you know, this is an entirely different conversation for a different time, but I will say this - &quot;At least we're not Nazis!&quot; does not absolve anything. Casual prejudice is a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to continue the possible-derail, I gotta say I personally find the whole &quot;Nazis are obviously evil&quot; thing to be ... frustrating. It's not that it's offensive, but caricaturing a real-life group of people makes it difficult to actually understand them and that's as true for racial minorities as it is for political fringes. ... (looks at American election) ... &quot;fringes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:04:06-08:00","id":1000340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000092#post1000092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius has nothing but utter contempt for those who don't consider intelligence to be the defining quality of a human being. And that means that all of the author's veiled distain is targeted at people like me. I am not an exceptionally intelligent person, heck I have trouble doing mental math. According to the game Mania doesn't overflow from me, and likely if I touch an invention I'll ruin it for someone who's superior in every way to me. It hurts reading a game like that, it's depressing seeing a world like that. If that is what being a Genius is like then I don't want to play from the perspective of one.<br /> <br /> And that is all I have. Just bitter disappointment and melted wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a change of perspective? If we consider the Game Books as written by the splat in question (or at least determined to paint them as positively as possible), the inherent exclusionary subtext makes sense. What <i>else</i> would a Genius, excluded themselves from the rest of society, and achieving their triumph through the power of their &quot;superior intellect&quot; write?<br /> <br /> Genius doesn't seem more pretentious than Mage's or Mummy's tone, in which poor unAwakened minds corrupt real magic or all other efforts at Relic creation are just aping Irem's one true methods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-08-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:53:04-08:00","id":1000372,"title":"","content":"Except Genius belittles real people for real qualities while both Mage and Mummy belittles for supernatural qualities. And the fact that higher education increases the chance of becoming a Genius implies this view is shared by the actual game, not just its characters.<br /> <br /> Edit 1: Every Sleeper (that is normal person) in Mage is equal from the Mages' perspective. And there's nothing stopping anyone from Awakening. And that keeps players (especially those who already are marginalized by society) interested because they get away from all the toxic behaviour and attitudes they already experience in society. In Dark Eras there's even a sidebar that tells the players that they should ignore the prejudices of the era if they don't find it enjoyable to play. It's a possible angle for drama, but ultimately secondary to the players' enjoyment.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: To know where I'm coming from, I'm one of those who are mostly favoured by the demographics and language used in the book, but I am a target of exclusionary language of other kinds. It's downright painful to read that you're inferior to other people, even if it's worded a whole lot nicer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-08-2016, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T12:34:16-08:00","id":1000380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000372#post1000372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Genius belittles real people for real qualities while both Mage and Mummy belittles for supernatural qualities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fictional people. Also note that the material gives instances of non-academics becoming Inspired.<br /> <br /> Considering certain personality qualities aid/allow one to complete an Awakening (it is possible to turn away from it), Mage also weights personal traits. Mummy is more a presumptuous IP-Law issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000372#post1000372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the fact that higher education increases the chance of becoming a Genius implies this view is shared by the actual game, not just its characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>And an investigative/obsessive personality increases the chance of becoming Awakened. Lack of folklore knowledge and genre-savy increases the chance of becoming a Changeling. So?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000372#post1000372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Sleeper (that is normal person) in Mage is equal from the Mages' perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they aren't. &quot;Destroy the followers of the Lie.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000372#post1000372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's nothing stopping anyone from Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing stops anyone from becoming Inspired.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000372#post1000372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that keeps players (especially those who already are marginalized by society) interested because they get away from all the toxic behaviour and attitudes they already experience in society. In Dark Eras there's even a sidebar that tells the players that they should ignore the prejudices of the era if they don't find it enjoyable to play. It's a possible angle for drama, but ultimately secondary to the players' enjoyment.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can ignore it just as easily here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T12:45:00-08:00","id":1000387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000380#post1000380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering certain personality qualities aid/allow one to complete an Awakening (it is possible to turn away from it), Mage also weights personal traits. Mummy is more a presumptuous IP-Law issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>But those traits aren't tied to socioeconomic status. While there are definitely Inspired who don't come from academic backgrounds, but such Genii are still in the <i>overwhelming</i> majority according to the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No they aren't. &quot;Destroy the followers of the Lie.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Again, that isn't aimed at any social class, though. &quot;followers of the Lie&quot; is a group that you can opt into or out of. You aren't born a servant of the lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you can ignore it just as easily here. </div> </div> </div>Arguably, yes, but it's still kind of worrying that it was included in the first place. Historical prejudices are one thing, but this was something that somebody voluntarily wrote into the setting, probably (hopefully) unaware of how it might turn away a lot of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:02:36-08:00","id":1000394,"title":"","content":"Malonkey <i>gets it</i>.<br /> <br /> So does Tessie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:31:36-08:00","id":1000409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000380#post1000380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they aren't. &quot;Destroy the followers of the Lie.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That, is specifically from the Free Council's Core Beliefs. It literally refers to the Awakened followers of the Exarchs (The Seers of the Throne, in case you were unaware), and is alongside other beliefs like: Democracy seeks the truth, and Humanity is Magical. There could be no other organization farther from the point you were trying to make than the Free Council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-08-2016, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T14:28:01-08:00","id":1000436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000387#post1000387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But those traits aren't tied to socioeconomic status. While there are definitely Inspired who don't come from academic backgrounds, but such Genii are still in the <i>overwhelming</i> majority according to the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>They somewhat are (it's hard to be curious and obsessive about mysteries when you are struggling to survive). And there <i>is</i> something of a thematic self-selection bias.<br /> <br /> And, interestingly enough, Mummies are even more tied to socio-economic status, considering the inherent background. Also a bit of pre-selection bias.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000387#post1000387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, that isn't aimed at any social class, though. &quot;followers of the Lie&quot; is a group that you can opt into or out of. You aren't born a servant of the lie.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000372#post1000372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Sleeper (that is normal person) in Mage is equal from the Mages' perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>My response was directly aimed at &quot;Sleepers are all equal in Mages' eyes.&quot; No, they aren't. Some are seen more favorably, some less so. Some are closer to being Awakened, some are committed to living in the Lie. There is already the class schema for Sleepers &gt; Sleepwalkers &gt; Proximi &gt; Awakened (followed by sub-groupings ranging up to Masters and Archmasters).<br /> <br /> The Guardians of the Veil also slot people into &quot;worthy of allowing to Awaken&quot; and &quot;not worthy - get them lost in a Labyrinth&quot;. Hardly equal.<br /> <br /> All mages might not hold such views. But I think I've established the counter-point that &quot;Sleepers are all equal in Mages' eyes.&quot; is false, due to counter examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000387#post1000387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably, yes, but it's still kind of worrying that it was included in the first place. Historical prejudices are one thing, but this was something that somebody voluntarily wrote into the setting, probably (hopefully) unaware of how it might turn away a lot of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-08-2016, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:19:59-08:00","id":1000457,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>, you cannot seriously believe that curiosity and obsession with the unknown are only inherent in those who aren't bogged down with the everyday struggles of survival? <br /> <br /> All humans have a curiosity for the unknown, and when confronted with the unknown all<br /> humans have the capacity to become obsessed with it's mysteries. This is regardless of class, vocation, ethnicity, geography, or mental faculties. All of them have the potential to see through the Lie and Awaken. Not all of them will choose to, instead preferring normalcy to the unknown, and those who try to Awaken don't always succeed (although most failed Awakenings are the result of intimately personal reasons for the Sleeper, or the result of outside tampering with the Awakening), but none the less anyone can Awaken. <br /> <br /> As for the whole &quot;Sleepers are all equal in Mages' eyes&quot; counter point you made, your argument falls flat under your own examples. The class schema you mentioned is Order specific, highlighting the Hubris and still very human belief systems that color Mage Society. Interestingly enough though, the fact that they exist at all indicates that Sleepers are given careful consideration in their organizations hierarchy because all Sleepers have the potential to become Awakened like them. If they truly didn't see Sleepers as anything but second class citizens then so much effort wouldn't be put into either incorporating them into their ethos or they wouldn't spend so much time trying to control who Awakens in order to swell their own ranks. We have a great example of a splat that doesn't consider their Sleeper equivalents to be anything but second class citizens, it's Genius the Transgression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-08-2016, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:43:14-08:00","id":1000477,"title":"","content":"Well.....actually, Awakening often <i>does</i> have it's mages look at Sleepers as second class citizens. Sure, the Seers, Ladder*, and Mysterium are the worst of the bunch, but they all do it to some degree.<br /> <br /> The <i>difference</i> is that Mage frames this (subtly) as a problem with Mage society, where as Genius, for as cruel as it's language is, never really seems like it expects you to disagree with it. Genius validates it's casual disregard for mundane humanity where Mage keeps up the dissonance. Both of these games can, in various ways, be seen about playing 1%, to borrow from the writers and developers of Awakening-but where Mage asks questions about that position and ultimately remembers that it's characters are monsters, Genius just default assumes it's character (and to an extent, it's players) are the victims in a cruel world and ultimately pins the blame outside of the characters.<br /> <br /> Some might argue that both succeed, since Mage is first and foremost a game about the horror of humanity writ large, while Genius supposedly is secretly a game about cosmic horror. And you know, I might agree with that-but cosmic horror is a bullshit genre anyways. It doesn't help that Geniuses** are larger than cosmic horror really need.<br /> <br /> *Sure, the Ladder is insanely humanist and highly encouraging, but they also have a literal caste system they dream of attaining, and sleepers follow under mages at all times.<br /> <br /> **Long standing question answered-Technically genii is the most gramatically correct version, but common parlance has changed enough that it's barely in use, likely to disappear, with geniuses filling the void. The use of genii strictly because it's correct in a twilit grammar is pretty much the textbook definition of academics being assholes to sate their need for intellectual validation.***<br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> how deep Genius's disregard for people is.<br /> <br /> ***I say this as an asshole academic who is all about validating his own intellectual standing, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-08-2016, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:56:03-08:00","id":1000524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000477#post1000477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well.....actually, Awakening often <i>does</i> have it's mages look at Sleepers as second class citizens. Sure, the Seers, Ladder*, and Mysterium are the worst of the bunch, but they all do it to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>...ya, that's a fair point. I admit I definitely got a bit too zealous in that last post. Sorry, Vent0.<br /> <br /> I will still stick to my guns about every human, and hypothetically any life form, having the potential to awaken though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Tidying Up 11-08-2016, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T18:52:11-08:00","id":1000576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000524#post1000524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...ya, that's a fair point. I admit I definitely got a bit too zealous in that last post. Sorry, Vent0.<br /> <br /> I will still stick to my guns about every human, and hypothetically any life form, having the potential to awaken though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is also worth noting that you are dead on that the main point of prejudice is nothing real world, inherently. Genius explicitly calls people out for actual problems where as the divide in Mage is fictional(there might be a few specific cases in the Legacies that aren't, but I don't know for sure)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:37:27-08:00","id":1003076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000457#post1000457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>, you cannot seriously believe that curiosity and obsession with the unknown are only inherent in those who aren't bogged down with the everyday struggles of survival?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I say that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000436#post1000436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They somewhat are (it's hard to be curious and obsessive about mysteries when you are struggling to survive).</div> </div> </div> </div>I said it is <i>harder</i>. If you are worrying about your next meal, chasing the Mystery Play that leads to an Awakening is harder to justify - uncertain outcome vs lost time and energy. When there are kids to take care of, you aren't as free to just wander off and <i>maybe</i> sign your name to a Watchtower. The curiosity can be there, but the person might not be as free to pursue it. There is a reason the Ladder encourages certain behaviors and viewpoints - it helps people escape the perpetual trap of the Lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000457#post1000457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All humans have a curiosity for the unknown, and when confronted with the unknown all<br /> humans have the capacity to become obsessed with it's mysteries. This is regardless of class, vocation, ethnicity, geography, or mental faculties. All of them have the potential to see through the Lie and Awaken. <b>Not all of them will choose to, instead preferring normalcy to the unknown</b>, and those who try to Awaken don't always succeed (although most failed Awakenings are the result of intimately personal reasons for the Sleeper, or the result of outside tampering with the Awakening), but none the less anyone can Awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just because &quot;let's go on an adventure&quot; has burned them before. It isn't advertised you are winning cosmic power at the start of most Mystery Plays, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-14-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:47:50-08:00","id":1003082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1000477#post1000477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>difference</i> is that Mage frames this (subtly) as a problem with Mage society, where as Genius, for as cruel as it's language is, never really seems like it expects you to disagree with it. Genius validates it's casual disregard for mundane humanity where Mage keeps up the dissonance. Both of these games can, in various ways, be seen about playing 1%, to borrow from the writers and developers of Awakening-but where Mage asks questions about that position and ultimately remembers that it's characters are monsters, Genius just default assumes it's character (and to an extent, it's players) are the victims in a cruel world and ultimately pins the blame outside of the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you support this with examples? Because merely from my memory, Mage pretty much talks about the Awakening as a uniformly good thing, and Mages are better off than the rest of the &quot;Sleepers&quot; who believe in the &quot;Lie&quot;, while Genius pretty much states that Inspired are insane and the rest of humanity is really better off without having their brains cooked by Inspiration. Like, the Genii who think they are above humanity and blame others for their failings are clearly labelled as the <i>bad guys</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In case it wasn't clear, I'm honestly curious how you came to that viewpoint, and interested in specific examples that establish it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-14-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:53:22-08:00","id":1003112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003082#post1003082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you support this with examples? Because merely from my memory, Mage pretty much talks about the Awakening as a uniformly good thing, and Mages are better off than the rest of the &quot;Sleepers&quot; who believe in the &quot;Lie&quot;, while Genius pretty much states that Inspired are insane and the rest of humanity is really better off without having their brains cooked by Inspiration. Like, the Genii who think they are above humanity and blame others for their failings are clearly labelled as the <i>bad guys</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In case it wasn't clear, I'm honestly curious how you came to that viewpoint, and interested in specific examples that establish it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As specific examples go, that'll have to wait, but I'm not necessarily disinclined to it, sure. I talk about the casually toxic language Genius has briefly in the first rant, and it's not hard to fish. Mage is a little harder, because it has that tightrope walk that all the Second Editions have had of both making the monsters seem awesome and at the same time slip in the unease.<br /> <br /> <i>Outside</i> of the books, which raises the questions of death of the author and had valid that is to hold(And boy howdy do I have mixed opinions on that) as well as questions of how representative fandoms are of mediums(particularly as far as fan games go, where the fandom more clearly owns the work than canon pieces), the crew of Awakening have made it tremendously clear that Mages are monsters and that they do not have healthy views of Sleepers as a societal norm, the main example being that Mages are effectively the 1%. Genius, in the mean time, has quite a body count of people banned for hyper-aggressive misanthropy of five years, and even the unbanned tend towards the various shades of disregard to disdain towards &quot;the common masses&quot;. Even if Genius was careful with it's wording (it's not), the several years I've had of dealing with Genius fans* would lead me to about the same conclusion, even if I had to end up accusing Genius of nuance.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, there's a lot of questions in the usefulness of that, not the least of which is I have admitted to bias before, so I can understand if people want me to toss that out and back it with textual support. I keep busy with my last class, though, and other projects are also demanding my attention.<br /> <br /> *Okay, not every Genius fan has basically been terrible, but experience has shown Genius fans to either be apologetic and inclined for nostalgic reasons or they tend to be some degree of terrible human being-rare is someone in-between those two. I don't want to say the latter has happened enough that I have to say the worst part of Genius is it's fanbase because #notallfans, but experience <i>really</i> wants me to, to a point that I went around to reading Genius just to find out if there was something in there to incite such common, terrible behavior. I really did not want to believe that was the case, but I expected it, and Chapter 1 went well beyond them. Until Catalysts, anyways.<br /> <br /> The fact that a lot of Genius fans have been receptive to fixing the toxic elements I pointed out is highly encouraging, whether they read it from me or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T20:25:43-08:00","id":1003216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003082#post1003082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you support this with examples? Because merely from my memory, Mage pretty much talks about the Awakening as a uniformly good thing, and Mages are better off than the rest of the &quot;Sleepers&quot; who believe in the &quot;Lie&quot;, while Genius pretty much states that Inspired are insane and the rest of humanity is really better off without having their brains cooked by Inspiration. Like, the Genii who think they are above humanity and blame others for their failings are clearly labelled as the <i>bad guys</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In case it wasn't clear, I'm honestly curious how you came to that viewpoint, and interested in specific examples that establish it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that Mage talks about the Awakened experience in terms of wonderment. It doesn't meaningfully talk about the Sleeper experience relative to the Awakened one; that's something you've added. It's not that being Awakened is <i>good</i>, per se, but that it's <i>captivating</i>; the value judgement is entirely your own. I suspect that some people have an easier time understanding why that's scary than others. I can't speak to how Genius talks about anything because it's been years since I read it.<br /> <br /> But, yeah. One of my continued frustrations with Mage in specific is that it doesn't spend enough time discussing what makes a Mage monstrous, so it's something that we have to hash out on forums all the time. For all that it drops mentions of &quot;hubris&quot; and &quot;addiction&quot; and &quot;obsession&quot;, it never actually <i>explores</i> those terms. Which might be a smarter move from a marketing standpoint, considering how strongly people have reacted to Promethean's language; I might be grumpy about it, but it's not like I'm going to stop buying the books. (I am a bit irritated by a lot of the language in Mage, honestly, and feel that it doesn't convey its content clearly enough, but Mage is also the line I know best, and I think I'd be equally irritated with the other books if I dove into them to the same degree.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:16:52-08:00","id":1003284,"title":"","content":"Vent0, I stand by my statement about mortal curiosity in the Chronicles of Darkness. This is because mystery and danger permeates the world to a degree where it's nearly impossible for a mortal civilian to go their entire lives without interacting with the supernatural or unknown in some meaningful way. I bring your attention to the questions for mortal character creation involving setting Integrety Breaking Points, in particular: &quot;What has your character forgotten?&quot; [might not be the exact question, but point is that if a question about what experiences has your character forced themselves to forget about or convince themselves that it wasn't real then the supernatural is decidedly prevalent to every being in the Chronicles of Darkness.]<br /> <br /> As for my examples about Mage, I was being more metaphoric with my statement about some won't choose to Awaken. No Mage during their Awakening will have any idea what the hells going on. Some might be aware of an Awakening, like Sleepwalkers in the Orders or Proximi, but here's the thing: Supernal Magic is insidious. Even if you somehow knew it was coming, you mind would be altered by the Mystery Play to make the secrets hidden behind the Lie tantalizing enough to seek them out. No one signs a Watchtower knowing that they'll gain cosmic powers, that's not what an Awakening is all about...or at least that what the Otherworld want's you to think. Aaaaand clever lead into the next paragraph:<br /> <br /> There are actually some great examples of what makes Mages monstrous, so much so that it had a noticeable impact on how the Orders have been called out on their ideological bullshit and how Banishers have been reimagined as either botched Awakenings or active realizations on the insidious nature of Supernal Magic in 2nd Edition. The reason it's difficult to find is because it's not in the Mage gameline, it's Witch Finders from Hunter the Vigil. Gives Mages a once over purely from a mortal perspective, highlights just what makes an antagonist Mage in a Hunter or Mage game, highlights how there are Mages beyond &quot;Supernal&quot; Mages and how they're just as deadly a threat as the prideful practitioners of &quot;Supernal&quot; Magic, and exposes the insidious nature of Supernal Magic and how Mages justify using an otherworldly power that bends reality to it's own laws while reality desperately tries to eliminate all traces of it from within it's bounds. It's fantastic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Side Note: Actually, thinking about Hunter the Vigil, Genius would greatly benefit from having a Mortal Remains-like entry regarding how Hunters see Geniuses, and just what interesting stories could be made with Geniuses as antagonists. Every Hunter installment has both broadened what each gameline is capable of, and has much needed mortal perspectives of the supernatural to inspire new ideas and interesting questions to bring up during Chronicles for those gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 11-15-2016, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:47:04-08:00","id":1003294,"title":"","content":"Mages' mistreatment of Sleepers is in fact stated several times in Awakening from the introduction to the Supporting Cast appendix. But I have long come to expect Genius fans to argue against a version of the game that exists only in Kyle Maquis' head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T03:29:56-08:00","id":1003305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003294#post1003294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages' mistreatment of Sleepers is in fact stated several times in Awakening from the introduction to the Supporting Cast appendix. But I have long come to expect Genius fans to argue against a version of the game that exists only in Kyle Maquis' head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Mage society (and mages) is not perfect, and mages have plenty of issues. But those are only Fallen Lies, for unlike Kyle Maguis who has seen the <i>true Mage</i>, we are only Sleepers compared to his genius, able to comprehend only what is handed us by the developers. :V<br /> <br /> It's not like the Orders have their flaws and hubris <i>pointed out right in their descriptions</i> or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T06:42:41-08:00","id":1003362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003294#post1003294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages' mistreatment of Sleepers is in fact stated several times in Awakening from the introduction to the Supporting Cast appendix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so?<br /> <br /> EDIT: You mean this as an example of how Mages are shown to be monstrous, then?<br /> <br /> If so, what about that is inherent to the Mage condition as opposed to said Mages merely being a-holes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003294#post1003294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I have long come to expect Genius fans to argue against a version of the game that exists only in Kyle Maquis' head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you expand that? I can see it either to mean the &quot;version of the game that exists only in Kyle Maquis' head&quot; to mean Mage, which makes no sense, since only Kyle Maquis would know that, or mean Genius, in which case why wouldn't that just be in the PDF that is already out?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-15-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T07:05:03-08:00","id":1003371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003284#post1003284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vent0, I stand by my statement about mortal curiosity in the Chronicles of Darkness. This is because mystery and danger permeates the world to a degree where it's nearly impossible for a mortal civilian to go their entire lives without interacting with the supernatural or unknown in some meaningful way. I bring your attention to the questions for mortal character creation involving setting Integrety Breaking Points, in particular: &quot;What has your character forgotten?&quot; [might not be the exact question, but point is that if a question about what experiences has your character forced themselves to forget about or convince themselves that it wasn't real then the supernatural is decidedly prevalent to every being in the Chronicles of Darkness.]</div> </div> </div> </div>And I stand by my statement that people under stress are <i>less</i> likely to pursue Mystery Plays of their own volition (I'd presume Astral Journeys operate more on dream logic, and are thus exempt from what most people would decide while awake). I didn't say they can't Awaken, or that they aren't curious - I said they are less inclined to pursue that curiosity, which might lead to Awakening, thus reducing representation amongst the Awakened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003284#post1003284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my examples about Mage, I was being more metaphoric with my statement about some won't choose to Awaken. No Mage during their Awakening will have any idea what the hells going on. Some might be aware of an Awakening, like Sleepwalkers in the Orders or Proximi, but here's the thing: Supernal Magic is insidious. Even if you somehow knew it was coming, you mind would be altered by the Mystery Play to make the secrets hidden behind the Lie tantalizing enough to seek them out. No one signs a Watchtower knowing that they'll gain cosmic powers, that's not what an Awakening is all about...or at least that what the Otherworld want's you to think. Aaaaand clever lead into the next paragraph:</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I'm confusing forum discussion with text, but aren't people who are already obsessive and curious more likely to Awaken than anyone else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003284#post1003284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are actually some great examples of what makes Mages monstrous, so much so that it had a noticeable impact on how the Orders have been called out on their ideological bullshit and how Banishers have been reimagined as either botched Awakenings or active realizations on the insidious nature of Supernal Magic in 2nd Edition. The reason it's difficult to find is because it's not in the Mage gameline, it's Witch Finders from Hunter the Vigil. Gives Mages a once over purely from a mortal perspective, highlights just what makes an antagonist Mage in a Hunter or Mage game, highlights how there are Mages beyond &quot;Supernal&quot; Mages and how they're just as deadly a threat as the prideful practitioners of &quot;Supernal&quot; Magic, and exposes the insidious nature of Supernal Magic and how Mages justify using an otherworldly power that bends reality to it's own laws while reality desperately tries to eliminate all traces of it from within it's bounds. It's fantastic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Questionably relevant, since that is Hunter - which isn't exactly authoritative on any game-line outside itself. Hasn't it been stated that Mages really <i>aren't</i> appropriate for Hunter games?<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, I've read Witch Finders and probably use more components from it than any other part of Hunter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003284#post1003284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side Note: Actually, thinking about Hunter the Vigil, Genius would greatly benefit from having a Mortal Remains-like entry regarding how Hunters see Geniuses, and just what interesting stories could be made with Geniuses as antagonists. Every Hunter installment has both broadened what each gameline is capable of, and has much needed mortal perspectives of the supernatural to inspire new ideas and interesting questions to bring up during Chronicles for those gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since Genius is a fan-game, a Mortal Remains chapter is pretty much impossible. Fans might make one, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:13:09-08:00","id":1003461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003362#post1003362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you expand that? I can see it either to mean the &quot;version of the game that exists only in Kyle Maquis' head&quot; to mean Mage, which makes no sense, since only Kyle Maquis would know that, or mean Genius, in which case why wouldn't that just be in the PDF that is already out?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Kyle Marquis has a problem with Awakening. He does not like it. Genius was in many ways a response to what he did not like about Awakening, which in turns tends to influence the opinion of fans of Genius as regards Awakening.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Kyle is working from several points of misapprehension about Awakening, stemming from his relationship to Ascension and the Sons of Ether/Technocracy, (I did not casually talk about the history of Genius for nothing.) He is hyper critical of a game that does not exist, because how he views Awakening is remarkably off base.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, so? </div> </div> </div>Hey, uh, pro-tip: when you ask someone to provide citation about how Mage subtly asserts that it's characters and their viewpoints are monstrous and wrong and the developer of the game comes in and tells you one big place where the game does exactly that but in a blunt way, the correct answer is not &quot;Okay, so?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-15-2016, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:33:08-08:00","id":1003473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003461#post1003461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kyle Marquis has a problem with Awakening. He does not like it. Genius was in many ways a response to what he did not like about Awakening, which in turns tends to influence the opinion of fans of Genius as regards Awakening.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Kyle is working from several points of misapprehension about Awakening, stemming from his relationship to Ascension and the Sons of Ether/Technocracy, (I did not casually talk about the history of Genius for nothing.) He is hyper critical of a game that does not exist, because how he views Awakening is remarkably off base.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Okay. Then the &quot;Lemuria controlled development for much of history&quot; was an oWoD call-back? Because it seemed very oWoD to me, as opposed to nWoD's trend of keeping the influence of the shadows/supernatural vague and undefined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003461#post1003461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, uh, pro-tip: when you ask someone to provide citation about how mage subtly asserts that it's characters and their viewpoints are monstrous and wrong and the developer of the game comes in and tells you one big place where the game does exactly that but in a blunt way, the correct answer is not &quot;Okay, so?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really see how the fact that Mage's mistreatment of Sleepers was immediately pertinent to discussion regarding the ratio and influence of people Awakening. More of a headspace conflict of thinking the comment was refering to one topic, when it was in fact talking about another. I was asking for clarification regarding what point the comment was addressing. I'll edit to clarify, then.<br /> <br /> But how does Mages exploiting non-Mage establish that it isn't better to be a Mage than not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-15-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:35:01-08:00","id":1003475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003473#post1003473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't really see how the fact that Mage's mistreatment of Sleepers was immediately pertinent to discussion regarding the ratio and influence of people Awakening. More of a headspace conflict of thinking the comment was refering to one topic, when it was in fact talking about another. I was asking for clarification regarding what point the comment was addressing. I'll edit to clarify, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very clearly not what we were talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-15-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T11:11:58-08:00","id":1003493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003473#post1003473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. Okay. Then the &quot;Lemuria controlled development for much of history&quot; was an oWoD call-back? Because it seemed very oWoD to me, as opposed to nWoD's trend of keeping the influence of the shadows/supernatural vague and undefined.<br /> <br /> But how does Mages exploiting non-Mage establish that it isn't better to be a Mage than not?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yep. Very definitely a callback. That is correct.<br /> <br /> 2) Because it shows how dehumanizing and monstrous the mage perspective is, how easy it is to lose sight of humanity.<br /> <br /> Forgive me for politics, but Mage is about the horror that you are likely to become Trump or Clinton-so utterly removed from the common human experience by their power and position that their choices in relation to them can only bring pain(in a variety of ways, take your pick) and so utterly powerful and well-positioned that, well, your choices <i>are</i> going to impact people whether you want them to or not. Mage basically posits that, with the exception of the wisest, which most people are not, to have power is to inevitably become like either of those two, or really your choice of terrible person in power, to become the tyrant you fought against, and to think yourself right in having done so.<br /> <br /> We might want the power and resources made available to Trump or Clinton, but Mage basically says &quot;Yeah, good luck without becoming them.&quot; And hence the core question is: Do you want everything you could have ever wanted at the expense of everything that makes you still human?<br /> <br /> There's also the point of how Mages are natural magnets for misery and woe, how the very nature of this supernatural makeup means they essentially will call in their worst times, but that's a different factor from this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T12:47:18-08:00","id":1003544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003493#post1003493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me for politics, but Mage is about the horror that you are likely to become Trump or Clinton-so utterly removed from the common human experience by their power and position that their choices in relation to them can only bring pain(in a variety of ways, take your pick) and so utterly powerful and well-positioned that, well, your choices <i>are</i> going to impact people whether you want them to or not. Mage basically posits that, with the exception of the wisest, which most people are not, to have power is to inevitably become like either of those two, or really your choice of terrible person in power, to become the tyrant you fought against, and to think yourself right in having done so.<br /> <br /> We might want the power and resources made available to Trump or Clinton, but Mage basically says &quot;Yeah, good luck without becoming them.&quot; And hence the core question is: Do you want everything you could have ever wanted at the expense of everything that makes you still human?<br /> <br /> There's also the point of how Mages are natural magnets for misery and woe, how the very nature of this supernatural makeup means they essentially will call in their worst times, but that's a different factor from this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that.<br /> <br /> Though it still seems to me to indicate that it is better to at least be on an equivalent level, rather than one more casualty to be stepped on. A Mage can choose to not use their abilities, if they want. A non-Mage cannot choose to use Mage abilities (baring edge cases), if they want. The only dehumanization Awakening does to you is what you would do anyways, given power (which is part of its Horror - you have no one to blame but yourself).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:10:44-08:00","id":1003559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003544#post1003544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for that.<br /> <br /> Though it still seems to me to indicate that it is better to at least be on an equivalent level, rather than one more casualty to be stepped on. A Mage can choose to not use their abilities, if they want. A non-Mage cannot choose to use Mage abilities (baring edge cases), if they want. The only dehumanization Awakening does to you is what you would do anyways, given power (which is part of its Horror - you have no one to blame but yourself).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's two points here.<br /> <br /> 1) To borrow from Mummy, power is a chain you wrap around yourself.<br /> <br /> Mage plays with this ideas in different ways than Mummy, but with the way Nimbus, inuring, Obsessions, and general power arcs in Mage goes, part of the problem of becoming powerful and why you will likely end up as [insert terrible politician of your choice here] is that you will basically get lost in the power and never be able to break free, so wrapped up in the symbol of yourself that you effectively stop being an actual person. In that way, it asks whether it is better to be beautifully, nobly powerless, as well as being self-possessive, or to surrender yourself to a demonstrably more monstrous icon of yourself, lacking free will but being &quot;safe&quot;. And, in fact, it makes the point that the desire to avoid being a casualty is often the first step to becoming that monster caging your own will.<br /> <br /> It's also, fundamentally, a false dichotomy-to not have power does not automatically make one a casualty. It is not the victims fault for not seizing power, if they even have the chance to. Mages <i>can</i> be wise. It's hard as hell, but every single one of them could. The horror is that they probably <i>won't</i> and be damn good at justifying it to themselves. And it begins with &quot;it is better to be on an equivalent level, rather than one more casualty to be stepped on.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, Wisdom doesn't lie down that path.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;The only dehumanization Awkaening does to you is what you would do anyways-&quot;<br /> <br /> Only, he says. It's about as bad as Just. Because it's something you would do anyways doesn't stop it from being dehumanizing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:19:22-08:00","id":1003563,"title":"","content":"Like, as comparable argument, you could avoid being stepped on by also persuading a vampire to Embrace you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:43:03-08:00","id":1003576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003544#post1003544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for that.<br /> <br /> Though it still seems to me to indicate that it is better to at least be on an equivalent level, rather than one more casualty to be stepped on. A Mage can choose to not use their abilities, if they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregarding Obsession, that's like, the biggest fucking theme in the game right now? That same mage still has a screwy aura that will fuck shit up, merely because he happens to be around to them. It'll be gradual, but when shit starts going down, you can bet the only sensible response is to try to fix it, because you can't ignore your hands shaking every time that something happens under the veil and fucks your shit. And the only way to fix it is to tap into the same arcane knowledge that began it all, unbeknown to you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:46:42-08:00","id":1003579,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887107-understand-wisdom?p=895967#post895967\">Related Rant.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:48:13-08:00","id":1003580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003563#post1003563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, as comparable argument, you could avoid being stepped on by also persuading a vampire to Embrace you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampirism, however, comes with its inherent downsides. Nothing intrinsically afflicts a Mage. You don't <i>have</i> to pursue mysteries (Obsession rewards but does not compel). Paradox is only a risk with spell use (and when observed or overreaching at that). The Nimbus may be an issue, but it's effect still isn't very clear. Being a Mage gives you options, albeit ones that will screw you over if you employ them without great caution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003576#post1003576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disregarding Obsession, that's like, the biggest fucking theme in the game right now? That same mage still has a screwy aura that will fuck shit up, merely because he happens to be around to them. It'll be gradual, but when shit starts going down, you can bet the only sensible response is to try to fix it, because you can't ignore your hands shaking every time that something happens under the veil and fucks your shit. And the only way to fix it is to tap into the same arcane knowledge that began it all, unbeknown to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, disregarding Obsession, because while you are encouraged to pursue them, nothing forces you as it stands. Would you be a sucky Mage? Sure. But a Sleeper is an even worse Mage. You have options. Whether you choose to employ them (and pay the costs) is up to you. But it is a choice Sleepers lack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-15-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:57:13-08:00","id":1003584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003580#post1003580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampirism, however, comes with its inherent downsides. Nothing intrinsically afflicts a Mage. You don't <i>have</i> to pursue mysteries (Obsession rewards but does not compel). Paradox is only a risk with spell use (and when observed or overreaching at that). The Nimbus may be an issue, but it's effect still isn't very clear. Being a Mage gives you options, albeit ones that will screw you over if you employ them without great caution.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically the only way to avoid the inherent downsides to being a mage is don't be a mage.<br /> <br /> Which is hard for mages to do, namely because <i>the world won't shut up</i>.<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, you're right, to a degree. A mage exercising his power wisely is still essentially a magnet for his own misery(the only way to avoid it is to not be a mage, which is hard when your sense keep telling you about shit), but will suffer far, far less than most of his ilk.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Wisdom is not an easy Mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-15-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:05:19-08:00","id":1003587,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mages aren't forced to follow Obsessions&quot; strikes me as kind of a weak argument. True, there aren't game mechanics punishing Mage players for not pursuing their characters' Obsessions, but that is more due to the carrot-over-stick design philosophy of Chronicles of Darkness Second Edition than Obsessions actually being a thing Mages can easily ignore in the setting. As well, Obsessions are kind of the major driving force of conflict in the game. Saying there's nothing forcing you to pursue them is a little like saying there is nothing forcing you to go on adventures in D&amp;D. Like, yeah, it's technically true, but there's kind of no game if you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-15-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:02:48-08:00","id":1003626,"title":"","content":"I'd also add that there's a deliciously sinister element to the charrot over stick philosophy of 2nd Edition too. There's all the incentive in the world to persue Myeteries and Obsessions from a purely mechanical standpoint, signifying how easy it is for a Mage to fall into the &quot;Well, maybe just this once&quot; trap of hubris. Sort of how Beats can be earned from choosing to take dramatic failures and by resolving negative Conditions, reinforces the themes of conflict and oppression for all the core games of the Chronicles of Darkness. <br /> <br /> As for my earlier statements about Hunter.<br /> <br /> 1) Hunter the Vigil is such a good gameline because not only does it stand on it's own with nothing but the premise, monster creation rules, and the ST's own dark and twisted imagination. But every installment adds to the already pre-existing gamelines by showing the mortal perspective of the games lore, powers, and themes. It allows us as an audience to spot commonalities and discrepancies, and ask questions about the gamelines that we wouldn't normally have cause to ask about. (I.E. Is the Supernal true reality? Or is it an alien, infectious dimension that wants to twist and warp the world to something more like itself like the Knights of St. George believe?)<br /> <br /> 2) I believe Genius could really use a fan-made Mortal Remains chapter. For all of the above mentioned reasons. (Take for instance, what if saaaay that whole Martian Invasion thing happened and the Genii deployed their forces to stop it. But Hunter observers witnesses the fight...and saw the Genii killing eachother, eyes bright with a chaotic and unstable energy that coldly hinted at a greater intelligence and purpose. Destroying the land in accordance to whatever nightmarish version of reality they're experienceing. How would the Hunters react? What does that say about the Genius gameline? What fun stuff could you do with that?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T22:45:06-08:00","id":1003790,"title":"","content":"Okay... before I go into a full-fledged argument, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a>, are you actually cool with this major thread derail? Because we're now having a full-on &quot;How to Mage&quot; discussion in the main CofD forums on a Genius thread. Which I'm happy to do, but I'm not going to pretend that I'm discussing Genius if I do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T01:01:39-08:00","id":1003810,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a>, that's a fair point. This isn't the Mage thread and my intention was to use examples from some of the core gamelines to illustrate what could be done to address some serious problems that Genius suffers from in the form of comparable examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T01:19:40-08:00","id":1003818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003580#post1003580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, disregarding Obsession, because while you are encouraged to pursue them, nothing forces you as it stands. Would you be a sucky Mage? Sure. But a Sleeper is an even worse Mage. You have options. Whether you choose to employ them (and pay the costs) is up to you. But it is a choice Sleepers lack.</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument seems to have gone over your head. Let me simplify it for you: if you're disregarding obsessions as a matter or course, you have no reason to call them as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T02:14:16-08:00","id":1003828,"title":"","content":"While Mage doesn't mechanically cripple you for not pursuing your Obsessions, it's pretty clear that that is a decent chunk of what the game is about, and it seems to me that choosing to ignore such an integral part of the game is kinda missing the point of sitting down and playing it in the first place. It's like what Charlaquin said about D&amp;D. The game doesn't mechanically cripple you for not going on some sort of adventures, but if you aren't interested in doing so then why are you even playing D&amp;D in the first place? I mean sure, you can do what you want with the game, but again, it seems like you're missing the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T03:32:21-08:00","id":1003845,"title":"","content":"Do people think I'm actually saying you <b>should</b> ignore Obsessions ina Mage game?<br /> <br /> No, I am saying a mage <b>can</b> ignore Obsessions (and other facets of Mage-hood). A vampire can't choose not to be a vampire by not using their abilities. A werewolf can't ignore or refrain from their nature without consequence. And a Genius can't go back to business as usual even if they don't build any Wonders.<br /> <br /> Just like D&amp;D Adventurers can just retire (or end retirement), Mages can opt out (and in) with little consequence (baring LTN). Mortals and other supernaturals don't have it as easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-16-2016, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T05:47:16-08:00","id":1003879,"title":"","content":"Mages are bombarded with visions of the supernatural everywhere they go. This is made quite clear in the text. They may close their eyes and blockade their ears, but the world won't shut up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:19:33-08:00","id":1003893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003626#post1003626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also add that there's a deliciously sinister element to the charrot over stick philosophy of 2nd Edition too. There's all the incentive in the world to persue Myeteries and Obsessions from a purely mechanical standpoint, signifying how easy it is for a Mage to fall into the &quot;Well, maybe just this once&quot; trap of hubris. Sort of how Beats can be earned from choosing to take dramatic failures and by resolving negative Conditions, reinforces the themes of conflict and oppression for all the core games of the Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Mage's themes are strengthened by it being opt-in/carrot - since there is nothing forcing you, <i>you</i> choose to employ your magic, and thus you must own its consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003626#post1003626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my earlier statements about Hunter.<br /> <br /> 1) Hunter the Vigil is such a good gameline because not only does it stand on it's own with nothing but the premise, monster creation rules, and the ST's own dark and twisted imagination. But every installment adds to the already pre-existing gamelines by showing the mortal perspective of the games lore, powers, and themes. It allows us as an audience to spot commonalities and discrepancies, and ask questions about the gamelines that we wouldn't normally have cause to ask about. (I.E. Is the Supernal true reality? Or is it an alien, infectious dimension that wants to twist and warp the world to something more like itself like the Knights of St. George believe?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter is good, but it isn't authoritative on other gamelines. Hunter says you can labotomize the magic out of someone - Mage says, no you can't (at least for Awakened). Of the two, Mage is more of an authority on Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003626#post1003626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I believe Genius could really use a fan-made Mortal Remains chapter. For all of the above mentioned reasons. (Take for instance, what if saaaay that whole Martian Invasion thing happened and the Genii deployed their forces to stop it. But Hunter observers witnesses the fight...and saw the Genii killing eachother, eyes bright with a chaotic and unstable energy that coldly hinted at a greater intelligence and purpose. Destroying the land in accordance to whatever nightmarish version of reality they're experienceing. How would the Hunters react? What does that say about the Genius gameline? What fun stuff could you do with that?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really need Genii shooting each other for Hunters to dislike them. The first encounter with Illuminated targeting an orphanage for &quot;spare parts&quot; is likely to do that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:22:54-08:00","id":1003894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003879#post1003879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are bombarded with visions of the supernatural everywhere they go. This is made quite clear in the text. They may close their eyes and blockade their ears, but the world won't shut up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither does a major city. Mages basically aren't deaf when most people are (able to pick up sensory input that exists, but many cannot perceive). Unless those supernatural signals come with a side of mind-control/influence, it just mean Mages need to learn to filter things out, which they'd arguably have to do anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:16:51-08:00","id":1003948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003894#post1003894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither does a major city. Mages basically aren't deaf when most people are (able to pick up sensory input that exists, but many cannot perceive). Unless those supernatural signals come with a side of mind-control/influence, it just mean Mages need to learn to filter things out, which they'd arguably have to do anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>sigh<br /> <br /> &quot;Mages can't shut their Gnosis off. Once your soul is opeed to the insights of a Path, it's always there. Every supernatural event, from the least ghost using it's Influences to the greatest cosmic Mysteries, stands out to a mage without trying. She feels an itch, or a faint aura or a sense of someone walking over her grave.<br /> <br /> <i>Constantly</i>.<br /> <br /> Other supernatural beings can pretend that the world's still &quot;normal&quot; despite becoming vampires or werewolves. Mages know that the supernatural is nearly omnipresent. Even if they try to live normal lives, they'd soon be provoked by their own sense for the uncanny.&quot;<br /> -Literally one of the first pages in the 2e corebook.<br /> <br /> Look, you can pretend all day that mages can just &quot;shut it off&quot;, but your interpretation isn't actually supported by the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T09:20:51-08:00","id":1003979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003845#post1003845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people think I'm actually saying you <b>should</b> ignore Obsessions ina Mage game?<br /> <br /> No, I am saying a mage <b>can</b> ignore Obsessions (and other facets of Mage-hood). A vampire can't choose not to be a vampire by not using their abilities. A werewolf can't ignore or refrain from their nature without consequence. And a Genius can't go back to business as usual even if they don't build any Wonders.<br /> <br /> Just like D&amp;D Adventurers can just retire (or end retirement), Mages can opt out (and in) with little consequence (baring LTN). Mortals and other supernaturals don't have it as easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make it &quot;as easy&quot; for a mage to disregard the effects of having Gnosis, you're running it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T10:47:32-08:00","id":1004005,"title":"","content":"Speaking as someone with shades of Christian American-fundamentalist in my upbringing, to be a &quot;good&quot; Mage, you need to become an ascetic. Not merely in a remote mountain, though that's progress, but in something so well-abjured that even the Underworld can't invade. Because the experience of being a Mage is the experience of someone who is constantly aware of sin. From the clothing people wear to the advertisements on the television to the lure of materialism on every street corner and every brand name on a tote bag, to be a good Mage in the human world demands a level of hyper-vigilance that goes well beyond paranoia into actively hating and willfully disbelieving in the world around you, because <i>all</i> of it is the enemy to some degree. The way we retain sanity in this world is to accept that it's simply full of evil and sin and all we can do is be lights in the darkness, guarding our hearts and keeping the faith.<br /> <br /> This is not a realistic view of any person so-raised except someone genuinely super-human. To be a Mage is to have an Obsession. End of story. It is true that a PC can be exceptional and choose not to pursue her Obsessions, but it is the nature of PCs to be exceptions to the rule. The existence of saints does not uplift the laity: it merely provides guiding beacons in a drowning landscape, glimmers of hope amidst despair. Switching to the Catholic worldview, this is why we have confession: because <i>no one</i> is free of sin and no one ever will be. (Except, y'know, Mage Jesus, but again, an exception proving the rules.)<br /> <br /> It is fine if you don't understand obsession. I am someone who has spent the past 15 years pursuing my obsessions. That's part of why I'm on this forum at all. Sure, I take a break quite often, and accomplish smaller things here and there, but these things often pale in comparison to my actual ambitions. So I understand obsession in a way that is unlikely universal, and I understand that you simply might not get it. I have been fortunate enough that I am not addicted to any profoundly-abusable substances (does cheese count? I like cheese), so there's a limit to how much I can understand about what it means to be addicted to something that's actively hurting you and consequently the people around you. I can understand how my obsession does, though; I can see it in how protective and defensive I am about it, in how I am frustrated and angry when I think I can make progress but am stymied by other obligations, and in how much of my self-worth I've bound up in its accomplishment. These are not healthy behaviors.<br /> <br /> I've thought about walking away. I've thought about it a lot, over these last 15 years. I always end up coming back. It's like co-dependence, like coming back to an abusive spouse. Because I'm still convinced that, if I just figure out that next bit, I'll be able to finish it and it'll be over. As if that would stop me from coming up with something new to obsess over. (Also, irrelevant, but yes, I've been getting professional help.)<br /> <br /> So yes. A perfect person could ignore their Obsession. But no one is perfect. We all sin. It is the air we breathe. Being a Mage is about being Awakened. It is about having tasted the fruit of knowledge and to know the difference between good and evil. And in knowing, we become complicit. Even to ignore the existence of the supernatural, to ignore the siren call of Mysteries, is a choice and that choice <i>matters</i>. Because that choice <i>is</i> your Obsession. You become a Banisher, and quickly descend into becoming one of the Mad: far from successfully ignoring your Obsessions, you become controlled by them. The Catholics call it &quot;false humility&quot;, a form of pride at your humility.<br /> <br /> Yeah. You can ignore your Obsessions. That's also a temptation. But I will tell you now: it makes things <i>worse</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:03:08-08:00","id":1004011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003948#post1003948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> sigh<br /> <br /> &quot;Mages can't shut their Gnosis off. Once your soul is opeed to the insights of a Path, it's always there. Every supernatural event, from the least ghost using it's Influences to the greatest cosmic Mysteries, stands out to a mage without trying. She feels an itch, or a faint aura or a sense of someone walking over her grave.<br /> <br /> <i>Constantly</i>.<br /> <br /> Other supernatural beings can pretend that the world's still &quot;normal&quot; despite becoming vampires or werewolves. Mages know that the supernatural is nearly omnipresent. Even if they try to live normal lives, they'd soon be provoked by their own sense for the uncanny.&quot;<br /> -Literally one of the first pages in the 2e corebook.<br /> <br /> Look, you can pretend all day that mages can just &quot;shut it off&quot;, but your interpretation isn't actually supported by the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the text doesn't actually contradict me. I'm not saying they can pretend the world is still &quot;normal&quot;. I'm not saying they don't detect the supernatural. I'm saying they can detect it and choose to ignore it. That's not an option for other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1003979#post1003979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you make it &quot;as easy&quot; for a mage to disregard the effects of having Gnosis, you're running it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean aside from the fact that I'm not trying to &quot;run&quot; Mage games like that? Only pointing out that Mages <i>can</i>?<br /> <hr /><br /> Actually addressing Genius, and how this pertains to it. Mages, for instance, seems metaphysically slanted toward being Awakened. Which is fine - it is a game about Mages, after all. Not all games are so spun, however. Vampire, for instance, seems to clearly posit that while there are some upsides to being Undead, it's a case of making lemonade out of lemons. Genius (as well) states that while you are capable of Wonders, you probably had it better before your Breakthrough. You achievements are &quot;grounded&quot; in fleeting Mania, you can't really contribute to accurate human knowledge, and you stand poised to descend into monstrosity.<br /> <br /> So when it is stated that Genius validates it's casual disregard for mundane humanity where Mage keeps up the dissonance, I'm confused. Sane Genii often envy non-Genii, while I've not really seen that sentiment represented amongst the Awakened. Non-Wonders are more reliable and stable, while I'm not aware of any way non-Awakened works can surpass Awakened ones. That seems to me to basically state that Mages are superior in Awakened (all positives, with negligible and avoidable negatives), while Genius is stating the Inspired are different, but there is still value in being Mortal.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying one is &quot;better&quot; than the other. Just supporting why I'm confused at the prior statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-16-2016, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:00:01-08:00","id":1004043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004011#post1004011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the text doesn't actually contradict me. I'm not saying they can pretend the world is still &quot;normal&quot;. I'm not saying they don't detect the supernatural. I'm saying they can detect it and choose to ignore it. That's not an option for other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You mean aside from the fact that I'm not trying to &quot;run&quot; Mage games like that? Only pointing out that Mages <i>can</i>?<br /> <hr /><br /> Actually addressing Genius, and how this pertains to it. Mages, for instance, seems metaphysically slanted toward being Awakened. Which is fine - it is a game about Mages, after all. Not all games are so spun, however. Vampire, for instance, seems to clearly posit that while there are some upsides to being Undead, it's a case of making lemonade out of lemons. Genius (as well) states that while you are capable of Wonders, you probably had it better before your Breakthrough. You achievements are &quot;grounded&quot; in fleeting Mania, you can't really contribute to accurate human knowledge, and you stand poised to descend into monstrosity.<br /> <br /> So when it is stated that Genius validates it's casual disregard for mundane humanity where Mage keeps up the dissonance, I'm confused. Sane Genii often envy non-Genii, while I've not really seen that sentiment represented amongst the Awakened. Non-Wonders are more reliable and stable, while I'm not aware of any way non-Awakened works can surpass Awakened ones. That seems to me to basically state that Mages are superior in Awakened (all positives, with negligible and avoidable negatives), while Genius is stating the Inspired are different, but there is still value in being Mortal.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying one is &quot;better&quot; than the other. Just supporting why I'm confused at the prior statement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I haven't read Genius, so I can only speak to Mage. But I think the way to look at it is this:<br /> <br /> Mage (the game) makes mages powerful, this makes mages (the characters) feel that they are 'better' than sleepers, Mage (the game) then brings forth the idea that maybe they aren't better, look at all this horrible stuff that happens because of them. Thus the game shows that the attitude Mages(the characters) have is wrong.<br /> <br /> I would also specifically disagree with this: 'Mages, for instance, seems metaphysically slanted toward being Awakened.'<br /> <br /> It isn't metaphysical, it is psychological. You have to be of an inquisitive and obsessive type to become a Mage and therefore all mages are inquisitive and obsessive. They <i>could </i> ignore their Obsessions but they won't, that's why they have them in the first place.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:08:04-08:00","id":1004046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Non-Wonders are more reliable and stable, while I'm not aware of any way non-Awakened works can surpass Awakened ones. That seems to me to basically state that Mages are superior in Awakened (all positives, with negligible and avoidable negatives), </div> </div> </div>As for the first point, certain non-awakened (linear) magic has been noted in the game as not provoking paradox. I'm not sure if this changed or was disregarded entirely with the 2E mage setting.<br /> <br /> As far as being all positives, a few good points were raised about why it isn't so, as the risks are not negligible without not being a mage entirely (aka, not using magic at all). But even if you don't, you raise the risk that another mage with a simple spell can discover what you are and take advantage of you for it. Not to mention other supernatural beings who can do the same. If you just ignore being a mage, you'll probably end up screwed over.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:23:54-08:00","id":1004056,"title":"","content":"Grounding: The problem at hand is that Genius and Mage both place it's characters as being toxic towards the sleepers/unenlightened, but that Mage does so in a way that condemns it's characters for their monstrosity where as Genius does it in such a way that it expects the reader to sympathize and validates any similar feeling they might have towards &quot;the common masses&quot;, or at least that is the premise I have established. Vent thinks that's bullshit and wants me to back it up. I have no problem with letting others back it up as well.<br /> <br /> But it's not a &quot;How are Mages monsters&quot;, although that is a highly pertinent sub-question to the problem of &quot;How does one game do it right and the other do it wrong?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:34:21-08:00","id":1004059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004056#post1004056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grounding: The problem at hand is that Genius and Mage both place it's characters as being toxic towards the sleepers/unenlightened, but that Mage does so in a way that condemns it's characters for their monstrosity where as Genius does it in such a way that it expects the reader to sympathize and validates any similar feeling they might have towards &quot;the common masses&quot;, or at least that is the premise I have established. Vent thinks that's bullshit and wants me to back it up. I have no problem with letting others back it up as well.<br /> <br /> But it's not a &quot;How are Mages monsters&quot;, although that is a highly pertinent sub-question to the problem of &quot;How does one game do it right and the other do it wrong?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my apologies. Jumped in and just saw it phrased that way when I saw the comparison between the weaknesses of other game lines not being able to ignore what they are.<br /> <br /> I'm not extremely well versed in Genius, but I would think Mage being a condemnation of of montrous mages is evident in the Wisdom chart and Hubris?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:03:10-08:00","id":1004074,"title":"","content":"Well, it is a highly pertinent question. Lots of people have asked over the years &quot;Why <i>wouldn't</i> I want to be a Mage?&quot;, failing to see the monstrosity, or even the weaknesses, of it in comparison to the other lines.<br /> <br /> Considering Mage is the only game in the whole of the Chronicles to genuinely terrify me, you might imagine the problems I have-particularly since one of the big things that makes Mages terrifying is their ease of blindness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T17:46:24-08:00","id":1004178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004074#post1004074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is a highly pertinent question. Lots of people have asked over the years &quot;Why <i>wouldn't</i> I want to be a Mage?&quot;, failing to see the monstrosity, or even the weaknesses, of it in comparison to the other lines.<br /> <br /> Considering Mage is the only game in the whole of the Chronicles to genuinely terrify me, you might imagine the problems I have-particularly since one of the big things that makes Mages terrifying is their ease of blindness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing, though, is that (at least I) don't see any inherent monstrousness in being a Mage, per se. The Monstrosity comes into play in that Mage hands you a heap of power with little accountability. Being a Mage doesn't make one a monster - it just make being a monster <i>so easy</i>. And that's, I think, core to the horror and themes - you have no one to blame but yourself. No Beast driving you to attack. No Death Rage to blame upon the bodies at your feet. Lack of Clarity doesn't hide what you are doing, and nothing Inspires you toward these things other than your own desires. It's <i>all</i> on you. Mage's evil is humanity's evil, writ larger with reality bending power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T18:18:13-08:00","id":1004187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004178#post1004178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing, though, is that (at least I) don't see any inherent monstrousness in being a Mage, per se. The Monstrosity comes into play in that Mage hands you a heap of power with little accountability. Being a Mage doesn't make one a monster - it just make being a monster <i>so easy</i>. And that's, I think, core to the horror and themes - you have no one to blame but yourself. No Beast driving you to attack. No Death Rage to blame upon the bodies at your feet. Lack of Clarity doesn't hide what you are doing, and nothing Inspires you toward these things other than your own desires. It's <i>all</i> on you. Mage's evil is humanity's evil, writ larger with reality bending power.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the crux of your issue is on account of how alienating the cause and effect of how the personal horror themes is explored?<br /> <br /> You end your paragraph describing human monstrosity, but begin it saying it's not inherently monstrous to mages. See the contradiction?<br /> <br /> Again, all of that disregards that you have no blissful ignorance to disregard the horrible stuff that goes on around you. And the most human response is to sense this stuff and ask the big question: Why?<br /> <br /> Obsession follows from there.<br /> <br /> Does it requires more involvement from the Storyteller to evoke those themes? Sure. At least as much as it involves triggering Uratha into Kuruth, or exposing vampiric Touchstones to the dance macabre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T18:21:57-08:00","id":1004192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004178#post1004178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The thing, though, is that (at least I) don't see any inherent monstrousness in being a Mage, per se. The Monstrosity comes into play in that Mage hands you a heap of power with little accountability. Being a Mage doesn't make one a monster - it just make being a monster <i>so easy</i>. And that's, I think, core to the horror and themes - you have no one to blame but yourself. No Beast driving you to attack. No Death Rage to blame upon the bodies at your feet. Lack of Clarity doesn't hide what you are doing, and nothing Inspires you toward these things other than your own desires. It's <i>all</i> on you. Mage's evil is humanity's evil, writ larger with reality bending power.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's true for a lot of things, I imagine we have some definition problems here mixing in with a failure to appreciate certain ballkicking factors that ensure the struggle.<br /> <br /> But we're deviating-the problem is &quot;How does Mage condemn it's characters for the same sins Genius exults in?&quot;, which I will answer when I am not busy trying to build a brand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T20:44:32-08:00","id":1004228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004074#post1004074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is a highly pertinent question. Lots of people have asked over the years &quot;Why <i>wouldn't</i> I want to be a Mage?&quot;, failing to see the monstrosity, or even the weaknesses, of it in comparison to the other lines.<br /> <br /> Considering Mage is the only game in the whole of the Chronicles to genuinely terrify me, you might imagine the problems I have-particularly since one of the big things that makes Mages terrifying is their ease of blindness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. I agree with you. Being a mage is awesome. Being a <i>human </i>while being a mage is <i>way too easy.</i> In all ways, magnified fifty fold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T01:20:12-08:00","id":1004290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004178#post1004178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing, though, is that (at least I) don't see any inherent monstrousness in being a Mage, per se. The Monstrosity comes into play in that Mage hands you a heap of power with little accountability. Being a Mage doesn't make one a monster - it just make being a monster <i>so easy</i>. And that's, I think, core to the horror and themes - you have no one to blame but yourself. No Beast driving you to attack. No Death Rage to blame upon the bodies at your feet. Lack of Clarity doesn't hide what you are doing, and nothing Inspires you toward these things other than your own desires. It's <i>all</i> on you. Mage's evil is humanity's evil, writ larger with reality bending power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not knowledgeable enough about Vampire to speak to the thing with the Beast, or enough about Genius to speak to the thing with Inspiration, but if you come out of Kuruth surrounded by blood and gore, that's totally on you. Sure, maybe not the first few times, fine; you don't know what sets you off. But, y'know, figure that out and avoid it. Or lock yourself in a room. Sure, it'll make for a boring game, but at least you didn't kill anyone. (I mean, hell; the Rahu-perspective on the Elodoth is <i>literally</i> &quot;Kuruth is just one more tool in your toolbox&quot;.) It's not that different from ignoring your Obsessions. (I mean, yeah, it's different: it's a different set of mechanics for a reason. But it's not <i>that</i> different.)<br /> <br /> And as far as I know, low Clarity doesn't actually prevent you from seeing the consequences of your actions. Not sure where you get that or what you're trying to refer to. But Promethean/Changeling/Hunter is different-in-kind from Vampire/Werewolf/Mage to begin with. Also kinda suspect we'd disagree on what makes a Changeling monstrous, but I'm reserving opinions about that until it's actually published.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T03:19:15-08:00","id":1004318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004187#post1004187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You end your paragraph describing human monstrosity, but begin it saying it's not inherently monstrous to mages. See the contradiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because there isn't any. Mage doesn't add any more monstrosity than what is already there. For Vampire, it is human + vampire monstrosity. Promethean is just Promethean monstrosity, at least until they learn more about human nature. For Mage, it is just human, same as any other power you'd give humans. 1+x=1, ergo x is 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T05:18:07-08:00","id":1004344,"title":"","content":"That's not how it works. Gnosis is a potence. Mage monstrosity =Human monstrosity elevated to the G potence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:04:53-08:00","id":1004362,"title":"","content":"I appreciated ArcaneArts clarification of the issue, but it still feels like the discussion it drifting more towards 'What makes a mage inherently monstrous' over the previously stated 'How Mages and Geniuses differ in tone about treating sleepers.&quot; Both are, again, fair points of discussion. Just want to make sure I'm not getting lost again on the actual point of contention.<br /> <br /> But on the 'how are mages monstrous,' it still just seems as though the idea that mages can just not do magic to avoid pitfalls both avoids the intent of the game in general. When the Drivethru ad blurb goes on about hearing the call of the supernatural daily and being addicted to mysteries. To take what I think is a good summation from the wiki, &quot;Nothing external forces a mage to pursue the Mysteries, but those who do not have a natural curiosity and a willingness to go to great lengths to satisfy it simply do not Awaken.&quot; Those who even get to Awaken without said drive would inevitably reject it. But even assuming you can ignore using magic, having Awakened means that other mages, vampires, etc can somewhat easily discover what you are and take advantage of you for nefarious purposes if you can't defend yourself (and if you don't use magic, you probably can't). You're basically forced into it regardless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Mage, it is just human, same as any other power you'd give humans. </div> </div> </div>Except the point that mage goes off the Wisdom/Hubris pitfalls instead of normal morality. No power a normal human has in the world can compare to what mages can do. Losing your depth as a Mage isn't the same as a powerful/rich human doing the same because of the sheer range/strength will-working provides someone. Which is why abusing sleepers and ignoring morality for power is a large pitfall for Mages.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 11-17-2016, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:14:48-08:00","id":1004370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004318#post1004318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, because there isn't any. Mage doesn't add any more monstrosity than what is already there. For Vampire, it is human + vampire monstrosity. Promethean is just Promethean monstrosity, at least until they learn more about human nature. For Mage, it is just human, same as any other power you'd give humans. 1+x=1, ergo x is 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you assume that power doesn't change people. Granted, every human has the <i>potential</i> for the monstrosity of Mages, but not every human realizes that potential. And that theme is echoed by the fact that every human has the potential to awaken, but only a rare few do so. And at that, only the ones who are predisposed to the obsession that drives Mages to be monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:34:45-08:00","id":1004377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004370#post1004370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if you assume that power doesn't change people. Granted, every human has the <i>potential</i> for the monstrosity of Mages, but not every human realizes that potential. And that theme is echoed by the fact that every human has the potential to awaken, but only a rare few do so. And at that, only the ones who are predisposed to the obsession that drives Mages to be monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that mages get power. But magic isn't the only kind of power. We see the same trends when people get non-magical power. If the source of power differs, but the outcome remains the same, it isn't the source that is responsible but the mere presence of the power (for a given individual). If they abuse their power when given wealth and authority instead of magic, can you really say the magic is at fault?<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the entire argument hinges on whether one believes that power inherently corrupts (or merely allows for corruption to reach noticeable levels). Captain America vs Red Skull (Movie version of the argument).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:39:15-08:00","id":1004380,"title":"","content":"I believe power inherently changes people. Whether that change makes them corrupt is up to them, but rare is the person it doesn't change for the worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:45:29-08:00","id":1004383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004362#post1004362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the 'how are mages monstrous,' it still just seems as though the idea that mages can just not do magic to avoid pitfalls both avoids the intent of the game in general. When the Drivethru ad blurb goes on about hearing the call of the supernatural daily and being addicted to mysteries. To take what I think is a good summation from the wiki, &quot;Nothing external forces a mage to pursue the Mysteries, but those who do not have a natural curiosity and a willingness to go to great lengths to satisfy it simply do not Awaken.&quot; Those who even get to Awaken without said drive would inevitably reject it. But even assuming you can ignore using magic, having Awakened means that other mages, vampires, etc can somewhat easily discover what you are and take advantage of you for nefarious purposes if you can't defend yourself (and if you don't use magic, you probably can't). You're basically forced into it regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm not saying anyone should run a Mage game with Mages avoiding being mages. I'm saying Mages have the capability to actually do so, where other supernaturals cannot. As for &quot;but others can find you and use you&quot;, that separates you from non-Mages how? Especially since &quot;automatically affects mortals&quot; or &quot;affects mortals more&quot; powers won't work on you, you'd have forewarning, passive Supernatural Tolerance, and you'd have the <i>option</i> of using magic anyways. A normal Mortal can't opt-into using magic in an emergency (baring Merits and Relics, that may be available).<br /> <br /> Given the comparison of &quot;Mage who refrains from using magic&quot; and &quot;Average Mortal&quot;, who is better off in these scenarios? Who has more options?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004362#post1004362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the point that mage goes off the Wisdom/Hubris pitfalls instead of normal morality. No power a normal human has in the world can compare to what mages can do. Losing your depth as a Mage isn't the same as a powerful/rich human doing the same because of the sheer range/strength will-working provides someone. Which is why abusing sleepers and ignoring morality for power is a large pitfall for Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans don't have normal Morality (anymore - it is Integrity now). As for Magic vs Wealth, I'd disagree that more options denotes a qualitative change. Given Wealth, Authority, and advanced technology, are we really talking that much a degree of difference? Again, is it the magic itself (Mage-ness) or just having a lot of power at your disposal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:48:56-08:00","id":1004384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004380#post1004380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe power inherently changes people. Whether that change makes them corrupt is up to them, but rare is the person it doesn't change for the worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I disagree that power truly changes a person (as opposed to simply revealing unexpressed traits), so that is probably the basis for the disconnect here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:07:03-08:00","id":1004389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004383#post1004383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Magic vs Wealth, I'd disagree that more options denotes a qualitative change. Given Wealth, Authority, and advanced technology, are we really talking that much a degree of difference? Again, is it the magic itself (Mage-ness) or just having a lot of power at your disposal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when Bill Gates can bring people back from the dead, create biblical plagues, control the weather, create life, create and destroy matter and energy in flagrant defiance of thermodynamics, erase people's minds, create extradimentional space, Create and control actual spirits, and travel through time, then we won't be talking about a meaningful difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:15:41-08:00","id":1004394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I'm not saying anyone should run a Mage game with Mages avoiding being mages. I'm saying Mages have the capability to actually do so, where other supernaturals cannot. </div> </div> </div> I understand that. My counterpoint is that you'll never actually run into a mage that has pursued his mystery play to awakening, has actually gone through/accepted with awakening, but then doesn't pursue their obsessions. It simply won't happen. The circumstances/odds make it a near impossibility in how awakening is presented, from what I see. Technically a vampire could reach Golconda on the same night they are embraced, but you'll never really see it happen and it shouldn't be presented that vampires aren't monsters because it is possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for &quot;but others can find you and use you&quot;, that separates you from non-Mages how? Especially since &quot;automatically affects mortals&quot; or &quot;affects mortals more&quot; powers won't work on you, you'd have forewarning, passive Supernatural Tolerance, and you'd have the <i>option</i> of using magic anyways. A normal Mortal can't opt-into using magic in an emergency (baring Merits and Relics, that may be available). </div> </div> </div>Because supernatural beings such as Vampires, Mages, and Werewolves aren't typically going out of their way to harass/abuse your typical non-Mage. But Vampires and Mages can have very compelling reasons to go out of their way to harness the fact that you are a mage or kill you.<br /> <br /> But the situation isn't the same if you're prefacing 'option' of magic. Because if you know how to use it to an extent, you are studying it. Which puts you right into the situation of obsession and possible hubris. It is putting it into an even more impossible situation of a Mage who awakened, studied some magic, then has no more dealings with magic except in self-defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given the comparison of &quot;Mage who refrains from using magic&quot; and &quot;Average Mortal&quot;, who is better off in these scenarios? Who has more options? </div> </div> </div> That'd be like saying a soldier in Yemen (just to pick a random country we've had involvement in, could be any combat zone) is safer than an Average Joe in America because he knows how to fight/use a gun. The Average Mortal is significantly less likely to run afoul of the supernatural compared to an Awakened because their unique power can be identified/targetted. Whereas there are billions of other average mortals that don't attract supernaturals like a moth to a candle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humans don't have normal Morality (anymore - it is Integrity now). As for Magic vs Wealth, I'd disagree that more options denotes a qualitative change. Given Wealth, Authority, and advanced technology, are we really talking that much a degree of difference? Again, is it the magic itself (Mage-ness) or just having a lot of power at your disposal? </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I always forget all the new changes to said systems in that regard. But my point is more that the focus changes to Wisdom/Hubris over what mortals experience. Showing the basis that typical mortal versus Mage experience difference is just that, revolving around containing your hubris in the face of such power.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we are talking about a massive difference. Technically it depends on what splat you get into, but if we're talking just mundane wealth, authority, and technology, yeah, it is a large degree of difference. Magic really is that powerful, and is intended to be. and why there isn't a gameline called Billionaire: The WealthoningTM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 11-17-2016, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:26:05-08:00","id":1004400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004389#post1004389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, when Bill Gates can bring people back from the dead, create biblical plagues, control the weather, create life, create and destroy matter and energy in flagrant defiance of thermodynamics, erase people's minds, create extradimentional space, Create and control actual spirits, and travel through time, then we won't be talking about a meaningful difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus he needs to be able to do all that without actually <i>spending</i> any of his resources. Mages have literally <i>infinite</i> &quot;money&quot;, so there's yet another issue. Why bother using spells in moderation if they have no cost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:38:28-08:00","id":1004517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004400#post1004400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus he needs to be able to do all that without actually <i>spending</i> any of his resources. Mages have literally <i>infinite</i> &quot;money&quot;, so there's yet another issue. Why bother using spells in moderation if they have no cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana and Reach are free now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:41:34-08:00","id":1004519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004362#post1004362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciated ArcaneArts clarification of the issue, but it still feels like the discussion it drifting more towards 'What makes a mage inherently monstrous' over the previously stated 'How Mages and Geniuses differ in tone about treating sleepers.&quot; Both are, again, fair points of discussion. Just want to make sure I'm not getting lost again on the actual point of contention.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted I wasn't rebuking you earlier-do what thou will. Conversations do change over time.<br /> <br /> It's just more that I don't want to lose sight of what I'm saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:50:18-08:00","id":1004528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004517#post1004517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana and Reach are free now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they have things they can spend resources on. And while Reaching too hard comes with consequences, a Mage can always keep Reaching. Like, there's not a limited amount of Reach. &quot;I can afford to spend one more Reach, yeah...&quot; So while mages have limits they can still do most things without having to <i>sacrifice</i> anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:13:13-08:00","id":1004534,"title":"","content":"Nitpick - modern psychology gives more weight to the idea that power doesn't corrupt, but rather just enables. The overwhelming majority of one's personality is fixed by one's genetics and early formative years. Power changes your environment, and grants new reactions to environmental stimuli, but it doesn't fundamentally change you as a person. Someone that respects the privacy and innate rights of other sentient beings isn't going to change. Studies show that people with a strong sense of compassion and empathy respond positively to gaining power, rather than negatively. Power does nto corrupt. It heightens pre-existing ethical leanings. <br /> <br /> The larger factor of mental shift in Mage actually comes from the Orders and their cult-mentality, combined with peer pressure and group think effects. Which has nothing to do with their magic but rather basic human psychology. But, putting that aside for a moment - the majority of horror in Mage doesn't come from corruption. It comes from messing up with your power because you didn't realize the full implications of your actions and making things worse. Hubris isn't corruption. Hubris is thinking you know best for people, and things spirling out of control even when you have the best intentions. Its trying to be a good person and effing up because you know just enough to get into trouble. &quot;Power corrupts&quot; is not a theme of 2e mage (unless we're talking about the Abyss, which is a different can of worms).<br /> <br /> I also feel compelled to point out that a mage that doesn't cast spells is also a part of the game. Its literally built into High Wisdom. <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> So, where does the monstrocity of being a mage come from? My personal take focuses on Obsessions and the Nimbus. Now, Obsessions don't have a lot of mechanical kick to them, but I personally play it like the Obsession Condition, where you get constantly distracted and upset and frustrated away from working towards them. And the Nimbus Tilt? It spreads like a disease, infecting people around you. You alter reality around you just by existing. That's kind of scary when you really think about it. If you are a Mastigos with a Nightmare-ish Nimbus, then you spread misery around everyone you spend time with. Think about it. That's sickening. Moros could be making the world around them rot even with being perfectly Wise. Even if you have a more benevolant Nimbus, you're still messing with people's lives just by existing in a way that vamps and wolves and lings don't. Now, add on the spells spreading that Nimbus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:15:15-08:00","id":1004535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004517#post1004517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mana and Reach are free now?</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004528#post1004528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, they have things they can spend resources on. And while Reaching too hard comes with consequences, a Mage can always keep Reaching. Like, there's not a limited amount of Reach. &quot;I can afford to spend one more Reach, yeah...&quot; So while mages have limits they can still do most things without having to <i>sacrifice</i> anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana is a renewable resource. Reach isn't a resource and can be Contained if it goes wild. Granted, wealth also renews itself by that same logic - you spend it, it goes away for a while, then you get more of it back in time (and work). So, the entire difference is moot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:35:38-08:00","id":1004552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004535#post1004535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mana is a renewable resource. Reach isn't a resource and can be Contained if it goes wild. Granted, wealth also renews itself by that same logic - you spend it, it goes away for a while, then you get more of it back in time (and work). So, the entire difference is moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>#ParadoxSequestration, #SustainableMana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T12:09:59-08:00","id":1004566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004519#post1004519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted I wasn't rebuking you earlier-do what thou will. Conversations do change over time.<br /> <br /> It's just more that I don't want to lose sight of what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotcha. Just wanted to make sure it didn't seem like I was trying to derail your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also feel compelled to point out that a mage that doesn't cast spells is also a part of the game. Its literally built into High Wisdom. </div> </div> </div>I don't have the book in front of me, so I don't know the precise wording. But I have the impression it was built around not casting petty/unnecessary spells, not around abstaining from casting period. It reflects being responsible with magic and not about not using it at all. The two are decidedly different. You don't risk Wisdom for using magic, you risk it for using it when you don't have to, which isn't necessarily in a self-defense context. And this, again, is the absolutely highest level of Wisdom.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T12:39:25-08:00","id":1004582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004534#post1004534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also feel compelled to point out that a mage that doesn't cast spells is also a part of the game. Its literally built into High Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always been untrue. A Mage at all times is to do magic. A High Wisdom Mage just knows the time and place for it, in accordance to his enlightened will in harmony with the circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-17-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:07:27-08:00","id":1004616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004534#post1004534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick - modern psychology gives more weight to the idea that power doesn't corrupt, but rather just enables. The overwhelming majority of one's personality is fixed by one's genetics and early formative years. Power changes your environment, and grants new reactions to environmental stimuli, but it doesn't fundamentally change you as a person. Someone that respects the privacy and innate rights of other sentient beings isn't going to change. Studies show that people with a strong sense of compassion and empathy respond positively to gaining power, rather than negatively. Power does nto corrupt. It heightens pre-existing ethical leanings.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was an interesting-looking book I noticed the other day, but didn't pick up (and can't, for the life of me, remember enough of the title to search for it usefully). But the cover flap said it would be arguing that actually, power doesn't merely not-corrupt; it's actually really, really good and most people actually use it quite well. Unfortunately, I don't visit that bookstore very often anymore, so it'll be a while before I can find it again. =/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T18:27:50-08:00","id":1004734,"title":"","content":"Well, here's the thing. Whether or not you personally believe power corrupts, the saying is true in the Chronicles of Darkness. While some ST's might run it otherwise, the core and gamelines as a whole adhere to this philosophy and it's illustrated time and again through the splats, powers, and antagonists.<br /> <br /> To give two relevant examples that still tie into the now dual nature of this thread.<br /> <br /> 1) In Mage, before we even get into how real world psychology breaks down when literal magic is involved, the Awakening alone forever alters the person who becomes a Mage. Their psyche and mentality will be tied to their Path for the rest of their lives, as will their senses and talents for magic. Combine that with the Supernal Realm's Blue &amp; Orange morality and the positive reinforcement mechanics behind Obsessions and Arcane Exp and corruption becomes second nature to the Awakened. <br /> <br /> 2) For the sake of the argument &amp; core topic, if we look at Genius the delusions and drive to create stems solely from the chaotic energy of Mania that courses through the Inspired's minds. This energy is so powerful that it can completely invert a Genius' personality and cognitive awareness to a degree that very few other power sources....actually nvm. Most power sources in the core CofD gamelines do that pretty well to. Point is, a Genius' mind and personality is forever altered by the power that courses through their minds. Pare that with the nihilistic undertone and academic exceptionalism subtext and you have a witch's brew of corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish. 11-17-2016, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T19:59:27-08:00","id":1004770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004582#post1004582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has always been untrue. A Mage at all times is to do magic. A High Wisdom Mage just knows the time and place for it, in accordance to his enlightened will in harmony with the circumstance.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1004734#post1004734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, here's the thing. Whether or not you personally believe power corrupts, the saying is true in the Chronicles of Darkness. While some ST's might run it otherwise, the core and gamelines as a whole adhere to this philosophy and it's illustrated time and again through the splats, powers, and antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ummm... no, its not true. And, no, I don't see it &quot;illustrated time and again.&quot; Corruption exists, but not because of monsters having power. Its because <i>they're monsters with the drives of monsters. </i>Corruption in VtR is the result having the insticts to see humans as nothing more than food. Corruption in WtF comes from giving into spirits and listening to them, taking the easy path, instead of following the Oath; individually, uncorrupted Forsaken have more power, but fewer numbers. In Promethean, corruption is the result of despair and Tormented emotions, while more power actually drives them closer towards the New Dawn. In CtL, its the very-human psychological tendacy for abusers to fall into absue cycles, irregardless of power; corruption can take the form of becoming a willing victim instead of abuser. In Demon, power is unrelated to corruption in any way - you become corrupt from selling out to the angels, usually to &quot;go home&quot; or avoid capture. Beast... corruption is just falling out of the teaching culture; that has to do with personality rather than power<br /> <br /> I find your statement to be flawed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) In Mage, before we even get into how real world psychology breaks down when literal magic is involved, </div> </div> </div> Prove it. You're making a bold claim with no reason to believe it. Mages are consistantly portrayed as being human, having human drives and needs. Baring the use of artificial intervention of some sort (be it a spell or chemicals), mages should reflect human psychology.<br /> <br /> Now, you want to throw out human psychology for the sake of a story? That's one thing. Wouldn't be the first time science took a back seat to story. But that has nothing to do with magic, and everything to do with tweaking a setting to fit your narrative. It also risks losing empathy with your players - stories need to resonate with their audience, and departing from the science of how people actually think can cause dissonance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Awakening alone forever alters the person who becomes a Mage. Their psyche and mentality will be tied to their Path for the rest of their lives, as will their senses and talents for magic. Combine that with the Supernal Realms Blue &amp; Orange morality and the positive reinforcement mechanics behind Obsessions and Arcane Exp and corruption becomes second nature to the Awakened. </div> </div> </div> &quot;Corruption becomes second nature.&quot; No, it doesn't. Awakening ties you to a Path, but there is nothing about a Path that innately pushes you towards corruption. Obsessions can include beneficial directions and studies, including raising Wisdom. Arcane XP can come in a multitude of non-corrupt methods. You're telling us that corruption is a thing here, with nothing to back it up. This feels like nothing more than confirmation bias.<br /> <br /> And what's up with &quot;Blue and Orange morality?&quot; Integrity is not morality. Wisdom is not morality. Mages keep the human morals they were raised with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) For the sake of the argument &amp; core topic, if we look at Genius the delusions and drive to create stems solely from the chaotic energy of Mania that courses through the Inspired's minds. This energy is so powerful that it can completely invert a Genius' personality and cognitive awareness to a degree that very few other power sources....actually nvm. Most power sources in the core CofD gamelines do that pretty well to. Point is, a Genius' mind and personality is forever altered by the power that courses through their minds. Pare that with the nihilistic undertone and academic exceptionalism subtext and you have a witch's brew of corruption. </div> </div> </div> I'm not that familar with Genius, so I'll pass on commenting about that. However, I will say that this - what you are describing isn't corruption. Its a mind-altering substance, equivalent to a drug or alcohol. Its not the same thing.<br /> <br /> I will also say that your use of &quot;power source&quot; is a bit odd. This isn't D&amp;D 4e. The Beast of VtR isn't a power source - concentrated life energy in the form of vitae is; the Beast's instincts are what twist a vampire's mind. I get that you're talking about monstrous beings developing monster impulses. But this has nothing to do with power corrupting you. Its the transformation away from being human that leads to corruption, irregardless of power. PCs, upon becoming inhuman monsters, effectively have their genome rewritten. Their biological instincts change in a direction that includes the possibility of corruption and ethical failings. Mages, however, do not gain new insticts or urges - even their Obsessions are tied to human thought, not alien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-17-2016, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T06:42:56-08:00","id":1004910,"title":"","content":"MCN, <br /> <br /> While I disagree with your counter argument you do make two very good points. The first is that I should clarify my point further when I state that &quot;power corrupts.&quot; The second is that you're entirely right when you say their monstrous nature drives them towards corruption. I feel this stems from the same core premise that we are both hinting at, and that is that all facets of our own world (be it modern day human institutions to mythological beings) are cast as a dark reflection within the Chronicles of Darkness. <br /> <br /> In regards to my statement about power corrupts within the Chronicles of Darkness. Let me clarify by saying that I don't mean corruption as evil, I mean corruption as distortion and transformation into something monstrous. Corruption is less about succumbing to a moral shortcoming and more about supernatural and temporal power twisting and changing a person into something else due to it's nature within the Chronicles of Darkness. A monster's behaviors and powers are a core part of their nature, to illustrate further all of the Core Gamelines power states (Blood Potency, Primal Urge, Gnosis, Azoth, Wyrd, Psyche, Sekhem, Primus, and Lair) all mechanically reinforce the idea of slowly metamorphosing into an even greater monster or aberration (yes, even Azoth. If that weren't the case then a Centimani wouldn't be able to increase their Azoth.) And all of those states empower a supernatural creature's powers, further distancing themselves from the humans they were (in the case of Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Geist, Mummy except in reverse as Sekhem decreases, and Beast) or the humans they wish to become (in the case of Promethean, also Mummy, and Demon) as well as enforce the supernatural banes and taboos associated with being a monster. <br /> <br /> Side Note: My earlier statement about the Supernal Realms Orange &amp; Blue morality is in reference to the inherently alien nature of the Supernal and it's denizens. It's so beyond human understanding that conventional morality has no sway, and this is explicitly illustrated in the Supernal Being creation section in 2nd Edition describing that a Supernal entity does have a virtue and vice, but they don't adhere to any human virtues and vices. (Ex. Virtue: Orange and Vice: Blue.) This is also illustrated again nicely in Demon the Descent since their Virtues and Vice are completely alien compared to humans as well, or by the Temkhat's (might have misspelled) Immortal Virtue from the Deceived in Mummy the Curse (One literally being Corruption mind you.) <br /> <br /> And as for modern psychology being broken down when literal magic is involved...well I'll just name off a couple of things that might just do that to a human mind: Mind Arcanum, Life Arcanum, Legacies, Prelacies, Artifacts, Paradox, the God Machine, the Lower Depths, and of course the Awakening itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 11-18-2016, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:51:52-08:00","id":1005118,"title":"","content":"I am increasingly skeptical that &quot;monstrosity&quot; even has value as a concept, much less as some kind of design goal or critical yardstick. I certainly don't care if mages are monsters or not - what a useless territory to fight over - when what matters is if the horror game can do horror, which it manifestly can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T15:28:09-08:00","id":1005132,"title":"","content":"jacobkosh, would you care to elaborate further?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:19:36-08:00","id":1005226,"title":"","content":"Adding to the derail with a nitpick:<br /> <br /> Mage <i>does not</i> describe what happens to people when you give them power.<br /> <br /> Mage describes what happens to people when you give them a form of power that has no intrinsic cost besides mental effort and acts as a date rape drug on the people around them. The negative effects (Paradox) hurt <i>someone else</i> unless they feel like being a nice guy.<br /> <br /> Mages are the mystical equivalent of Paris Hilton.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> That being <i>said</i> - Genius could strongly benefit from an adjustment. Focus less on the cool toys (let's be honest here - the game as it stands is a vehicle for the cool toys), and more on the psychology.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Damn it, now I want to write SRMD as a condition set...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T22:20:11-08:00","id":1005244,"title":"","content":"And place more responsibility on the Genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T00:00:39-08:00","id":1005262,"title":"","content":"I may still disagree in regards to Mage, but you two do still make great points. Plus the refocus on Genius and addressing it's issues is greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T03:12:17-08:00","id":1005291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1005244#post1005244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And place more responsibility on the Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Genius *is* responsible for what they do, though (baring Illumination).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:55:40-08:00","id":1005373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1005291#post1005291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Genius *is* responsible for what they do, though (baring Illumination).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha. No.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">words</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T14:38:43-08:00","id":1005482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1005373#post1005373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ha. No.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">words</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Support? ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T15:35:56-08:00","id":1005496,"title":"","content":"Actually, the burden of proof is on you since ArcaneArts is (somewhat rudely, perhaps) questioning your statement. And I'd also like to hear some support for how Geniuses are forced to take responsibilities or face meaningful consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T07:17:07-08:00","id":1005696,"title":"","content":"The idea of geniuses being forced to take responsibility is discussed in &quot;The Peerage and the Law&quot; (GtT 129). As it turns out...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 129</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Peerage vacillates between being a hierarchical society and a loose fraternity of mad scientists. Currently the organization is as loose as it has been in almost a century, with the foundations little more than mailing-lists, vestigial societies wrapped around their magazines and earlier history. This was no accident: the approach of the millennium saw increasingly paranoid and exclusionary behavior from the Peerage, which seemed to be eating itself after the collapse of Lemuria. Witch hunts and purges rooted out the corruption in the Demiurges, but then went farther...too far...and the whole Inspired world threatened to tilt toward madness and civil war. Over the course of several months in 1998, geniuses from all the foundations met and forged the Lucidity Concord (sometimes called the Pact of ARPAnet) that dismantled most of the formal structures of the foundations, proscribed the more aggressive and inquisitorial fellowships, and generally ended &quot;The Peerage&quot; as a unified organization with hierarchies and secret decoder rings.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> But for now, there is no formal law among the Peerage. Nonetheless, there are guidelines, vestigial moral structures from the old days. While there's no formal punishment system in place anymore, violating these rules can get a Peer alienated, snubbed, or\u2015if his crimes are egregious enough\u2015simply &quot;taken care of&quot; in order to prevent a descent into dangerous public violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah, the Peerage isn't this organization that will police Geniuses any more. In terms of responsibilities and consequences, you'd probably want to look at &quot;Drawbacks of Obligation&quot; (GtT 87), &quot;The Resources Merit&quot; (GtD 88), &quot;Antagonism&quot; (GtD 317), and various sections on unmada and Illuminated (GtD, 34, 290, 348, 365, etc.)<br /> <br /> One of the weak points of Genius is that realistic consequences cut most Geniuses off from most of what makes them special. This is especially described in detail in &quot;The Resources Merit.&quot; If you cut them off from society (and thus funding) and send a mob after them a Promethean will still have all their Transmutations, a Beast their Atavisms and Nightmares, a Princess their Charms, and a Genius... whatever they can carry with them, whatever they invested in Merits like Laboratory or Dumpster Diver, and a few minor abilities that stem from their ability to spend Mania. The author says that this weak point should be treated as an opportunity for story hooks and plot as opposed to a threat to bring the game to a halt by turning its PCs into broke people wishing they had enough money to do all their cool stuff, but it's a tension I get the sense some feel is not adequately resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T09:20:14-08:00","id":1005730,"title":"","content":"I can't deny that alienation is a meaningful consequence, but it feels thematically weak compared to Mage. Sure, left-handed Mages are also hunted down if they're obvious enough to get noticed, but Mages face supernatural consequences of their actions regardless if they get noticed by other Mages. Mutating spells, falling Wisdom, Paradox Conditions, and Abyssal incursions are all very real possibilities if a Mage does not keep a handle on their magic. The lesson is unequivocally &quot;You should not do this&quot;, not &quot;You should not be caught doing this&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: I've read some of your page suggestions as well.<br /> Resources doesn't really fit what I assumed responsibility meant in this context; that a Genius should take responsibility for their own actions. It feels more like the responsibility one has as a business owner or freelancer. YMMV how well that plays out in a game.<br /> <br /> Antagonizing the Masses is definitely more like it, but it lacks a sense of urgency. That should be expanded from one page to being a much larger part of the book, imo. It feels a lot more related to the concept of mad scientists than Lemuria which gets a much bigger focus.<br /> <br /> And then Obligation/Illuminated. Low Obligation really doesn't feel very punishing, but that's probably because it has so weak penalties compared to low Humanity in Vampire, and I found no other mechanical advantage as in Mage. And becoming an Illuminated... Well, it sounds more like something to which one should aspire, but terminology aside they seem like a fitting type of antagonist. I just don't see the reason why Illuminated exists when they seem to act like morally bankrupt Geniuses. Both Draugr and Mad seems a lot more distinct since they are quite clearly something that normal Vampires and Mages aren't.<br /> But Illuminated as a punishment for transgression... It just feels like a cop out for explaining why your character becomes unplayable. If I designed Genius I'd try to emulate increasing carelessness as a Genius becomes too wrapped up in their work to pay attention to safety. Or take a page from Promethean and add something similar to Disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-20-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:02:11-08:00","id":1005764,"title":"","content":"Here here Tessie,<br /> <br /> I would also add that Genius gets too caught up in the Science! aesthetic when it comes to designing the consequences of being a Genius (I.E. Alienation from the Peerage and financial bankruptcy.) The whole opening paragraph of the book lays down the idea that Mania might be an alien influence shaping a Genius for some unknowable purpose, and that a Genius' own ideas and inspiration might not even be their own...and then they do nothing with it. (They try with the Illuminated, but it winds up being more of a twisted ego trip more than anything.)<br /> <br /> It's funny, but Demon the Descent actually does give us an example of how to do the &quot;being reshaped by an alien intelligence&quot; thing right with the Half-Demons and their Reverse Cipher. Essentially the more attention they draw from/the more they work with the God Machine the more powerful they become as their Cipher unlocks like a normal Demon...until they unlock the equivalent of the Final Secret and become either a literal or figurative slaves to the Machine. This would be perfect for mechanically illustrating a Genius' descent into Illumination, and hinting back at that potential for a great and terrible force working it's will through the Genii.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-20-2016, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:37:16-08:00","id":1005775,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>, I appreciate that you read the pages. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a>, I agree, and I've been thinking about the Pentagram especially as a sort of analogue to Illumination, although in my case I was thinking of the idea of a true falling and a break from any internal or external controls or fetters. But I really like your idea of it as a God-Machine trap of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:51:07-08:00","id":1005780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1005696#post1005696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the weak points of Genius is that realistic consequences cut most Geniuses off from most of what makes them special. This is especially described in detail in &quot;The Resources Merit.&quot; If you cut them off from society (and thus funding) and send a mob after them a Promethean will still have all their Transmutations, a Beast their Atavisms and Nightmares, a Princess their Charms, and a Genius... whatever they can carry with them, whatever they invested in Merits like Laboratory or Dumpster Diver, and a few minor abilities that stem from their ability to spend Mania. The author says that this weak point should be treated as an opportunity for story hooks and plot as opposed to a threat to bring the game to a halt by turning its PCs into broke people wishing they had enough money to do all their cool stuff, but it's a tension I get the sense some feel is not adequately resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, this can actually be a good idea. It would need a lot of tweaking and refinement and playing around with what the options are when the Genius is low(never always completely close the door when it's a major template, which Genius shouldn't be), but it is distinctive of the archetype and can be a good way to handle narrative flow as well as being a knob on tension.<br /> <br /> <i>Mechanically</i>, so far Genius has been...not incompetent.I need to read more before I say competent outright, and it's certainly not even as good as some of the clumsier canon books, but the ideas work, even if the executions aren't always there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:53:52-08:00","id":1005785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1005730#post1005730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't deny that alienation is a meaningful consequence, but it feels thematically weak compared to Mage. Sure, left-handed Mages are also hunted down if they're obvious enough to get noticed, but Mages face supernatural consequences of their actions regardless if they get noticed by other Mages. Mutating spells, falling Wisdom, Paradox Conditions, and Abyssal incursions are all very real possibilities if a Mage does not keep a handle on their magic. The lesson is unequivocally &quot;You should not do this&quot;, not &quot;You should not be caught doing this&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: I've read some of your page suggestions as well.<br /> Resources doesn't really fit what I assumed responsibility meant in this context; that a Genius should take responsibility for their own actions. It feels more like the responsibility one has as a business owner or freelancer. YMMV how well that plays out in a game.<br /> <br /> Antagonizing the Masses is definitely more like it, but it lacks a sense of urgency. That should be expanded from one page to being a much larger part of the book, imo. It feels a lot more related to the concept of mad scientists than Lemuria which gets a much bigger focus.<br /> <br /> And then Obligation/Illuminated. Low Obligation really doesn't feel very punishing, but that's probably because it has so weak penalties compared to low Humanity in Vampire, and I found no other mechanical advantage as in Mage. And becoming an Illuminated... Well, it sounds more like something to which one should aspire, but terminology aside they seem like a fitting type of antagonist. I just don't see the reason why Illuminated exists when they seem to act like morally bankrupt Geniuses. Both Draugr and Mad seems a lot more distinct since they are quite clearly something that normal Vampires and Mages aren't.<br /> But Illuminated as a punishment for transgression... It just feels like a cop out for explaining why your character becomes unplayable. If I designed Genius I'd try to emulate increasing carelessness as a Genius becomes too wrapped up in their work to pay attention to safety. Or take a page from Promethean and add something similar to Disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.^<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">words</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:55:39-08:00","id":1005786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1005764#post1005764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here here Tessie,<br /> <br /> I would also add that Genius gets too caught up in the Science! aesthetic when it comes to designing the consequences of being a Genius (I.E. Alienation from the Peerage and financial bankruptcy.) The whole opening paragraph of the book lays down the idea that Mania might be an alien influence shaping a Genius for some unknowable purpose, and that a Genius' own ideas and inspiration might not even be their own...and then they do nothing with it. (They try with the Illuminated, but it winds up being more of a twisted ego trip more than anything.)<br /> <br /> It's funny, but Demon the Descent actually does give us an example of how to do the &quot;being reshaped by an alien intelligence&quot; thing right with the Half-Demons and their Reverse Cipher. Essentially the more attention they draw of/the more they work with the God Machine the more powerful they become as their Cipher unlocks like a normal Demon...until they unlock the equivalent of the Final Secret and become either literal or figurative slaves to the Machine. This would be perfect for mechanically illustrating a Genius' descent into Illumination, and hinting back at that potential for a great and terrible force working it's will through the Genii.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this.^<br /> <br /> Demon is actually a hell of a book for Genius to take notes from in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T11:06:05-07:00","id":1145570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=998143#post998143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't science. That isn't even mad science. That's magic. Specifically, that is Mage: the Ascension Magik.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans can activate magical abilities to turn lead into gold, heal, control the elements etc. Aren't THEY mages?<br /> <br /> This is a moot argument. From the beginning, from Vampire, splats had a mystical SOURCE that provided a mystical ENERGY that they could turn into mystical POWERS.<br /> The source had different fluff each time but each splat operated on this same power system model.<br /> <br /> The part that Genius powers work because they believe in them exists only in your head and not in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T11:24:31-07:00","id":1145578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression#post997612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This turned out to be more of an opinion piece, if you have any thoughts on the points brought up please post them below.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like Genius: the Transgression, never though I'd be saying that but I do none the less. It shows what creativity a fan game can bring to the table, and it's ideas can inspire stories that wouldn't normally come up in a Chronicle of Darkness.<br /> <br /> This is what make me so disappointed in Genius' failings though. For all it's themes of inspiration, potential, and creativity the game itself is one of the most stifling gamelines of the fan-made series. And here's why, my own thesis if you will: Geniuses must be scientists.<br /> <br /> Sure, this might be the obvious point of the game. Play as a mad scientists, create impossible inventions, explore infinite dimensions, Ect. But not all geniuses are scientists, but in Genius the Inspired must become scientist or inventors in order to do anything involving Wonders. There are no artists who seek to create masterpieces in mediums never before attempted, no athlete so dedicated to the craft that their mind masters the physics of the game to elevate it to new dimensions, no musician who writes a song so inspiring that it births a sentient thought form in the depths of the human subconsciousness. If any of those examples became Inspired, their only hope to be playable is to don the white lab coat, strap on goggles, or take oration lessons because there is no way their Wonders will ever see the light of gameplay the way the rules are now. And that is the very opposite of inspiring.<br /> <br /> Again, this might just be the point of the game though. Being a mad scientist. But consider this: having the option to be a Genius from any background and profession opens up unlimited possibilities for character creation. Having the option to only play a Genius who's from a scientific field limits players options at character creation. Playing a mad scientist is achievable in both of the above options, while any other option is only available in one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider this thread to have conned me. I was promised a critique/analysis and what do I get? A single complaint that is not even true.<br /> <br /> One, this complaint is like saying &quot;You know what makes Vampire: the Masquerade bad? That you can only play as a vampire. I feel that this really ruins the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> But, two, IT'S NOT EVEN TRUE!<br /> <br /> Geniuses can come from any background and the book explains at length that most of the Dr., Prof., etc. titles are actually made up and have no academic background behind them, they often just picked to look trendy. Certainly Geniuses by fluff are meant to enter a kind of fevered, obsessed inspired state, captivated by a brilliant idea they just had when they engage in Wonder-making, as this is part of their aesthetic, but this can happen to literally any type of character. You can even make that a story, a character who doesn't quite understand where these ideas and compulsions come from.<br /> <br /> Even this too much for you? Ignore even that! I can't say -I-'ve never been guilty of it, slapping the Genius template on a character just to explain away the cool gadgets he owned for which the template would be a prerequisite. It's a roll-player and not role-player action but sure, go for it. Bend the system to fit your playstyle.<br /> <br /> And other than Geniuses there are other mini templates in the book. I did play as a rouge (Orphan) robot or runaway Beholden before, and on one occassion an old guy who was a Clockstopper who'd antagonize the party.<br /> <br /> I can't find it now but there was another comment above asking why you could not make a Genius who was an artist trying to make a never before seen masterpiece.<br /> You most certainly can; you'll need the Metaptropi track. 1st dots creates artifical sensations, higher dots create impossible spaces and materials.<br /> Be a bit creative and don't complain as soon as something not handed to you ready made for Pete's sake.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> Maybe I'll make a post explaining it one day if I felt OP Forums crowd was worth the bother, but...<br /> Genius is a game about creativity and self-expression.<br /> If you want to understand the game, skip right to Wonder-making and start making fun stuff using the variables, and try to come up with ways to build your favorite devices from films, stories you like. From that exercise campaigns, PCs, NPCs will all flow. If customization and expression is NOT the type of fun you look for in RPGs (see &quot;8 types of fun&quot; by the AngryGM) then you will likely not realize its merits so easily but that does not make it a bad game, tho it may not be your type of game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T14:08:30-07:00","id":1145627,"title":"","content":"Seriously guys. Seriously.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i299.photobucket.com/albums/mm288/larryo340/Funny%20Pictures/98bdcab5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T14:26:39-07:00","id":1145632,"title":"","content":"Just rereading the updates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1005496#post1005496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the burden of proof is on you since ArcaneArts is (somewhat rudely, perhaps) questioning your statement. And I'd also like to hear some support for how Geniuses are forced to take responsibilities or face meaningful consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Actually</u>, since ArcaneArts first asserted that Genii aren't responsible for their actions (making a claim), the burden of proof does in fact fall upon them fist as to why they aren't. I'll admit I should have asked for support first instead of a banal &quot;no you're wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8064\" data-vbnamecard=\"8064\">mp122984</a> summarized it well enough, anyways. A Genius who acts out of line gets punished both by their internal Karma meter, and by making enemies of pretty much everyone. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1005786#post1005786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also this.^<br /> <br /> Demon is actually a hell of a book for Genius to take notes from in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... Genius couldn't have taken notes from Demon, since <i>Genius came out before Demon was written</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T16:42:28-07:00","id":1145661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1145632#post1145632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just rereading the updates.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Actually</u>, since ArcaneArts first asserted that Genii aren't responsible for their actions (making a claim), the burden of proof does in fact fall upon them fist as to why they aren't. I'll admit I should have asked for support first instead of a banal &quot;no you're wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8064\" data-vbnamecard=\"8064\">mp122984</a> summarized it well enough, anyways. A Genius who acts out of line gets punished both by their internal Karma meter, and by making enemies of pretty much everyone.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> But... Genius couldn't have taken notes from Demon, since <i>Genius came out before Demon was written</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Wow, fucking hell. Just. Fucking hell.<br /> <br /> 2) Genius, as of Chapter 2, does not do much to encourage or incentivize responsbility, textually speaking, both in the fluff and the mechanics. They have a karma meter, but that Karma meter does little in terms of sting, and the game's fluff seems to encourage the hostility you reference more than it discourages it.<br /> <br /> 3) So, funny thing-There's this thread? It's kind of huge? It's called &quot;Genius: The Transgression 2nd Edition?&quot;. Where people are working on making a 2nd Edition. And you know, since Genius is a <i>thing</i>, it's not unreasonable to assume that people might, I dunno. Write supplements for it? Create updates? Expand on the material? Fucking do fan shit for a game they like? And they aren't doing it, like. All in the years before 2014? Like, they're doing it Now? They were doing it when this Thread came out? And <i>they</i> can take hints from Demon the Descent?<br /> <br /> Maybe you should think about shit like that before getting on my case. Because, you know, <i>I know that Genius couldn't have taken hints from a game that wasn't out.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T17:09:10-07:00","id":1145673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1145661#post1145661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Wow, fucking hell. Just. Fucking hell.<br /> <br /> 2) Genius, as of Chapter 2, does not do much to encourage or incentivize responsbility, textually speaking, both in the fluff and the mechanics. They have a karma meter, but that Karma meter does little in terms of sting, and the game's fluff seems to encourage the hostility you reference more than it discourages it.<br /> <br /> 3) So, funny thing-There's this thread? It's kind of huge? It's called &quot;Genius: The Transgression 2nd Edition?&quot;. Where people are working on making a 2nd Edition. And you know, since Genius is a <i>thing</i>, it's not unreasonable to assume that people might, I dunno. Write supplements for it? Create updates? Expand on the material? Fucking do fan shit for a game they like? And they aren't doing it, like. All in the years before 2014? Like, they're doing it Now? They were doing it when this Thread came out? And <i>they</i> can take hints from Demon the Descent?<br /> <br /> Maybe you should think about shit like that before getting on my case. Because, you know, <i>I know that Genius couldn't have taken hints from a game that wasn't out.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>2. So, you still haven't read Chapter 3 and beyond? You are basing your entire assessment on 2/5ths (not counting the Appendices) of a book?<br /> <br /> 3. Maybe make that clear? I was expecting to see something like &quot;<i>Demon is actually a hell of a book for any working on Genius to take notes from in general.</i>&quot; or &quot;<i>Demon is actually a hell of a book for the Genius 2E crowd to take notes from in general.</i>&quot;, seeing as you are aware of those things. You just said &quot;Genius&quot; and there is only the one source, last updated 7 years or so ago (The 2E update thread isn't anywhere close to done, so 1.1 is all there is, even semi-officially).<br /> <br /> Regardless, you've clarified your meaning on that one, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T17:24:06-07:00","id":1145679,"title":"","content":"I assumed it was obvious.<br /> <br /> Or, perhaps more accurately, I trust that readers aren't idiots.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I am still basing that off of what I've read. I admit, I could be wrong-though I doubt it, because Obligation is totally in Chapter 2.<br /> <br /> I kind of have better things to do than read a game I don't like and continue a fight I don't care about anymore, for now anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T14:46:09-07:00","id":1146449,"title":"","content":"@Vree<br /> <br /> I do apologies if this thread ended up wasting your time. That was never my intention, in fact at first it truly was meant to look at the fan game from a critical but unbiased lens. My original critiques were relatively critical but fair up until a certain point, an that was because much like a sea shell that washed ashore from the Ocean Oroboros in the Anima Mundi the more I read an looked at the game the more and more harder it was to remain unbiased as I was filled with mounting anger and disgust. Looking back over it now after having sufficiently cooled off my final critical evaluation of Genius: the Transgression 1st Edition is that while it was a fascinating idea filled with great potential it ultimately suffered from the creator's bias against Mage: the Awakening and nostalgia for Mage: the Ascension with smattering of unintentional bigotry and masoginy pared with scientific fetishism. <br /> <br /> The Genius: the Transgression 2nd Edition thread was brought up earlier and I can pleasantly say that long before my well intended review tuned rage tangent the fan community had already recognized the problems with Genius and have worked tirelessly to make it the game they love and without the heinous undertones that held the original back from it's true potential. As of it's most current update I can honestly say I can't find anything to criticize about it and greatly look forward to it's forward progress. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T16:21:08-07:00","id":1146475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1146449#post1146449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Genius: the Transgression 2nd Edition thread was brought up earlier and I can pleasantly say that long before my well intended review tuned rage tangent the fan community had already recognized the problems with Genius and have worked tirelessly to make it the game they love and without the heinous undertones that held the original back from it's true potential. As of it's most current update I can honestly say I can't find anything to criticize about it and greatly look forward to it's forward progress. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I'm sure I'll come up with something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For real, thanks.<br /> <br /> Quick note, I've been quiet lately because I'm moving things to a wiki. Once I've done that, more substantive stuff will be coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T14:14:01-07:00","id":1153797,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> (before I go off on a tangent<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks.<br /> I wasn't really looking to post on these forums, I was only browsing reviews for random titles and these two threads came up in Google.<br /> I realize I was in the wrong to expect <i>actual</i> reviews. You probably just intended this one as a vague discussion thread.<br /> But when I when I opened a link with a title like &quot;A critical look at...&quot; and the whole thing was like one paragraph long and a single complaint I was like whaaat xD<br /> (It also didn't help that I clicked on this second after Arcane's link and the utter disaster THAT review was. I was promised reviews, not bullshit dammit! xD)<br /> <br /> Still, I REALLY appreciate the friendly response and it is a welcome break after the horrid stuff of a dozen of Arcane's comments I just checked.<br /> It's the kind of thing that gives me hope for this place.<br /> <br /> I <i>would</i> offer my opinion on the various comments in the earlier pages because there were a few that people said they didn't know the answer to,<br /> buut I also realize that this topic is kind of dead and people really don't care that much anymore.<br /> (And it really doesn't bother me how people feel about game A or game B, just if they can have a polite chat.)<br /> <br /> ..Except for this one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1146449#post1146449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unintentional bigotry and masoginy pared with scientific fetishism</div> </div> </div> </div>Why oh WHY did you have to add this.<br /> I was about to put you down as a nice guy<br /> and you do this to me.<br /> <br /> You're just an asshole too who throws around big words because overly sensitive radical justice warrior behavior is the new black, guys!<br /> Accuse Moochava of being secretly a rapist and a gay-hater as well too, why don't you? <br /> (I recall there were no gay NPCs in Genius. Why not? Don't you know this is the age of Progress with elevated expectations? And can somebody please think of the children?)<br /> <br /> sigh You guys are such, agh!. Do you think accusing people of horrible things is just something fun to do without consequences?<br /> Don't just throw terms you don't understand around like racist or mysoginist.<br /> Don't just put a Cain mark on people because you thought something they wrote could perhaps be taken the wrong way or something <br /> These are serious allegiations, okay?<br /> <br /> If you DO choose to say one you should damn well KNOW the weight of the accusation you're making, and be able to back it up.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong but I'm thinking you base that &quot;mysoginist&quot; comment solely on one part of the book that talks about the statistics of supernaturals and the female % is lower<br /> Buut I also think that it's unimportant to deduce what you were thinking cuz it also seems that you've copied these allegiations wholesale from Arcane's thread. Which is a HORRIBLE idea.<br /> Arcane is like the WORST role model for appropriate fan behavior EVER that you should be taking lessons from.<br /> <br /> I wish every time I come here we could just have a nice chat but honestly fandoms filled with children appreciate their fanartists/fan writers more and approach topics with more reason than this hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T16:16:36-07:00","id":1153826,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2330\" data-vbnamecard=\"2330\">Vree</a> <span style=\"color:red\">That post is absolutely inappropriate. Right off the bat calling another user an asshole is a personal attack, which is not acceptable, and it only gets worse from there, insinuating that our users don\u2019t know what the words racist and mysoginist mean, attacking the character of another user, and disrespecting the forum community here as a whole.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T16:32:30-07:00","id":1153830,"title":"","content":"I suppose vitriol of that sort means I have well and truly arrived...somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T16:51:18-07:00","id":1153831,"title":"","content":"Also as an aside, I'm sorry if anyone dislikes my thoughts on Genius and think they are over the top and harsh, but, uh. Not changing my opinion, and basically calling me the...well, all of the above is <i>really</i> not helping to change it. It also doesn't help the impression I have of most Genius fans, which I really wish I didn't have as a result of experience and actually <i>would</i> like to change my viewpoint on.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm a professional, not <i>just</i> a fan, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-28-2017, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T16:15:20-07:00","id":1154873,"title":"","content":"Let me make my point crystal clear:<br /> <br /> In the Genius the Transgression 1st Edition document there is a metric listed early on that details the in-world rate at which people regularly become Genii. It specifies the most likely conditions that allow for a Genii to gain their first Inspiration: Academia and other cerebral occupations. It also lists numbered percentages for both men and women in academia as a base line. <br /> <br /> If you add both of those numbers together, it doesn't equal 100%.<br /> <br /> Meaning.<br /> <br /> That the creator either accidentally forgot to make the statistic equal up to 100%. <br /> <br /> Or. <br /> <br /> That the creator intentionally made a metric that has hard in-world data to suggest that gender neutral individuals have a below 10% rate of becoming Genii even in the ideal circumstances. <br /> <br /> After spending months shadowing the progress of Genius the Transgression 2nd Edition I have come to the opinion that the creator intention's were to showcase that real world academia is so toxic to gender non-binary individuals that tragically many must keep their true selves a secret from the world or else face expulsion or worse, thus why the in-game metric is so low. Thus, the creator unintentionally gave their work a bigoted undertone. Most fans who I've observed either look at this gross sentiment that way, or ignore the statistics all together in favor of a more traditional CofD theme of &quot;Anyone can become Splat X given the right circumstances.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ignoring it's existence though will do no service to anyone. Acknowledging it and making sure that a creator's intent isn't heinous is never a bad thing. That is critical examination. <br /> <br /> I choose to give this game's creator the benefit of the doubt because I believe in GtT 2E's themes and intent. But I acknowledge that this is my own personal opinion and that I am giving them the benefit of the doubt despite what is literally written in the 1st Edition document's opening chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T17:03:44-07:00","id":1154886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1154873#post1154873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me make my point crystal clear:<br /> <br /> In the Genius the Transgression 1st Edition document there is a metric listed early on that details the in-world rate at which people regularly become Genii. It specifies the most likely conditions that allow for a Genii to gain their first Inspiration: Academia and other cerebral occupations. It also lists numbered percentages for both men and women in academia as a base line.<br /> <br /> If you add both of those numbers together, it doesn't equal 100%.<br /> <br /> Meaning.<br /> <br /> That the creator either accidentally forgot to make the statistic equal up to 100%.<br /> <br /> Or.<br /> <br /> That the creator intentionally made a metric that has hard in-world data to suggest that gender neutral individuals have a below 10% rate of becoming Genii even in the ideal circumstances.<br /> <br /> After spending months shadowing the progress of Genius the Transgression 2nd Edition I have come to the opinion that the creator intention's were to showcase that real world academia is so toxic to gender non-binary individuals that tragically many must keep their true selves a secret from the world or else face expulsion or worse, thus why the in-game metric is so low. Thus, the creator unintentionally gave their work a bigoted undertone. Most fans who I've observed either look at this gross sentiment that way, or ignore the statistics all together in favor of a more traditional CofD theme of &quot;Anyone can become Splat X given the right circumstances.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ignoring it's existence though will do no service to anyone. Acknowledging it and making sure that a creator's intent isn't heinous is never a bad thing. That is critical examination.<br /> <br /> I choose to give this game's creator the benefit of the doubt because I believe in GtT 2E's themes and intent. But I acknowledge that this is my own personal opinion and that I am giving them the benefit of the doubt despite what is literally written in the 1st Edition document's opening chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I ranted a fair bit about this in my own review of Chapter 1, I do want to reiterate and clarify points on this:<br /> <br /> I don't believe for a second that Marquis intended to make his work come across as bigoted. I do not think he was trying to communicate any personal biases, conciously or not. While I don't readily believe that he was trying to showcase academic bigotry in a meaningful way, I do believe that he wanted to be evocative of academia because, well, duh, mad scientists, and therefore lazily mirrored the image without thinking too hard how it came across, flaws and all. It's a bad result, but it's a human problem, and one that probably would have been resolved had Kyle worked with someone who was credible as an editor.<br /> <br /> And I wanna double down on the idea that being critical of this, even if it's an innocent mistake, is important, because yeah, Genius should become a better game by learning from it's mistakes. It is literally the most influential fangame in the community, and the people who adore it and even draw strength from it should be rewarded with a version of the game that is honed and sharpened, that is both more aware of- and possessive of- itself and more aware of it's audience and treats them respect because they respected it first.<br /> <br /> If we can't wonder if something went too far before hand in the effort to improve a game about mad scientists, we have probably lost the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T17:35:50-07:00","id":1154893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1154873#post1154873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me make my point crystal clear:<br /> <br /> In the Genius the Transgression 1st Edition document there is a metric listed early on that details the in-world rate at which people regularly become Genii. It specifies the most likely conditions that allow for a Genii to gain their first Inspiration: Academia and other cerebral occupations. It also lists numbered percentages for both men and women in academia as a base line.<br /> <br /> If you add both of those numbers together, it doesn't equal 100%.<br /> <br /> Meaning.<br /> <br /> That the creator either accidentally forgot to make the statistic equal up to 100%.<br /> <br /> Or.<br /> <br /> That the creator intentionally made a metric that has hard in-world data to suggest that gender neutral individuals have a below 10% rate of becoming Genii even in the ideal circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Genius the Transgression v1.1 page 32</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the available demographics, the Inspired are 56% male, 40% female, and 4% not answering to either gender identity, with those numbers equalizing slowly but steadily; male-female parity should occur around 2030 according to projections.</div> </div> </div> </div>That line?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1154873#post1154873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After spending months shadowing the progress of Genius the Transgression 2nd Edition I have come to the opinion that the creator intention's were to showcase that real world academia is so toxic to gender non-binary individuals that tragically many must keep their true selves a secret from the world or else face expulsion or worse, thus why the in-game metric is so low. Thus, the creator unintentionally gave their work a bigoted undertone. Most fans who I've observed either look at this gross sentiment that way, or ignore the statistics all together in favor of a more traditional CofD theme of &quot;Anyone can become Splat X given the right circumstances.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Genius the Transgression v1.1 page 31-32</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of those geniuses with their origins in mortal science, about 60% came to Inspiration naturally, in the course of independent study. The rest were deliberately guided and spent time as beholden. Either this was a period of apprenticeship before the inchoate geniuses were allowed to embrace their full power, or they were intended to remain as mere servants and technicians, but grew Inspired of their own accord.<br /> <br /> About 12% of geniuses become Inspired though they possess no particular scientific or technical background, nor formal training time under another genius. The old term for such a person was a raudus, a raw &quot;lump&quot; of genius. They possess no training, but they have raw talent and some kind of frantic drive that pushes them into a Breakthrough. The beat cop who sees one crime too many and decides to mess around with an armored suit, the mother whose children are menaced by mysterious underground machines and who ransacks libraries to find out how to stop them, the laborer who watches a loved one wither of untreatable cancer, and who starts asking around about &quot;impossible&quot; cures...all these people are geniuses for whom the Breakthrough comes first and mundane knowledge comes later.<br /> <br /> One genius in three has a PhD or equivalent. (Two geniuses in three will claim to have a PhD or equivalent, or will put &quot;Doctor,&quot; &quot;Doc,&quot; or &quot;Professor&quot; in their names and not feel guilty about it.) This means that the Inspired population is an educated one. However, not every genius comes to her new life in the &quot;traditional&quot; manner of being a scientist and then going mad. Many, perhaps most, are hobbyists and come to Inspiration through those hobbies: amateur astronomers who see something they can't explain and are consumed with obsession, computer geeks whose machines start doing things that don't make sense, or graphic artists who stumble upon a color palette that produces impossible effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those paragraphs?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1154873#post1154873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring it's existence though will do no service to anyone. Acknowledging it and making sure that a creator's intent isn't heinous is never a bad thing. That is critical examination.<br /> <br /> I choose to give this game's creator the benefit of the doubt because I believe in GtT 2E's themes and intent. But I acknowledge that this is my own personal opinion and that I am giving them the benefit of the doubt despite what is literally written in the 1st Edition document's opening chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to establish such metrics don't do anyone any good when said universes are going to differ from table to table.<br /> <br /> Presenting such metrics as in-universe statistics compiled by a group as obsessed with numbers as they are at bad research methods is fine, provided it is clearly presented as such. In universe narrators aren't given the presumption of omniscience or impartiality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-01-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T17:58:22-07:00","id":1154906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1154893#post1154893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presenting such metrics as in-universe statistics compiled by a group as obsessed with numbers as they are at bad research methods is fine, provided it is clearly presented as such. In universe narrators aren't given the presumption of omniscience or impartiality.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the point is to demonstrate that geniuses are bad at research but bent on producing results, all that's needed is &quot;Ask ten groups of mad statisticians what the demographics of the Englightened are and you'll get twenty-one sets of data contradicting each other.&quot; Even if it needed actual 'data' to communicate the idea, it should at least be made as clear a disclaimer as is possible for the form that everything that follows is probably bullshit: &quot;While the following statistics are often bandied about by the Enlightened whenever the conversation comes up, no Genius has ever actually been able to verify that sources or validity of these claims, which, while not surprising given how geniuses operate, does make it frustrating for anyone who has to deal with peers who are hell-bent on believing these shoddy results&quot;<br /> <br /> As it stands, we are presented this information as though it were fact in much the same way that most of the Chronicles books are delivered by an omniscient third-person narrator, with no real challenge to or exploration of it's validity. As such, it comes off as a giant bag of alienating bullshit.<br /> <br /> If you are correct, than the intent must be made clearer to be a joke, or at least non-serious. If you are not, then it's a mistake, and it should be fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:03:53-07:00","id":1154908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1154906#post1154906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the point is to demonstrate that geniuses are bad at research but bent on producing results, all that's needed is &amp;quot;Ask ten groups of mad statisticians what the demographics of the Englightened are and you'll get twenty-one sets of data contradicting each other.&amp;quot; Even if it needed actual 'data' to communicate the idea, it should at least be made as clear a disclaimer as is possible for the form that everything that follows is probably bullshit: &amp;quot;While the following statistics are often bandied about by the Enlightened whenever the conversation comes up, no Genius has ever actually been able to verify that sources or validity of these claims, which, while not surprising given how geniuses operate, does make it frustrating for anyone who has to deal with peers who are hell-bent on believing these shoddy results&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> As it stands, we are presented this information as though it were fact in much the same way that most of the Chronicles books are delivered by an omniscient third-person narrator, with no real challenge to or exploration of it's validity. As such, it comes off as a giant bag of alienating bullshit.<br /> <br /> If you are correct, than the intent must be made clearer to be a joke, or at least non-serious. If you are not, then it's a mistake, and it should be fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:07:04-07:00","id":1154909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1154908#post1154908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this might be the easiest conversation we've ever had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:04:22-07:00","id":1154929,"title":"","content":"*Reads Vent0's posts*<br /> <br /> Fair point, although it could be argued (somewhat hilariously in retrospect) that the narrator for GtT 1st Ed had the exact same problem of the narrator for MtAw 1st Ed in that they don't do that good of a job of differentiating their &quot;in world&quot; voice from their &quot;game creator&quot; voice.<br /> <br /> It was a common problem with a lot of the earlier 1st Ed's material though, so honestly it's no wonder that it's so often overlooked despite the disgusting implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-01-2017, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:33:20-07:00","id":1154937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=1154929#post1154929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Reads Vent0's posts*<br /> <br /> Fair point, although it could be argued (somewhat hilariously in retrospect) that the narrator for GtT 1st Ed had the exact same problem of the narrator for MtAw 1st Ed in that they don't do that good of a job of differentiating their &quot;in world&quot; voice from their &quot;game creator&quot; voice.<br /> <br /> It was a common problem with a lot of the earlier 1st Ed's material though, so honestly it's no wonder that it's so often overlooked despite the disgusting implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, it's still not an uncommon problem with much of 2nd Ed's material. Maybe not to the same degree as the section of Genius in question, but I've repeatedly defended MtAw 2e on the basis that its writing presents mages in a more positive light than they are intended to be viewed due to the fact that mages are assumed to be the protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T19:08:09-08:00","id":1176143,"title":"","content":"Thank you ArcaneArts for the &quot;<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also, </span></span></span></div><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/moochava/genius\" target=\"_blank\">from the place where you 